graph': 'BEIRUT, Lebanon — In the Syrian city of Aleppo, children carrying groceries climb 15-foot mounds of rubble on their way home. Shoppers ignore vibrations from falling bombs. Buildings stand sliced in half, wires and beds and bathtubs exposed, with families still living inside. Most days, doctors have just seconds to decide which children to try to save and which to let die, as parents shriek and explosions shake the ground.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Where CPR on a Boy Is Time Wasted: U.S. Doctors Recall Aleppo’s Horrors', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Aleppo, Syria: Where CPR on a Boy Is Time Wasted', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALEPPO (SYRIA)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hospitals', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Physicians for Human Rights', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Al Nusra Front', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Syrian American Medical Society', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T00:07:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anne Barnard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anne', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barnard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e78dc71d-7067-50af-a9d3-715d8f93443d', 'word_count': 1474, 'uri': 'nyt:/