he sanctuary of St. Paul’s Chapel in Lower Manhattan will shed its current pink and blue scheme for a creamier tone, revealed by a microscopic examination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/nyregion/super-white-or-white-dove-restoring-st-pauls-colonial-color.html', 'snippet': 'In a renovation, the sanctuary of St. Paul’s Chapel in Lower Manhattan will shed its current pink and blue scheme for a creamier tone, revealed by a microscopic examination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'King George III ruled New York when St. Paul’s Chapel was built in Lower Manhattan.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Super White or White Dove? Restoring St. Paul’s Colonial Color', 'kicker': 'Building Blocks', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peering Into the Past  of a Historic Church  to See Its Truest Hue', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "St Paul's Chapel (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Trinity Church (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Financial District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restoration and Renovation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Churches (Buildings)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T09:00:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6107674a-528e-58b6-89b0-97b5b97289e7', 'word_count': 751, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6107674a-528e-58b6-89b0-97b5b97289e7'}, {'abstract': 'Daido Moriyama’s images of Shinjuku are like being in “Blade Runner,” a futuristic place of phantoms, electric energy and tension.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/01/in-shinjuku-blade-runner-in-real-life/', 'snippet': 'Daido Moriyama’s images of Shinjuku are like being in “Blade Runner,” a futuristic place of phantoms, electric energy and tension.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I walk in the evening with my camera from Kabuki-cho to Kuyakusho-dori and then along Okubo-dori toward Shin-Okubo Station, I sometimes feel a shiver running down my spine. I find myself flinching for some reason, even though nothing in particular has happened. Shadow-spirits squirm amid the darkness of the back streets, under the lights and neon signs. The sight line of the small camera in my hand picks up the sensitive reactions of these wraiths, like electrical impulses. As they perceive coarse tremors in the surrounding air, my cells quiver with tension. Wandering around, enveloped in the vaguely violent atmosphere, I persuade myself that it is my duty as a photographer to photograph Shinjuku without shrinking back. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Shinjuku, ‘Blade Runner’ in Real Life', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Tokyo (Japan)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T09:00:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daido Moriyama', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daido', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Moriyama', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'ran