s.com/2016/08/02/arts/international/review-jesus-christ-superstar-the-trial-of-jane-fonda-and-now-we-are-here.html', 'snippet': 'Three plays in London explore suffering, then and now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — You might expect London’s summer theater to take on a correspondingly sunny hue, but no. While the stage event of the season, “Harry Potter and the Cursed Child,” delivers up an epic rife with family fissures and forces of darkness, a number of smaller productions are speaking to humans’ capacity for suffering, then and now.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 830}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 740, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/30/arts/30lonB/30lonB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Jesus Christ Superstar,’ ‘The Trial of Jane Fonda’ and ‘Now We Are Here’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fonda, Jane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jesus Christ Superstar (Play)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T11:31:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'International Arts', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Wolf', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wolf', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f67092e4-52f2-5a73-8881-50b2952db437', 'word_count': 1148, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f67092e4-52f2-5a73-8881-50b2952db437'}, {'abstract': 'This book is the script of a production that just opened in London, and even though it lacks the play’s much-talked-about special effects, it is a stay-up-all-night read.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/books/harry-potter-and-the-cursed-child-review.html', 'snippet': 'This book is the script of a production that just opened in London, and even though it lacks the play’s much-talked-about special effects, it is a stay-up-all-night read.', 'lead_paragraph': 'J. K. Rowling’s magical seven-volume Harry Potter series is the ultimate bildungsroman, tracing that young wizard’s coming of age, as he not only battles evil but also struggles to come to terms with the responsibilities, losses and burdens of adulthood. In the course of those books, we see a plucky schoolboy, torn by adolescent doubts and confusions, grow into an epic hero, kin to King Arthur, Luke Skywalker and Spider-Man.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/books/review/01Booksrowling-web2/01Booksrowling-web2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Harry Potter and the Cursed Child’ Explores the Power of Time', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Wizardly Journey in Time', 'name': None, '