mooth cup in 10 minutes flat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/dining/cold-brew-coffee-maker-prisma.html', 'snippet': 'A new appliance promises a smooth cup in 10 minutes flat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cold-brewed coffee, for many the gold standard when it comes to a smooth-tasting cup, takes planning and time. Now the product developers at FirstBuild, a subsidiary of GE Appliances, have come up with the Prisma. The machine uses a vacuum infusion system to produce excellent cold-brewed coffee in a mere 10 minutes. The gadget has a handblown 23.7-ounce carafe and takes regular pleated-paper basket filters. But there’s still a wait as presale orders will not deliver for about a year: Prisma Cold Brew Coffee Maker, $240 (discounted from what will be the regular price of $299), indiegogo.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1131, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1131}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 544, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1685, 'width': 894, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnercoffee/03burnercoffee-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cold-Brewed Coffee Without the Hourslong Wait', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Chill: Cold-Brewed Coffee  Without the Long Wait', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffee', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'IndieGoGo.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Electric Company', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'FirstBuild', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T13:55:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1e4fe7e3-3f89-5257-bdaa-055f3efa8338', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1e4fe7e3-3f89-5257-bdaa-055f3efa8338'}, {'abstract': 'Arrowood Farms in the Hudson Valley is now serving beers and duck prosciutto made on the farm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/dining/arrowood-farms-beer.html', 'snippet': 'Arrowood Farms in the Hudson Valley is now serving beers and duck prosciutto made on the farm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few years ago, Blake Arrowood, an English teacher in Southeast Asia, decided to become a farmer and cultivated 48 acres in the Hudson Valley, not far from New Paltz, N.Y. He grew hops along with rye, and raised ducks, too, and took on a brewing partner, Jacob Meglio, after the state passed legislation making it easier for farmers to brew beer. The farm now produces nine beers, including one made with organic rye. All are served at the farm, along with duck prosciutto made in-house. The brews are sold and served in the Hudson Valley and also at Malt and Mold’s two Manhattan locations. When the new Rouge Tomate reopens later this summer in Chelsea, a selection of Arrowood’s beers will be the only ones offered on tap: Arrowood Farms, 236 Lower Whitfield Road, Accord, N.Y., 845-253-0389, arrowoodfarms.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerfarm1/03burnerfarm1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Hops Farm Turns to Brewing', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cultivate: A Gentleman Brewer at a Farm Upstate', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Arrowood Farms', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River Valley (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rouge Tomate (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Malt and Mold (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chelsea (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gramercy Park (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T13:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2159075-2875-51ba-aea1-31e1f04b9adb', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2159075-2875-51ba-aea1-31e1f04b9adb'}, {'abstract': 'The cookbook “Leon Happy Salads,” from a London restaurant chain, has clever tips for better-dressed greens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/dining/leon-happy-salads-book.html', 'snippet': 'The cookbook “Leon Happy Salads,” from a London restaurant chain, has clever tips for better-dressed greens.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Here’s a cookbook to inspire when the heat is off the charts. Prep time for many of the salads in this colorful volume from Leon, a casual English chain, is five minutes. Bright ideas fill categories like classics, including a Greek salad topped, inventively, with fried feta. Polish herring and potatoes with beets in horseradish cream, and chicken tonnato with artichokes and haricots verts, are meal-worthy. The BKT salad swaps out lettuce for kale, and there are many cool Asian influences in the sprightly dressings. Basic ingredients, salad-making principles (including the architecture involved), an array of crunchy garnishes and dressings are included: “Leon Happy Salads” by Jane Baxter and John Vincent (Conran Octopus, $19.99).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 604, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 604}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1019, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1203, 'width': 1196, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbook/03burnerbook-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New Inspiration for Summer Salads', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Toss: Inventive English Recipes   for Fresh Summer Salads', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Salads', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Leon Happy Salads (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T13:58:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/266ccb0c-7c6f-5842-bd0c-4d5f9a176012', 'word_count': 114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/266ccb0c-7c6f-5842-bd0c-4d5f9a176012'}, {'abstract': 'Scott Gold is named the bacon critic for Extra Crispy, a breakfast-centric website.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/dining/bacon-critic-extra-crispy-scott-gold.html', 'snippet': 'Scott Gold is named the bacon critic for Extra Crispy, a breakfast-centric website.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scott Gold, a 39-year-old food writer specializing in meat, beat out around 1,000 applicants for the title of bacon critic for Extra Crispy, Time Inc.’s new website about breakfast, brunch and the foods involved. “This job is tailor-made for me,” he said with gusto. When it comes to bacon, he likes a medium-thick slice and a balance of smoke, fat and salt with an “intensely porcine” quality. He can’t resist the bacon at Peter Luger Steak House in Brooklyn. “Bacon is rarely terrible,” he said. “Who sends back bacon?” At the same time, he acknowledges that spectacular bacon is hard to find. But now he is on the case, given three months to travel around the globe, reporting weekly on his discoveries. In November, at the end of his assignment, he’ll crown one bacon as the best: extracrispy.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbacon1/03burnerbacon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbacon1/03burnerbacon1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbacon1/03burnerbacon1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbacon1/03burnerbacon1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/dining/03burnerbacon1/03burnerbacon1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03