. “I wanted to have a collection that you can pack in a suitcase to cover all your needs,” she says of her clothing line Deitas. “So it’ll always remain capsule size.” With simple lines, mixable pieces and a muted palette, Deitas cuts down on the plague of morning indecision by offering the ease of a weekend-away-wardrobe at home.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Brand to Know: The Line Making Silk Modern (and Packable)', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Making Silk Packable', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sweden', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dahlin, Josephine', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deitas (Fashion Label)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-01T15:57:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Ronan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ronan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa9b19a9-95ac-5c9e-8d4f-babd0fdc00f4', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa9b19a9-95ac-5c9e-8d4f-babd0fdc00f4'}, {'abstract': 'Activate your Olympic spirit with a challenge from the Rio resident and mathematician Marco Moriconi.', 'web_url': 'https://wordplay.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/01/moriconi-olympics/', 'snippet': 'Activate your Olympic spirit with a challenge from the Rio resident and mathematician Marco Moriconi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our puzzle this week was suggested by Marco Moriconi, a regular Numberplay contributor who makes his home in Rio, site of the upcoming Olympic Games.