onists will release hundreds of the salamanders, which have been raised to maturity, into streams in Ohio.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/science/hellbenders-salamanders.html', 'snippet': 'To try to restore their population, conservationists will release hundreds of the salamanders, which have been raised to maturity, into streams in Ohio.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Take a two-foot-long muscle with a skeleton and coat it in multiple layers of snot. Now squish the muscle down so it’s flat. Add four short legs, eighteen toes, a big, wide mouth and beady eyes. Forget about eyelids. Stretch some skin out along the slimy muscle and wrinkle it on the sides. This is how it will breath. Now stick that creature under a big rock in a fast river or stream and leave it alone. You’ve just made an adult eastern hellbender, the biggest salamander in North America.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/science/02tb-hellbender01/02tb-hellbender01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/02/science/02tb-hellbender01/02tb-hellbender01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/science/02tb-hellbender01/02tb-hellbender01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/science/02tb-hellbender01/02tb-hellbender01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/scie