k': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Molina, Edilberto', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reverol, Nestor', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-02T00:28:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b08d3c0f-36b3-55a7-9dd3-2ee4215dc5bc', 'word_count': 554, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b08d3c0f-36b3-55a7-9dd3-2ee4215dc5bc'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Pazcoguin, a New York City Ballet soloist, plays the elegant Victoria in the revival of “Cats” on Broadway.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/arts/dance/about-last-night-georgina-pazcoguin-cats-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Pazcoguin, a New York City Ballet soloist, plays the elegant Victoria in the revival of “Cats” on Broadway.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The cats in “Cats” are a diverse group. Victoria, the most elegant of the Jellicle tribe, wears white from head to paw, symbolizing purity and innocence. For Georgina Pazcoguin, the New York City Ballet soloist who plays Victoria in the current Broadway revival of that Andrew Lloyd Webber musical, the role fulfills a childhood dream. She grew up obsessed with a videotape of the Broadway production. “Catholic school ended at 2 p.m., and my dance classes started at 4:30 or 5 p.m.,” she said. In between, she watched “Cats.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/01/arts/dance/03LASTNIGHT-slide-F29W/03LASTNIGHT-slide-F29W-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/