 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inventions and Patents', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-02T11:51:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Obituaries', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By JACK WILLIAMS', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WILLIAMS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f2f5c0c2-f717-5694-a0f7-a82eab62f78b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f2f5c0c2-f717-5694-a0f7-a82eab62f78b'}, {'abstract': 'Week 5 of our contest ran during the Republican convention, and many of the 807 entries reflected that. Read the work of our winner, Gabe S., who wrote about junk food and government subsidies, then see what else teenagers around the world were thinking about during one hot week in July.', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/summer-reading-contest-winner-week-5-on-how-the-government-supports-your-junk-food-habit/', 'snippet': 'Week 5 of our contest ran during the Republican convention, and many of the 807 entries reflected that. Read the work of our winner, Gabe S., who wrote about junk food and government subsidies, then see what else teenagers around the world were th...', 'lead_paragraph': 'Week 5 of our Summer Reading Contest ran during the Republican convention, and many of the 807 entries reflected that. Over and over, students weighed in on Donald J. Trump and his message, Melania Trump’s speech, Ted Cruz’s refusal to endorse Mr. Trump, and what the convention said to them about the Republican party in general. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/01/learning/JunkFoodLN/JunkFoodLN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_na