ster for the party holding the White House.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/us/politics/reagan-trump-clinton-election-polls.html', 'snippet': 'Unlike in past presidential contests, a sour national mood does not necessarily spell disaster for the party holding the White House.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A political lifetime ago, Ronald Reagan’s pollster seized on this question to frame the campaign’s argument during his 1980 presidential campaign: “Is the country headed in the right direction, or is it on the wrong track?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Pessimism Might Not Be a Winning Bet for Republicans', 'kicker': 'Letter From America', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reagan, Ronald Wilson', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-02T17:23:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Harwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/39457776-737b-5810-bb1b-a70d0e716027', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/39457776-737b-5810-bb1b-a70d0e716027'}, {'abstract': 'Donald J. Trump’s clash with a Muslim couple whose Army captain son was killed in Iraq has turned a spotlight on Muslims in the United States military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/us/muslims-us-military.html', 