'headline': {'main': 'Faun Fables’s Summer Tour Diary, from the Alps to Oklahoma', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-02T17:57:59+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/563af5fe-ba29-558a-a29f-31c2c1c20a4b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/563af5fe-ba29-558a-a29f-31c2c1c20a4b'}, {'abstract': 'The alt-folk group Faun Fables, which now includes three members under age 10, shares a tour diary from their travels in Europe and the US.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/t-magazine/travel/faun-fables-band-europe-travel-diary.html', 'snippet': 'The alt-folk group Faun Fables, which now includes three members under age 10, shares a tour diary from their travels in Europe and the US.', 'lead_paragraph': '“I felt a calling, the gypsy family, the Von Trapp family singers,” says Dawn McCarthy, who fronts the alt-folk band Faun Fables along with her partner, Nils Frykdahl. (Their website describes them as “art-witch songtellers,” which should give you some idea of what they sound like.) The band is now truly a family affair: It includes the couple’s three young daughters, Edda, 8, Ura, 6, and Gudrin, 3. Edda and Ura are in school during the year at the family’s home in Sonoma County, Calif.; but during their summer break, Faun Fables pack up their gear to drive cross-country for tours — and travel to European music festivals.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/02/t-magazine/02tmag-faunfables-slide-8D95/02tmag-faunfables-slide-8D95-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum