ogether as distance dies.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/02/the-unbundled-city/', 'snippet': 'Clumping together as distance dies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I want to indulge myself a bit, talking about today’s interesting article in the Times about corporate headquarters moving back to cities and how it relates to an old discussion in one of my home fields, economic geography.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unbundled City', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-02T21:07:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/201b9dea-e06c-5a98-86d0-39ca7be9e875', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/201b9dea-e06c-5a98-86d0-39ca7be9e875'}, {'abstract': 'Documentaries on PBS and Discovery consider a gorilla who signs; viral outbreaks; and the coming water crisis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/arts/television/the-messages-of-koko-zika-and-the-colorado.html', 'snippet': 'Documentaries on PBS and Discovery consider a gorilla who signs; viral outbreaks; and the coming water crisis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Three television documentaries are vying for your attention over the next two days, serendipitously stacked in order of accessibility. Start off by revisiting a famous talking gorilla, then get serious with everybody’s favorite modern nightmare, devastating viruses. If you make it through those two (which are on Wednesday night on PBS) on Thursday, Discovery has a graduate-level offering about the never sexy but crucial issue of water rights.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_