 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mirzoeff', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/228e710d-78c3-5cd4-ba25-88541a17f933', 'word_count': 2311, 'uri': 'nyt://article/228e710d-78c3-5cd4-ba25-88541a17f933'}, {'abstract': 'Men like me who didn’t fight owe a debt to those who did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/opinion/why-trump-is-not-like-other-draft-dodgers.html', 'snippet': 'Men like me who didn’t fight owe a debt to those who did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Boston — On the evening of Dec. 1, 1969, I was sitting on the floor of a crowded Brandeis University dorm room while on the TV the birth dates of men across the nation, contained in small blue capsules, were drawn out of a container. This lottery would largely determine who among some 850,000 of the draft-eligible would go to Vietnam and who would be left to carry on with their careers, free from the threat of enemy fire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 318, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 318}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1087, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/opinion/03gup/03gup-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Trump Is Not Like Other Draft Dodgers', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From One Draft Dodger to Another', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Draft and Recruitment (Military)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gup, Ted', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-03T07:21:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ted Gup', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ted', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gup', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/eeb85603-864a-5af1-91ee-8720376f34b5', 'word_count': 829, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eeb85603-864a-5af1-91ee-8720376f34b5'}, {'abstract': 'She could win over Republicans who now feel orphaned if she had the right pro-growth economic policies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/opinion/how-clinton-could-knock-trump-out.html', 'snippet': 'She could win over Republicans