https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/03/1916-anxiety-in-berlin-over-war/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Berlin tries to check the spread of peace demonstrations in 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Strict measures have been taken by the Berlin authorities with a view to checking the spread of peace propaganda and with a view to netting those responsible for it. The proclamations scattered broadcast at night calling on the people to rise against the continuation of the war have had their effect, and signs of trouble in many towns are causing grave anxiety in Berlin. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Anxiety in Berlin Over War', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Berlin (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-03T10:50:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/97fa8693-50ff-50ea-9d17-dd7e507b17ba', 'word_count': 98, 'uri': 'nyt://article/97fa8693-50ff-50ea-9d17-dd7e507b17ba'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to make a hard decision about an old dog before a stressful trip and weighing politeness against public health when it concerns a contagious child.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/magazine/can-i-put-down-my-aging-pooch.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on how to make a hard decision about an old dog before a stressful trip and weighing politeness against public health when it concerns a contagious child.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our family dog, a 14-year-old terrier, is currently living with my wife and me in Paris. She has made the trans-Atlantic flight three times in the past year (crated in the belly of the plane) when we return home for various family events. The trip is stressful for her (and for me), but she has always rebounded quickly to her normal self, which is a pretty energetic and healthy dog. Recently, however, her health has declined a bit: less energy, hearing loss, brief moments of apparent confusion and an as-yet-unexplained brief seizure. But she is happy and devoted to my wife and me, enjoying meals and daily walks.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07ethicist/07mag-07ethicist-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07ethicist/07mag-07ethicist-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 633, 'width': 396, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07ethicist/07mag-07ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07ethicist/07mag-07ethicist-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07ethicist/07mag-07ethicist-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can I Put Down My Aging Pooch?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can I Put Down My Aging Pooch?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food Stamps', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Euthanasia and Assisted Suicide', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicine and Health', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-03T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1fe162da-da29-59f8-a221-376b60933433', 'word_count': 1823, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1fe162da-da29-59f8-a221-376b60933433'}, {'abstract': 'A sometimes-sad sitcom from the 1990s showed what it felt like to be black in America.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-roc.html', 'snippet': 'A sometimes-sad sitcom from the 1990s showed what it felt like to be black in America.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From the opening notes of its theme song — an a cappella version of “God Bless the Child” — I knew I was going to like “Roc.” That song was one I’d heard my father croon my whole life, its lyrics cutting through the smoke from his cigarette as he grilled hamburgers or reclined on the couch and closed his heavy eyelids. To this day, “God Bless the Child” sounds like home to me. I’ve also come to think it sounds like how I feel as a black person living in America: all at once hopeful, resigned, familial, lonely, beautiful, sad.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 438, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 438}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 748, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1496, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07lor-copy/07mag-07lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: ‘Roc’', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Roc’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cosby, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Roc (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Cosby Show (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-03T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Cord Jefferson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Cord', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jefferson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/82221c92-418c-5b0c-8d5a-0b9a64ba7178', 'word_count': 960, 'uri': 'nyt://article/82221c92-418c-5b0c-8d5a-0b9a64ba7178'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper on protesting at the R.N.C., revisiting “Fight the Power” and why Donald Trump is like an amusement park attraction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/magazine/chuck-d-thinks-rage-is-good-for-america.html', 'snippet': 'The rapper on protesting at the R.N.C., revisiting “Fight the Power” and why Donald Trump is like an amusement park attraction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’re part of the new supergroup Prophets of Rage, which you call “a collective task force of revolutionary musicians,” along with some members of Rage Against the Machine and Cypress Hill. How is it different from performing with Public Enemy? It’s like being in the Olympics. They’re the best in the world. I’m the weakest link. I’ve never been part of something where I can play s