After a trip a few years ago, during which I spent a few days each in Belfast, Cork and Dublin, I returned home feeling I’d failed myself, and perhaps failed Ireland, by limiting myself to cities. Next time, I would find a cottage in the countryside, where I would read, and write, and take long head-clearing walks. That was the only mandate I gave myself: the promise of an Irish pastoral in real time.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/travel/07FOOTSTEPS2/07FOOTSTEPS2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name':