“The Pinault Collection, Bourse de Commerce.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — The 18th-century bourse in the pulsing heart of this city has long been something of a landmark, its central location a boon to its former use as a wheat and corn exchange, its iron cupola so distinctive that Victor Hugo said it resembled an “English jockey cap.” Now the luxury goods billionaire François Pinault is racing to meet a self-imposed deadline to turn the building into a private museum by the end of 2018, spurred by the hope, he says, that art can offer solace to a nation scarred by terror attacks.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 385}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/arts/04PINAULT1/04PINAULT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 657, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 