is warming up before a race, she often thinks about a younger version of herself who came to the track with her father.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/what-alexi-pappas-think-about-before-a-race/', 'snippet': 'When Alexi Pappas is warming up before a race, she often thinks about a younger version of herself who came to the track with her father.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before a big race, I always feel more sensitive than usual. I feel as if I could cry any minute and also never cry again. I feel nervous. I notice the texture of the grass on the warm-up field more than I usually do — I also sense my heartbeat more than on a normal day when I don’t notice it at all. Stray frizzy hairs tickle the back of my neck. I try my best to keep the thoughts positive and productive and inspiring. Or at least distracting in a good way. When I step on the starting line, I will need to be razor-focused and entirely present – more so than any other time in my life. But on the warm-up field, it is perfectly fine — in fact, encouraged — to daydream. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Running for Your Past and Future Self', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pappas, Alexi (1990- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-04T09:45:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexi Pappas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pappas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b0e8a2af-0f56-5c07-9132-f050025a7819', 'word_count': 180, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b0e8a2af-0f56-5c07-9132-f050025a7819'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s w