lized crust of potatoes make a delicious blank canvas for breakfast, lunch or dinner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/magazine/hash-browns-with-every-meal.html', 'snippet': 'The caramelized crust of potatoes make a delicious blank canvas for breakfast, lunch or dinner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I had one of the great breakfasts of my life a few years ago on San Juan Island, north of Seattle, in a waterside coffee shop that served commercial fishermen, hippie farmers, kayak tourists and boat builders in equal measure. The grated hash browns there were cooked in thin sheets and run under a broiler beneath a handful of grated cheese to create crisp pancakes that could be used as a platter on which to serve fried eggs, or as a hat to top them, depending on your mood. When I got home to New York, I started making them for dinner as well as breakfast, as a side dish for steaks or chicken or lamb. It was labor-intensive to make the dish and ultimately annoying because one of my children wanted it all the time. So together we worked out a hack.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/magazine/07eat/07mag-07eat-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Hash Browns With Every Meal', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Go for Gold', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sifton, Sam', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potatoes', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-04T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd7571aa-6d34-5d05-8edd-50276ff2fa5c', 'word_count': 677, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd7571aa-6d34-5d05-8edd-50276ff2fa5c'}, {'abstract': 'If he can increase his standing in the polls by five points in the next six weeks or so, he’ll qualify for the debate and could have a big impact.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/upshot/can-gary-johnson-the-libertarian-nominee-swing-the-election.html', 'snippet': 'If he can increase his standing in the polls by five points in the next six weeks or so, he’ll qualify for the debate and could have a big impact.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Gary Johnson’s first run for the presidency in 2012, as the Libertarian Party candidate, he won just under 1 percent of the popular vote. He did not surpass 3 percent in any state.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 424, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 424}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 724, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1447, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/03/upshot/03UP-3rd-Johnson/03UP-3rd-Johnson-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Gary Johnson, the Libertarian Nominee, Swing the Election?', 'kicker': 'The 2016 Race', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Politics (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 1992', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Gary E', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Libertarian Party (US)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Elections (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-04T11:00:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Upshot', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Josh Katz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Josh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Katz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8afa347-8f0e-5dc9-8520-7b2a29c9f9e1', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8afa347-8f0e-5dc9-8520-7b2a29c9f9e1'}, {'abstract': 'Major third-party presidential candidates have never had an easy time of it, even when they were former presidents or billionaires.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/upshot/third-party-candidates-through-the-years.html', 'snippet': 'Major third-party presidential candidates have never had an easy time of it, even when they were former presidents or billionaires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Recent polls show the Libertarian Party nominee, Gary Johnson, at around 10 percent nationally, a relatively high number for a third-party candidate this late in the campaign season. Major third-party presidential candidates have never had an easy time of it, even when they were former presidents or billionaires. Here’s a short his