jor': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-04T16:19:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/d4b4a631-09a9-513c-9ae1-6b2269ba866e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/d4b4a631-09a9-513c-9ae1-6b2269ba866e'}, {'abstract': 'Also, arguing over an ashtray, how to stand up to a selfish friend and the curious case of the always-undercooked burger.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/fashion/social-qs-dating-work-supervisor.html', 'snippet': 'Also, arguing over an ashtray, how to stand up to a selfish friend and the curious case of the always-undercooked burger.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I went to dinner with a supervisor from work, unsure what his intentions were. After dinner, he was direct: He is interested in me romantically and wants to date. He said that he had thought through the professional ramifications, and they were worth it for him. But I still have ambitions at the firm. And even though he would never be in a position to promote me, he is very much a boss. The date was amazing, and he is amazing. Should I continue seeing him?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'w