niacs” will be newly rereleased this week, shares the four-decade-long tale of his iconic facial hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/t-magazine/entertainment/john-waters-mustache-director.html', 'snippet': 'The director, whose sleazy classic “Multiple Maniacs” will be newly rereleased this week, shares the four-decade-long tale of his iconic facial hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'John Waters doesn’t remember exactly why he first grew his iconic pencil mustache, but he does remember when: 1970. It had only been six years since the Baltimore native graduated high school, and only four since he had been kicked out of NYU during a marijuana bust on campus. But he was already a prolific filmmaker, then working on his fifth film and what he calls his “real” first feature, “Multiple Maniacs” (1970), which will receive a theatrical rerelease at New York’s IFC Center beginning on August 5. “I dressed like a hippie pimp,” he says of his sartorial style during the period when he made the film. “I had long hair and wore ridiculous thrift-shop shirts. The mustache just went along with my sleazy look.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/t-magazine/04tmag-waters01/04tmag-waters01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 420, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/04/t-magazine/04tmag-waters01/04tmag-waters01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 420}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/t-magazine/04tmag-waters01/04tmag-waters01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 717, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/t-magazine/04tmag-waters01/04tmag-waters01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 143