://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/06/sports/olympics/rio-games-opening-ceremony-flame-caldron.html', 'snippet': 'Fire is a rarer element than even gold at the Olympic Games. Usually, just one athlete is selected to close the opening ceremony.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RIO DE JANEIRO — Sometimes it is one of the most famous athletes in the world, like Muhammad Ali in 1996. Other times it is an archer or a cross-country skier whose name you will never hear again. But whoever it is, the person who lights the caldron at the opening ceremony is given one of the highest honors at an Olympics.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 834, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1667, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/06/sports/06CALDRONadd/06CALDRONadd-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20