in two recent interviews.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/06/us/politics/hillary-clinton-nabj-nahj.html', 'snippet': 'Before a convention of minority journalists, the Democratic nominee said she “may have short-circuited” when asked about her private email use in two recent interviews.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Hillary Clinton on Friday sought to explain her recent mischaracterization of the F.B.I. investigation into her private email server, saying she “may have short-circuited” in her remarks during a television interview on Sunday when she asserted that the F.B.I. director, James B. Comey, had called her statements about her private email servers “truthful.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A ‘Short-Circuit’ on F.B.I. Inquiry? Hillary Clinton Seeks to Explain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Did She ‘Short-Circuit’ on the F.B.I. Inquiry? Clinton Seeks to Explain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alcindor, Yamiche', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Assn of Black Journalists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Comey, James B', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-05T10:00:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yamiche Alcindor and Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yamiche', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alcindor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1811179-1d7b-53f5-93a4-ac211a686759', 'word_count': 935, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1811179-1d7b-53f5-93a4-ac211a686759'}, {'abstract': 'Figuring out how to make fire was no doubt an evolutionary boon to our ancestors. But it may have led to our smoking habit and the emergence of tuberculosis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/science/fire-smoke-evolution-tuberculosis.html', 'snippet': 'Figuring out how to make fire was no doubt an evolutionary boon to our ancestors. But it may have led to our smoking habit and the emergence of tuberculosis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When early humans discovered how to build fires, life became much easier in many regards. They huddled around fire for warmth, light and protection. They used it to cook, which afforded them more calories than eating raw foods that were hard to chew and digest. They could socialize into the night, which possibly gave rise to storytelling and other cultural traditions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/science/09SMOKE/09SMOKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/05/science/09SMOKE/09SMOKE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/science/09SMOKE/09SMOKE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 