e': 'YOURISH', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Derek', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'WATKINS', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Tom', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'GIRATIKANON', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Jasmine', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'LEE', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/f25678b0-68ad-5c0d-94ab-e9e2de0c6635', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/f25678b0-68ad-5c0d-94ab-e9e2de0c6635'}, {'abstract': 'Rodrigo Duterte’s solution to the crime and drug problems — extrajudicial assassinations — will do grievous harm to the country’s democracy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/05/opinion/the-presidents-killing-spree-in-the-philippines.html', 'snippet': 'Rodrigo Duterte’s solution to the crime and drug problems — extrajudicial assassinations — will do grievous harm to the country’s democracy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'During his campaign, Rodrigo Duterte promised, in so many words, that he would launch a killing spree aimed at ridding the Philippines of drug-related crime as soon as he became president. He offered bounties to the police, the military, indeed anyone who wanted to help him with the job of assassinating 100,000 criminals during his first six months in office. He bragged there would be so many bodies in Manila Bay that “the fish will grow fat.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The President’s Killing Spree in the Philippines', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duterte, Rodrigo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-05T12:46:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/53b6757e-4f3d-5bc9-9ede-055466133898', 'word_count': 337, 'uri': 'nyt://article/53b6757e-4f3d-5bc9-9ede-055466133898'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: China on the brink of rebellion in August, 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/05/1891-china-on-the-brink-of-rebellion/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: China on the brink of rebellion in August, 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Our Shanghai correspondent, in a letter which we publish today [Aug. 6], sends us news of the gravest importance. China is on the brink of a rebellion permeating every corner of the Empire.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/blogs/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/06/blogs/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 872}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/blogs/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/blogs/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung/06iht-retrospective-Li-Hung-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1545, 'width': 1063, 'subType': 'sup