celerator bootcamp. Here’s some insight into what we learned.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/05/design-thinking-for-media-that-matters/', 'snippet': 'Eight New York Times product managers and engineers recently participated in Matter’s media startup accelerator bootcamp. Here’s some insight into what we learned.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the end of May, eight New York Times product managers and engineers participated in Matter’s media startup accelerator bootcamp. Over four strenuous days, we learned the process of design thinking: a human-centered, prototype-driven approach to creating something that fills a meaningful need in someone’s life.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Design Thinking for Media That Matters', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Entrepreneurship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Matter Ventures', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-05T14:15:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Ording', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ording', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5d7bdf9-b635-58e8-946b-06d4611846c9', 'word_count': 655, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5d7bdf9-b635-58e8-946b-06d4611846c9'}, {'abstract': 'Commissioner William B. Evans’s leadership style and close ties with minority communities have helped keep police-related violence in Boston to a minimum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/06/us/boston-police-chief-on-defusing-tensions-relationships-matter.html', 'snippet': 'Commissioner William B. Evans’s leadership style and close ties with minority communities have helped keep police-related violence in Boston to a minimum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BOSTON — The violent confrontations between the police and minorities that have erupted in many cities over the last couple of years have created new pressures on police commanders across the country. Many of them were already dealing with issues of morale, recruitment and retention, and community relations. But Boston, a city with a history of racial tensions, has been comparatively calm.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/05/us/06bostonpd-web1/06bostonpd-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Boston Police Chief on Defusing Tensions: Relationships Matter', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boston Police Chief on Defusing Tensions: Relationships Matter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Evans, William B (1959- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Boston (Mass)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Minorities', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attacks on Police', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-05T14:16:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b39568f-8322-5913-b7f9-d96766bba038', 'word_count': 1503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b39568f-8322-5913-b7f9-d96766bba038'}, {'abstract': '“It’s almost always better when your subject is in motion,” the theater critic writes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/05/insider/ben-brantleys-no-1-tip-for-interviewing-barbra-streisand-get-her-to-show-you-the-house.html', 'snippet': '“It’s almost always better when your subject is in motion,” the theater critic writes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider delivers behind-the-scenes insights into how news, fe