s, it led with the good news — nearly 38 percent of students statewide were proficient in English and about 39 percent were proficient in math, up from the previous year’s results. But it also warned that the scores could not be compared with previous results “apples to apples,” because of changes in the way the tests were written and given.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York State Test Scores Inspire Conflicting Interpretations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Test Scores Inspire Clashing Interpretations', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tests and Examinations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de Blasio, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Elia, MaryEllen (1948- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-06T02:08:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f64f3d7a-121a-5632-ac3e-cbae6c23f9c4', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f64f3d7a-121a-5632-ac3e-cbae6c23f9c4'}, {'abstract': 'The government always seems to be making, neglecting, forgetting and rediscovering its covenant with veterans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/06/opinion/broken-promises-to-homeless-vets.html', 'snippet':