ion of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-06T18:30:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian McFadden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McFadden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cdc99c54-6415-5d5c-93a0-110906e0bab7', 'word_count': 9, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cdc99c54-6415-5d5c-93a0-110906e0bab7'}, {'abstract': 'The community school model makes alleviating the ills of poverty part of academic success. So far, it’s working.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/07/opinion/sunday/to-teach-a-child-to-read-first-give-him-glasses.html', 'snippet': 'The community school model makes alleviating the ills of poverty part of academic success. So far, it’s working.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Half a dozen police cars ring the entrance to the Morris Educational Campus in the Bronx. To enter this venerable Gothic-style building, I have to make my way through a phalanx of policemen and be scanned by a metal detector.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/opinion/sunday/07kirp/07kirp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/07/opinion/sunday/07kirp/07kirp-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/07/opinion/sunday/07kirp/07kirp-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': N