ense of identity that he is not permitted to resign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'At 82, Emperor Akihito of Japan Wants to Retire. Will Japan Let Him?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Japan’s Emperor Humbly Asks: Let Me Retire', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Soble, Jonathan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'AKIHITO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Naruhito, Crown Prince of Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Royal Families', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Michiko, Empress of Japan', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ABE, SHINZO', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-08T01:01:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Soble', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soble', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03553a0c-b4e4-59f9-94bb-bcf1868327d3', 'word_count': 1389, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03553a0c-b4e4-59f9-94bb-bcf1868327d3'}, {'abstract': 'Dr. Pitanguy established himself in Brazil as one of the world’s most famous plastic surgeons, as much through his marketing savvy as through his surgical skills.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/08/obituaries/dr-ivo-pitanguy-pioneering-brazilian-plastic-surgeon-dies-at-93.html', 'snippet': 'Dr. Pitanguy established himself in Brazil as one of the world’s most famous plastic surgeons, as much through his marketing savvy as through his surgical skills.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dr. Ivo Pitanguy, a pioneering Brazilian plastic surgeon who performed face lifts, tummy tucks and other procedures on the rich, famous and royal, becoming rich, famous and celebrated in his own right, died on Saturday at his home in Rio de Janeiro. He was 93.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/obituaries/08Pitanguy-obit/08Pitanguyobit-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ivo Pitanguy, Plastic Surgeon to the Stars and a Celebrity Himself, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ivo Pitanguy, Brazil’s Plastic Surgery Pioneer, Dies at 93', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pitanguy, Ivo (1926-2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plastic Surgery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-08T01:19:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Singer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Singer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/7388602c-bfcf-5c13-985a-cf9af8d1fb87', 'word_count': 1114, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7388602c-bfcf-5c13-985a-cf9af8d1fb87'}, {'abstract': 'As the head of a Chamber of Commerce, Mr. Tiber, an unlikely counterculture hero, offered a home for the music festival. He wrote two memoirs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/08/arts/music/elliot-tiber-who-with-a-permit-unleashed-woodstock-and-himself-dies-at-81.html', 'snippet': 'As the head of a Chamber of Commerce, Mr. Tiber, an unlikely counterculture hero, offered a home for the music festival. He wrote two memoirs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July 1969, the town of Wallkill, N.Y., dealt a potentially mortal blow to Woodstock Ventures, a group of rookie promoters hoping to organize a grand festival of rock music in rural New York.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/arts/08Tiber-Obit1/