91-d5c50f677677', 'word_count': 843, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b18dcd04-9c69-5aa8-b691-d5c50f677677'}, {'abstract': 'The truth is we “sustain” nature to preserve the resources needed for our own consumption.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/08/opinion/against-sustainability.html', 'snippet': 'The truth is we “sustain” nature to preserve the resources needed for our own consumption.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many stories that can be told about the origins of the environmental movement in the West, perhaps the most common is that it began with the emergence of Romanticism in the late 18th century. In this version, environmentalism was born as the good twin to evil industrialization. Today, when we talk about ecological sustainability and environmental preservation, we typically still understand them in terms of a battle between nature and industry.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stoneWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stoneWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stoneWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stone1Web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stone1Web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/06/opinion/08stone1Web/08stone1Web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Against ‘Sustainability’', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Against ‘Sustainability’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sustainable Living', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Descartes, Rene', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Sixth Extinction: An Unnatural History (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-08T07:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Butman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Butman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b070863-411f-5caf-a964-5dce847ff261', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b070863-411f-5caf-a964-5dce847ff261'}, {'abstract': 'On what is likely the most diverse college campus in the United States, Muslim women who wear a hijab talk about their lives.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/08/listening-to-the-voices-from-hijabi-world/', 'snippet': 'On what is likely the most diverse college campus in the United States, Muslim women who wear a hijab talk about their lives.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To set foot on the campus of Rutgers University, Newark, is to witness a majority-minority census in three dimensions. Brown, black, beige and every shade in between, the university’s population is robust with first-generation Americans redefining attitudes about race, interfaith dialogue and national identity. Those features have led it to be ranked by U.S. News and World Report as the most diverse campus in the United States. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Listening to the Voices From Hijabi World', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim Veiling', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muslim-Americans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Rutgers, The State University of New Jersey', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Jersey City (NJ)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Newark (NJ)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-08T08:00:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Julie Winokur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Julie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Winokur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434ca156-9afb-5e4b-bfee-e606b43e217e', 'word_count': 582, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434ca156-9afb-5e4b-bfee-e606b43e217e'}, {'abstract': 'Taiwan said the deportations of five of its people to the mainland, which followed similar ones in April, showed “contempt for human rights.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/world/asia/china-kenya-taiwan-deported.html', 'snippet': 'Taiwan said t