nnaise and comes in a spicier version, too.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The condiment of choice for chicken or meat at halal street carts is a thick drizzle that’s simply called white sauce. Jamal Rasoully, whose parents fled Afghanistan about 30 years ago and opened a restaurant in New York, said that they made such a sauce based on an old Pashtun recipe. Now, Mr. Rasoully has bottled the condiment, calling it Spin Sauce. The traditional sauce is yogurt-based, but this one has mayonnaise written all over it and certainly delivers all-purpose potential. There’s a spicier version and a fierce cayenne hot sauce, too: Spin Sauce, $11.99 for three 12-ounce bottles, spinsauce.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 663}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 927, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 1203, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB/10BURNERSAUCES-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/