to pasta and other dishes. Most bottarga is a fisherman’s afterthought, coming from parts of the catch that otherwise may be discarded. But Marc Slakmon, who learned to make it from his Tunisian grandmothers, has teamed up with a Florida fisherman who is catching gray mullet in the Gulf of Mexico. Their company, Dell’Isola Foods, produces Bottarga Dell’Isola, and chefs are praising its quality. It is rich, briny and pleasantly funky with an excellent consistency for slicing, shaving or grating: Bottarga Dell’Isola, $32 to $118 whole, depending on the size; $25 for a two-ounce jar of grated; bottargadellisola.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 372, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 372}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 634, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1269, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10BURNER-BOTTARGA-WEB/10BUR