rial': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b9e093a-ae9c-544a-9aea-b6e1ec065eff', 'word_count': 608, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b9e093a-ae9c-544a-9aea-b6e1ec065eff'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: In August 1871, the Bank of England makes a statement through the Herald Tribune to reassure about a potential financial crash.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/08/1891-bank-of-england-reassures/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: In August 1871, the Bank of England makes a statement through the Herald Tribune to reassure about a potential financial crash.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Governor of the Bank of England, Sir William Lidderdale, has consented to make a statement to the public through the Herald, in consequence of the alarming stories in America and on the Continent, to the effect that a general financial crash is near at hand, and that the British banks are afraid to let the full situation be known, for fear it would precipitate a panic throughout the world. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/blogs/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 497, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/blogs/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 587, 'width': 497, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/blogs/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1/09oldiht-1891-bankofengland1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/20