now-soap.html', 'snippet': 'In Toronto, Binu Binu makes sculptural bars packed with nourishing oils that take inspiration from the Korean bathhouse.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Korean body scrub is a spa experience not easily forgotten — the intensely exfoliating rubdown requires a certain amount of grit and courage. For the Toronto native Karen Kim, 36, the memory of her Korean grandmother buffing her body when she was 5 years old left a lasting impression: “The vigor and determination!” she says of the sloughing technique. “It was painful but effective.” Years later, when she was in her 20s, Kim traveled to Seok Mo Do, a fishing island off the coast of South Korea, with her mother and five aunts. Most days revolved around trips to the public baths and cleansing rituals. “Every morning, we’d take our sponges and buckets, and sit in the bath all day,” she says. “My Korean isn’t very good, so it was hard to communicate, but this was an intimate bonding moment.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08-tmag-binu-01/08-tmag-binu-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08-tmag-binu-01/08-tmag-binu-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08-tmag-binu-01/08-tmag-binu-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08-tmag-binu-01/08-tmag-binu-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 