al to the development of pop and the integration of MTV.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/arts/music/janet-jackson-control-anniversary.html', 'snippet': 'Thirty years after the release of her album “Control,” Janet Jackson remains essential to the development of pop and the integration of MTV.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The standard for planet-stopping artistic statements in pop music is now so high that you need a pilot’s license to compete with the Beyoncés, Kanyes and Kendricks of the world. But when Janet Jackson craved ascent, she didn’t go to flight school. She went to Flyte Tyme. That was the Minneapolis production company Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis operated and where the three came up with “Control,” Ms. Jackson’s third record and the first of their subtly strange, sonically complex thematic carnivals. The album turned 30 in February, peaked in popularity right about this time that year (hitting No. 1 in July) and still sounds today as much like 1986 as it does 2056. Some producers make hooks. These three made wedgies.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 999, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/arts/09JANET/09JANET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sorry, Ms. Jackson: You’re Underrated. ‘Control’ at 30', 'kicker': "Critic's Notebook", 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '30 Years Later, It’s Complicated  for Janet Jackson', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Morris, Wesley', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MTV Networks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jackson, Janet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-08T22:12:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Wesley Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Wesley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edafff6e-e588-5850-bc54-1eb73a642a92', 'word_count': 1569, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edafff6e-e588-5850-bc54-1eb73a642a92'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/08/08/nytnow/your-evening-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know at the end of the day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Her