'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ceaffda-c20c-594c-9de8-5b31da263ff7', 'word_count': 706, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ceaffda-c20c-594c-9de8-5b31da263ff7'}, {'abstract': 'Satellite imagery shows China has been building reinforced hangars on the disputed Spratly Islands that can easily accommodate warplanes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/world/asia/china-spratly-islands-south-china-sea.html', 'snippet': 'Satellite imagery shows China has been building reinforced hangars on the disputed Spratly Islands that can easily accommodate warplanes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When President Xi Jinping of China visited President Obama at the White House last September, he startled many with reassuring words about his intentions for the Spratly Islands, a contested area where the Chinese government has been piling dredged sand and concrete atop reefs for the past few years and building housing and runways on them.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New Photos Cast Doubt on China’s Vow Not to Militarize Disputed Islands', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Photos Raise Questions on China’s Promise Not to Militarize Disputed Islands', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South China Sea', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spratly Islands', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'v