-reality.html', 'snippet': 'Opdivo didn’t help my wife, or almost anyone else. So why can Bristol-Myers Squibb market it on TV?', 'lead_paragraph': 'TOWSON, Md. — Two days into a long-dreamed-of family vacation to Italy in August 2013, my wife, Ronna, became nauseated, unusually tired and short of breath. One of the great non-complainers in American history, she insisted that it was no big deal and valiantly tried to join in on various outings in the Italian countryside. But, after a few increasingly difficult days, even Ronna knew that it was time to go to the emergency room.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 432, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 432}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 737, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1168, 'width': 1622, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09JABLOW-web/09JABLOW-web-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Cancer-Drug Ads vs. Cancer-Drug Reality', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Drug Ads vs. Drug Reality', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lung Cancer', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jablow, Matt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Clinical Trials', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADVERTISING AND MARKETING', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bristol Myers Squibb Company', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food and Drug Administration', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matt Jablow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matt', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jablow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/e0911f9d-a3fe-5485-90d9-e6f1c8208bcd', 'word_count': 773, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e0911f9d-a3fe-5485-90d9-e6f1c8208bcd'}, {'abstract': 'Service members who have been assaulted shouldn’t have to add “other-than-honorable” discharge to their injustices.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/opinion/what-the-military-owes-rape-survivors-like-my-daughter.html', 'snippet': 'Service members who have been assaulted shouldn’t have to add “other-than-honorable” discharge to their injustices.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LA CROSSE, Wis. — When my daughter, Carri Leigh Goodwin, joined the Marine Corps in July 2007, she was a shy, quiet 18-year-old who loved reading and writing poetry. She joined the Marines to make me proud — I’m a former Marine — and to her surprise, she turned out to be good with a gun.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/09noling/09noling-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What the Military Owes Rape Survivors Like My Daughter', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Restoring My Daughter’s Honor', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Noling, Gary', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sex Crimes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodwin, Carri Leigh (1989-2009)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Marine Corps', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Post-Traumatic Stress Disorder', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alcohol Abuse', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mabus, Ray', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Navy', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goodwin, Carri Leigh', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Noling', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Noling', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/28dcf3f8-f23a-5b2b-a6fc-f34e7fef5f2f', 'word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/28dcf3f8-f23a-5b2b-a6fc-f34e7fef5f2f'}, {'abstract': 'The United Nations Security Council should impose an embargo on arms shipments as part of a solution to end the killing and other abuses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/opinion/time-to-get-serious-with-south-sudan.html', 'snippet': 'The United Nations Security Council should impose an embargo on arms shipments as part of a solution to end the killing and other abuses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since the founding of the nation of South Sudan five years ago, its citizens have gone from a brief moment of exhilaration and promise to the cruel reality of tribal violence, depredation and despair. Their leaders have failed them, and 