: None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/55bad651-5cc1-5463-95a4-e84db4a4b305', 'word_count': 3102, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55bad651-5cc1-5463-95a4-e84db4a4b305'}, {'abstract': 'Warplanes struck Sana, killing civilians, after the collapse of talks between Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed government.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/world/middleeast/yemen-sana-airstrikes.html', 'snippet': 'Warplanes struck Sana, killing civilians, after the collapse of talks between Houthi rebels and the Saudi-backed government.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SANA, Yemen — The military coalition led by Saudi Arabia significantly stepped up its bombing campaign in Yemen on Tuesday, striking the capital, Sana, and killing 21 people across the country, most of them civilians, according to medical and security officials in three provinces.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Saudi-Led Coalition Resumes Bombing of Yemeni Capital After Talks Collapse', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Saudi-Led Coalition Steps Up Bombing in Yemen After Peace Talks Collapse', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houthis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nordland, Rod', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Almosawa, Shuaib', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sana (Yemen)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T12:44:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shuaib Almosawa and Rod Nordland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shuaib', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Almosawa', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rod', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Nordland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6b840759-e75c-567c-999d-77bee5a25521', 'word_count': 689, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6b840759-e75c-567c-999d-77bee5a25521'}, {'abstract': 'It’s 90 days until the election. Twice a week on our new podcast, the campaign team at The Times will make sense of the final, delirious phase of the campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/podcasts/introducing-the-run-up-our-new-election-podcast.html', 'snippet': 'It’s 90 days until the election. Twice a week on our new podcast, the campaign team at The Times will make sense of the final, delirious phase of the campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s three months until Election Day. To guide you through this final, delirious phase of the presidential campaign, The New York Times is drawing on our all-star team of reporters, columnists, magazine writers and analysts to create a new podcast. It’s called The Run-Up.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/podcasts/09runup-illo/09runup-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 187, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/podcasts/09runup-illo/09runup-illo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 187}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/podcasts/09runup-illo/09runup-illo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': '