eral of the International Organization of la Francophonie, spent a recent morning at the sultry Lagoa Olympic venue, where the world’s most exciting rowing was taking place. She was not so interested in what was happening on the water.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1381, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2/10FRANCOPHONEWEB2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brazilians Speak Portuguese, but the Olympics Must Use French', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brazilians Speak Portuguese,  but Games Are Tied to French', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'French Language', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyall, Sarah', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of la Francophonie', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Language and Languages', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T14:17:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Olympics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Lyall', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyall', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/60be096e-7c53-564c-bbe4-22a04c175638', 'word_count': 1167, 'uri': 'nyt://article/60be096e-7c53-564c-bbe4-22a04c175638'}, {'abstract': 'One of our Search interns shares details about his summer project — improving word relevancy to increase the relevancy of search results — and his experience working with the team.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/summer-intern-report-prototyping-an-improved-search-query-with-machine-learning/', 'snippet': 'One of our Search interns shares details about his summer project — improving word relevancy to increase the relevancy of search results — and his experience working with the team.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was thrilled when I was offered the summer internship for two specific reasons. First, it was with The New York Times and second, I was going to join the Search team. I was looking for an opportunity that intersected with my interests in information retrieval and machine learning. More importantly, I would have a chance to use what I had been learning in grad school. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Summer Intern Report: Prototyping an Improved Search Query With Machine Learning', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internships', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Search Engines', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T14:31:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tushar Baraiya', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tushar', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Baraiya', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1a690f2c-ca8f-52b1-b10c-54c7fd546425', 'word_count': 937, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1a690f2c-ca8f-52b1-b10c-54c7fd546425'}, {'abstract': 'The meat is soaked in egg whites, breaded, pounded to half-inch thickness and fit to the size of the plate before being sautéed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/dining/chicken-paillard-21-club.html', 'snippet': 'The meat is soaked in egg whites, breaded, pounded to half-inch thickness and fit to the size of the plate before being sautéed.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am about as likely to order chicken paillard as I am to want my steak well done. But at lunch in the “21” Club Bar Room a couple of weeks ago, my arm was twisted by an enthusiastic captain, and I succumbed.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/dining/10PAILLARD-WEB1/10PAILLARD-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'hei