/10/dining/blackberry-farm-mary-celeste-beall.html', 'snippet': 'Sam Beall’s death cast his widow, Mary Celeste Beall, in an unimagined role, as the head of the Blackberry Farm resort and a leader in the elevation of hyper-local Southern cuisine.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WALLAND, Tenn. — For someone who could ski as well as Sam Beall, his first run down a Colorado slope that February afternoon was supposed to be easy.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Widow Takes the Helm at Blackberry Farm', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Living Epitaph', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Blackberry Farm (Walland, Tenn, Hotel)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beall, Sam (1976-2016)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beall, Mary Celeste', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Family Business', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T17:09:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kim Severson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Severson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f5251cd-bd40-5a0f-84bc-7c4ab00997b1', 'word_count': 1854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f5251cd-bd40-5a0f-84bc-7c4ab00997b1'}, {'abstract': '“The Republican Party has left us,” said the founder of Republican Women for Hillary. “We haven’t left the Republican Party.”', 'web_url': 'https://takingnote.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/09/conversations-what-made-two-republican-women-back-hillary-clinton/', 'snippet': '“The Republican Party has left us,” said the founder of Republican Women for Hillary. “We haven’t left the Republican Party.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“This Republican is voting for Hillary Clinton,” Jennifer Pierotti Lim proclaimed at the Democratic convention last month. That’s becoming a more common refrain lately, with high-profile Republicans like Meg Whitman throwing their support behind Mrs. Clinton. Ms. Lim, the founder of the volunteer group Republican Women for Hillary, and Meghan Milloy, the group’s chair, spoke in a recent interview about where they agree with the Democratic nominee, where they disagree and what the Republican Party would have to do to win them back.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/opinion/9northWEB3/9northWEB3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's