 of Norilsk, an industrial cityin an isolated part of Arctic Russia. No roads or trains lead there; internet is severely limited; and it is it closed to foreigners. Getting there, I would find out, is very difficult. Yet despite its obscurity, Norilsk has one of the largest mining and metallurgical complexes in the world and produces most of the earth’s palladium, an essential mineral in electronics and automobiles. Most of us probably have a bit of Norilsk in our pockets, bags or homes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'My Deadly, Beautiful City', 'kicker': 'Op-Docs', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Norilsk (Russia)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Air Pollution', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T20:01:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Victoria Fiore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Victoria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fiore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8947bd0f-1010-55a6-8d44-48e728a385ad', 'word_count': 357, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8947bd0f-1010-55a6-8d44-48e728a385ad'}, {'abstract': 'In his first public appearance in more than four years, the former Illinois governor apologized for his actions in a vast corruption scheme. But a federal judge upheld his 14-year sentence.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/us/judge-rejects-rod-blagojevichs-plea-for-reduced-sentence.html', 'snippet': 'In his first public appearance in more than four years, the former Illinois governor apologized for his actions in a vast corruption scheme. But a federal judge upheld his 14-year sentence.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Rod R. Blagojevich, a former governor of Illinois, sat in a f