8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-09T22:12:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. David Goodman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Goodman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/793684e2-ed47-5770-a75d-86ff1bb77dbd', 'word_count': 572, 'uri': 'nyt://article/793684e2-ed47-5770-a75d-86ff1bb77dbd'}, {'abstract': 'In this documentary, Molly Bernstein invites us to see the world through the lens of her subject, Ms. Purcell, a photographer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/movies/review-an-art-that-nature-makes-an-illuminating-look-at-rosamond-purcell.html', 'snippet': 'In this documentary, Molly Bernstein invites us to see the world through the lens of her subject, Ms. Purcell, a photographer.', 'lead_paragraph': '“An Art That Nature Makes: The Work of Rosamond Purcell” is the portrait of an artist who is not interested in portraits. Early in her career as a photographer, Ms. Purcell remarks, she stopped taking pictures of people. In the years since — she’s 74 now — she has established herself as a visual poet of the inanimate, a still-life painter with a camera.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/arts/10ARTNATURE/10ARTNATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/arts/10ARTNATURE/10ARTNATURE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/a