and Lil Yachty are among the acts scheduled to perform at this event in Manhattan. Local rappers are also on the bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two distinct tangents of Atlanta’s flamboyant, overflowing rap scene will take over the Manhattan waterfront on Saturday, Aug. 20: Migos, the three-headed hydra of euphoric, rapid-fire catchphrases, and Lil Yachty, the self-proclaimed “king of the teens,” with his singsong flow and constantly bouncing red-beaded braids. Both will bring the joyful youth contingent to the seventh annual Fool’s Gold Day Off party, which also features the promising local rappers Leaf, Meyhem Lauren and Dave East.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE3/14GUIDE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Atlanta Rappers Join Fool’s Gold Day Off Party', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; Singsong Flow and Red Braids', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Migos (Music Group)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lil Yachty (Rapper)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T13:55:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a87c829-73c3-5c74-9611-ddf95c96336e', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a87c829-73c3-5c74-9611-ddf95c96336e'}, {'abstract': 'More than 140 works by 35 artists, each one priced under $750, will be featured at this Brooklyn gallery.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/arts/design/collector-helper-at-anthony-philip-fine-art.html', 'snippet': 'More than 140 works by 35 artists, each one priced under $750, will be featured at this Brooklyn gallery.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Part of the mission of Anthony Philip Fine Art in Bushwick, Brooklyn, is to connect emerging artists with aspiring collectors. So the gallery’s latest show, opening Friday, Aug. 12, aims specifically at young and novice collectors. “Life Sized: A Small Works Invitational” features more than 140 artworks that are under 12 inches by 12 inches and priced under $750. “Our hope is that there will be something here for anyone looking to jump-start their collection,” Mr. Philip said. The 35 artists in the show work in a range of media, including painting, sculpture, photography, abstract art and traditional drawing. Among them are Kristen Balouch, Jonathan Quinn and Tariku Shiferaw from New York; Amy Lottes, Jeff Kapfer and Barb Flunker from Missouri; and artists from Kansas, South Carolina and Washington. (Through Sept. 3; anthonyphilipfineart.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 582, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 582}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 993, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1986, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE1/14GUIDE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Collector Helper at Anthony Philip Fine Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Priced to Sell and Made to Carry', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Collectors and Collections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Philip, Anthony, Fine Art (Brooklyn, NY, Gallery)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T13:56:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robin Pogrebin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pogrebin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc65e3ec-72e0-5a7f-bbbd-5970522f03db', 'word_count': 133, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc65e3ec-72e0-5a7f-bbbd-5970522f03db'}, {'abstract': 'The museum has a partnership with the new-music collective Bang on a Can, which is bringing the American Contemporary Music Ensemble to the sculpture garden.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/arts/music/in-the-garden-with-strings-at-the-noguchi-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The museum has a partnership with the new-music collective Bang on a Can, which is bringing the American Contemporary Music Ensemble to the sculpture garden.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are few lovelier places to hear music in New York City than in the sculpture garden of the Noguchi Museum in Queens. The museum has a partnership with the new-music collective Bang on a Can, which on Sunday, Aug. 14, brings the American Contemporary Music Ensemble to the garden. On the program are string quartets by Philip Glass and Meredith Monk as well as the premiere of a cello solo by Caleb Burhans, played by Clarice Jensen, the ensemble’s artistic director. (3 p.m., 718-204-7088, noguchi.org.)', 'pr