)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Releases (Entertainment)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T14:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Hoberman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d62ad89f-b259-5ca4-9440-f69c9e70075c', 'word_count': 973, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d62ad89f-b259-5ca4-9440-f69c9e70075c'}, {'abstract': 'The star of “Not Safe With Nikki Glaser” on Comedy Central will headline six shows, beginning on Thursday, Aug. 18.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/theater/the-comic-nikki-glaser-at-carolines-on-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'The star of “Not Safe With Nikki Glaser” on Comedy Central will headline six shows, beginning on Thursday, Aug. 18.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The dynamic stand-up comic Nikki Glaser has produced a popular podcast, co-hosted a short-lived talk show on MTV and starred in several memorable sketches on “Inside Amy Schumer.” But the best example of her wry and raunchy sense of humor may be in “Not Safe With Nikki Glaser,” a cheerfully sex-obsessed series on Comedy Central. The show, which includes high-concept videos that take her places like a porn shoot (where she feeds lines to actors) and a foot fetish party, helps Ms. Glaser come off as forever game, if also a little startled by her own chutzpah. This tension between her bluntness and her anxiety has long been the engine fueling her charismatic, assured stand-up, the bedrock of her prolific young career. She headlines six shows at Carolines on Broadway, starting on Thursday, Aug. 18. (212-757-4100, carolines.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE7/14GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Comic Nikki Glaser at Carolines on Broadway', 'kicker': 'The Week Ahead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Theater; Wry and Raunchy, Played for Laughs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Caroline's on Broadway", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Inside Amy Schumer (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Not Safe With Nikki Glaser (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Glaser, Nikki', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T14:02:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fa524547-3461-5591-8493-a27b76d0bd2d', 'word_count': 137, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fa524547-3461-5591-8493-a27b76d0bd2d'}, {'abstract': 'The IFC Center and Socrates Sculpture Park are featuring the films of Federico Fellini and Werner Herzog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/movies/a-fellini-summer-a-conquistadors-too.html', 'snippet': 'The IFC Center and Socrates Sculpture Park are featuring the films of Federico Fellini and Werner Herzog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In its Weekend Classics series, the IFC Center has been hosting a stealth Federico Fellini festival this summer, with screenings at the un-Fellinilike hour of 11 a.m. “Amarcord,” the director’s most nostalgic memoir, evoking the small coastal Italian town where he grew up, is on Sunday, Aug. 14; on Friday and Saturday is “Roma,” a valentine to the city to which he is eternally wed. (ifccenter.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 916, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/arts/14GUIDE5/14GUIDE5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewid