onaltech/sharing-the-laptops-screen-with-the-tv.html', 'snippet': 'You can watch the video from your laptop on your television, as long as you have the correct cable or other hardware to connect them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. I don’t have a tablet or internet television and I want to stream video from my laptop to my TV. How do I do that?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Sharing the Laptop’s Screen With the TV', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television Sets and Media Devices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Laptop Computers', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T15:17:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/e28fdb5b-2dfb-5bd6-9e39-c9e97906bf1c', 'word_count': 365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e28fdb5b-2dfb-5bd6-9e39-c9e97906bf1c'}, {'abstract': 'An island-ravaging cyclone hasn’t been able to keep the lifter Apolonia Vaivai from competing in the Olympics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/04/magazine/weight-lifting-her-way-from-fiji-to-rio.html', 'snippet': 'An island-ravaging cyclone hasn’t been able to keep the lifter Apolonia Vaivai from competing in the Olympics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On a Wednesday morning in July, the weight lifter Apolonia Vaivai leaned against the cinder-block wall of a crowded bus stall in the South Pacific port city of Suva, Fiji. Vaivai, who is 25 and just over five feet tall and thick with muscle, was wearing turquoise workout shorts and a matching T-shirt and cap bearing a Monster energy-drink logo that covered the tips of her ears. She had come to town to arrange a visa for the Rio Olympic Games, even though she was not yet sure if she was going. Fiji had earned one spot in the women’s weight lifting program, but Weightlifting Fiji, the country’s governing body for the sport, had yet to reveal who would fill it. Rather than wait in Suva for the announcement, Vaivai decided to make the jarring, four-hour bus-and-ferry trip home to Ovalau, a nearby island. “In three days,” she told me later on the ferry, “I’ll find out if I’m going to the Olympics.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 391, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 391}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/04/magazine/04mag-weightlifter/04mag-weightlifter-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 667, 'width': 1024, 'subType