.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10hamilton-obit/10hamilton-obit-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/sports/10hamilton-obit/10hamilton-obit-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seena Hamilton, a Pioneer in Youth Tennis, Is Dead at 92', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Seena Hamilton, 92, Who Founded ‘Super Bowl of Junior Tennis,’ Is Dead', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weber, Bruce (Journalist)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hamilton, Seena', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T16:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bruce Weber', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bruce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weber', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/5b303275-afd9-5ebb-8d9c-ac55fe3eabe0', 'word_count': 716, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5b303275-afd9-5ebb-8d9c-ac55fe3eabe0'}, {'abstract': 'Ryan McGinness breaks down some of the iconography in his striking series of “Signals” paintings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/t-magazine/art/ryan-mcginness-symbol-paintings.html', 'snippet': 'Ryan McGinness breaks down some of the iconography in his striking series of “Signals” paintings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The paintings in the artist Ryan McGinness’s new series, “Signals,” immediately invite interpretation — and then, just as quickly, elude it. Each of the pieces is a circular wood panel, 18 inches in diameter and ringed by a thick red outline. Inside are a handful of stark, graphic black-and-white symbols (a bomb with a seedling sprouting from it; a string tied around a middle finger) that strongly evoke meaning, without giving it all away. “They use the visual language of universal sign systems and therefore give the illusion that they are communicating blunt pedestrian information,” McGinness notes, “but they undermine that same visual language by evading elucidation.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/09/t-magazine/09tmag-mcginness01/09tmag-mcginness01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One Artist’s Very Symbolic New Work, Explained — Sort of', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Symbols', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGinness, Ryan', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-10T16:16:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandria Symonds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandria', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Symonds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bb7e9b9e-46db-584f-bee8-3079efab1151', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bb7e9b9e-46db-584f-bee8-3079efab1151'}, {'abstract': 'This peaceful haven for expat surfers has lately seen an uptick in hip new options like vegan cafes, music bars and housewares shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/travel/five-places-to-go-in-bali.html', 'snippet': 'This peaceful haven for expat surfers has lately seen an uptick in hip new options like vegan cafes, music bars and housewares shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked between beaches and rolling green rice paddies north of the flashy tourist hub of Seminyak, the bohemian enclave of Canggu (pronounced “CHANG-oo”) has always lived below the radar. A peaceful haven for expat surfers, Canggu’s mellow vibe and surf breaks have been luring backpack-toting travelers since the ’80s. Recently however, hip new options including vegan cafes, music bars and housewares shops have sprouted among the local staples like Old Man’s bar, Betelnut Café and Deus Ex Machina, a cafe and motorcycle shop. Don’t wait too long before heading this way. With a smattering of hotels in the pipeline, this laid-back area may soon see more bustle.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/travel/14SURFACING1/14SURFACING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main':