eb_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/10/t-magazine/food/cured-magazine-preservation-darra-goldstein.html', 'snippet': 'From the founder of Gastronomica and the media company behind “Mind of a Chef” comes Cured, a publication all about curing, pickling and fermenting.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last fall, the founder and editor of the James Beard Award-winning journal Gastronomica, Darra Goldstein, was busy “constructing a life without obligation.” She had left her own publication after closing the Fall 2012 issue; finished producing three books (“High Society Dinners: Dining in Tsarist Russia,” “The Oxford Companion to Sugar and Sweets” and “Fire and Ice: Classic Nordic Cooking”); and was phasing into her 2017 retirement from Williams College, where she has been teaching since 1983 and is the Willcox and Harriet Adsit professor of Russian. But an invitation from Joe Caterini, the managing partner at Zero Point Zero Production, the media company responsible for shows like “Anthony Bourdain: Parts Unknown” and the wildly popular “Mind of a Chef,” got in the way.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-cured03/10tmag-cured03-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-cured03/10tmag-cured03-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-cured03/10tmag-cured03-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 658, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-cured03/10tmag-cured03-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1317, 'width'