url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/running-across-america/', 'snippet': 'Every year some 10 to 20 runners set off to run across America, often with a fund-raising hook and a social media following.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The open road has long been a siren song for those wishing to cross the country by car, motorcycle, even bicycle. Add another traveling type to the list: runners, who are setting off on foot, often with a fund-raising hook and a social media following.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 426, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 426}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 947, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/21/health/runing-america/runing-america-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Running Across America', 'kicker': 'Well', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'New York City Marathon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T09:30:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jen A. Miller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jen', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Miller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1750ff34-dfbc-5baf-a763-9453d2b4fd79', 'word_count': 1024, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1750ff34-dfbc-5baf-a763-9453d2b4fd79'}, {'abstract': 'Employees of Abbott in India said that managers had pressured them into unethical tactics in an effort to bump up sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/business/dealbook/abbott-ausgrid-valeant.html', 'snippet': 'Employees of Abbott in India said that managers had pressured them into unethical tactics in an effort to bump up sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A sales job for Abbott in India may be a prized position, but the country is also a valuable market for the pharmaceutical company. And some employees have had to pay for the lengths that managers are willing to go to to win customers in India, where the industry is still fast-growing and highly competitive. It cost one employee his life — Ashish Awasthi jumped in front of a train, leaving a note saying that he committed suicide because he could not meet sales targets.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/business/11db-newsletter/11db-newsletter-articleLarge.jpg', 'height'