'}, {'abstract': 'President Edgar Lungu, who won a special election last year, is seeking a full term in a country whose copper-reliant economy has been hurt by weaker demand from China.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/world/africa/zambia-election-lungu-hichilema.html', 'snippet': 'President Edgar Lungu, who won a special election last year, is seeking a full term in a country whose copper-reliant economy has been hurt by weaker demand from China.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JOHANNESBURG — For the past decade, Zambia, a copper-rich nation in southern Africa, has been one of the continent’s success stories: a stable democracy that enjoyed rapid economic growth thanks to China’s ravenous demand for its main commodity.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Zambia Votes Amid Economic Slowdown and Political Violence', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Zambians Vote Amid a Slumping Economy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Onishi, Norimitsu', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Copper, Brass and Bronze', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lungu, Edgar C', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hichilema, Hakainde (1962- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Zambia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Patriotic Front (Zambia)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T12:36:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Norimitsu Onishi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Norimitsu', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Onishi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/081fde76-3b85-5452-bdff-d5f056a8e435', 'word_count': 899, 'uri': 'nyt://article/081fde76-3b85-5452-bdff-d5f056a8e435'}, {'abstract': 'The search giant’s mobile operating system was found to have unfairly favored digital services like Google Maps over those of Russian rivals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/business/international/google-fine-russia-antitrust-android.html', 'snippet': 'The search giant’s mobile operating system was found to have unfairly favored digital services like Google Maps over those of Russian rivals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Russian antitrust officials fined Google $6.8 million on Thursday, a relatively small penalty that nevertheless represents the latest in a growing list of global regulatory problems for the American search giant.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/business/01russiaandroid/01russiaandroid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/06/01/business/01russiaandroid/01russiaandroid-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/business/01russiaandroid/01russiaandroid-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/06/01/business/01russiaandroid/01russiaandroid-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/06/01/business/01russiaandroid/01russiaandroi