a company, now owned by Verizon, in 2005 and will be focusing on her new venture, Thrive Global.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/business/arianna-huffington-post.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Huffington helped begin the media company, now owned by Verizon, in 2005 and will be focusing on her new venture, Thrive Global.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Since it started 11 years ago, The Huffington Post has been synonymous with the personality and the interests of its co-founder, Arianna Huffington.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/business/12HUFFINGTON2/12HUFFINGTON2-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Arianna Huffington Is Leaving Huffington Post', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After 11 Years, The Huffington Post Will No Longer Be Run by Huffington', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Huffington Post', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Huffington, Arianna', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Appointments and Executive Changes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T13:02:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sydney Ember', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sydney', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ember', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8bd62205-9b96-594d-81f7-a75605739214', 'word_count': 1130, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8bd62205-9b96-594d-81f7-a75605739214'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The French attitude on racism is being questioned in the press in August 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/1966-france-worries-about-racism/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The French attitude on racism is being questioned in the press in August 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS, France — U.S. racial violence and the increasing immigration of foreign workers are beginning to inspire serious public concern in France. Hirtherto an all but taboo subject, the French attitude on racism is now being questioned in an important segment of the press. In the past two weeks, these observations have been made here: The respected, middle-class ‘‘Figaro,’’ under the ‘‘Harlem-sur-Seine’’ headline: ‘‘The most optimistic estimates of some high functionaries indicate that the Negro population of France will go up to 650,000 in 1980. Others, more ‘pessimistic,’ advance the figure of a million.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 12, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: France Worries About Racism', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'FRANCE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T13:06:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d5281923-87d2-5963-8bce-e31dffb3c58c', 'word_count': 104, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d5281923-87d2-5963-8bce-e31dffb3c58c'}, {'abstract': 'Macy’s announcement closely follows that of Walmart, which said it would buy Jet.com in what is widely viewed as a way to invigorate its online sales.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/business/macys-q2-earnings-store-closings.html', 'snippet': 'Macy’s announcement closely follows that of Walmart, which said it would buy Jet.com in what is widely viewed as a way to invigorate its online sales.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The great American consumer is very much alive. It’s just that people aren’t shopping like they used to, reluctant to pay full price or even leave the couch — cutting deep into the business of many top retailers.', 'print_sect