lian Murphy and Jamie Dornan, share impressions from the set.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The film’s director, Sean Ellis, and stars, Cillian Murphy and Jamie Dornan, share impressions from the set.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1357, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8/11tmag-anthropoid-slide-Z4Q8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind-the-Scenes Shots from the Set of ‘Anthropoid’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T14:58:01+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/0ca0bc24-6753-58a8-8991-f6b23aa08db0', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/0ca0bc24-6753-58a8-8991-f6b23aa08db0'}, {'abstract': 'The fashion-photographer-turned-director Sean Ellis shares beautiful photos from the set of “Anthropoid.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/t-magazine/entertainment/sean-ellis-anthropoid-film.html', 'snippet': 'The fashion-photographer-turned-director Sean Ellis shares beautiful photos from the set of “Anthropoid.”', 'lead_paragraph': '“I just don’t think period dramas work very well when they’re shot on the waxy, clean, sort of digital format,” says Sean Ellis, the director, co-writer and cinematographer of the new World War II thriller “Anthropoid.” “There’s too much detail, and it doesn’t feel real to me. Film is a little bit more forgiving and has a little bit more soul in it; there’s something beautiful in the grain.” Few would know better. As a fashion photographer, Ellis has shot for some of the world’s biggest brands and publications — among them Vogue, French Vogue and i-D — projects he prefers to capture the old-fashioned way. Ellis got his start with photography early on, after realizing the images in his head weren’t making it to paper when he tried to draw. “Something was lost in translation from my brain to my pen,” says Ellis. Instead, he photographed G.I. Joes, capturing imagined combat with the family camera.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Behind the Scenes of the Season’s Most Stylish Thriller', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On Screen; He Doesn’t Go Against the Grain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dornan, Jamie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ellis, Sean', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Cillian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Anthropoid (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T14:58:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Entertainment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nathan Reese', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reese', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffc94024-9d31-5d8f-a814-8693b6ad2866', 'word_count': 419, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffc94024-9d31-5d8f-a814-8693b6ad2866'}, {'abstract': 'Once our most intensive interventions end, we are left with this — a choice of tuna fish or chicken salad, or maybe some Oreos, brought up from the hospital basement.', 'web_url': 'https://well.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/when-a-patient-is-dying-food-appears/', 'snippet': 'Once our most intensive interventions end, we are left with this — a choice of tuna fish or chicken salad, or maybe some Oreos, brought up from the hospital basement.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When someone is dying in the intensive care unit, a tray of food appears. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/science/Oreos/Oreos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/11/science/Oreo