th his unauthorized ascent of the Fifth Avenue building.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In a city full of marquee buildings and landmarks under constant watch, it is just one among many. But as the primary residence of the Republican nominee in the midst of a heated presidential campaign, Trump Tower holds a particularly high-profile perch.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Tower Climber Now Faces Charges', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Tower Takes Center Stage Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rosenberg, Eli', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rogata, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stunts and Stuntmen', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Midtown Area (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Fifth Avenue (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T15:50:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eli Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eli', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/93db936f-3ee6-5d3d-9786-2bdf22b3d196', 'word_count': 918, 'uri': 'nyt://article/93db936f-3ee6-5d3d-9786-2bdf22b3d196'}, {'abstract': 'Aurélie Dupont, the new director of dance at the Paris Opera, shares her secrets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/t-magazine/fashion/aurelie-dupont-wellness-beauty-french-ballet.html', 'snippet': 'Aurélie Dupont, the new director of dance at the Paris Opera, shares her secrets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Earlier this month, Aurélie Dupont took over for Benjamin Millepied as director of dance at the Paris Opera — making her, in an industry that is still surprisingly male-dominated, one of the few women in the world directing a ballet company. Her credentials are impeccable: She’s a former étoile ballerina and was one of the most sought-after dancers in the world until ending her performance career in May 2015. As a dancer, Dupont called the Paris Opera home for 32 years — and with a 350-year-old legacy that makes it the oldest of its kind, the company is where ballet was born. But Dupont argues that in no way does this prevent it from remaining relevant to contemporary audiences. “Classical dance is an extraordinarily precise and physical art form,” she says. “It’s like a Chanel handbag — it endures through the generations. The old steps of ‘Swan Lake’ can be danced in ways which make them new. Just like your grandmother’s Chanel can be worn with sneakers in order to keep it modern.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/10/t-magazine/10tmag-aureliedupont01/10tmag-aureliedupont01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Wellness, Beauty and Style — According to a French Ballet Star', 'kicker': 'On Wellness', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ballet Beauty Tips', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Palais Garnier', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Paris Opera', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dupont, Aurelie (1973- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Paris (France)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T15:50:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Madison Mainwaring', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Madison', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mainwaring', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/94255d16-b78a-5570-93da-0e68dbaefc08', 'word_count': 855, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94255d16-b78a-5570-93da-0e68dbaefc08'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Italy’s army takes the Doberdo plateau in August 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/11/1916-italians-take-doberdo-plateau/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Italy’s army takes the Doberdo plateau in August 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN, Germany — Following the capture of Gorizia and the rout of the Austrian army driven beyond the town, the Italians have scored another magnificent triumph by hurling back the enemy from the area extending from south of Gorizia almost to the sea. The towns of Rubbia and San Martino and the whole of the Doberdo plateau are in the possession of the Italians, and their cavalry has at places driven back the enemy’s troops in disorder as far as the Vippacco torrent. The Austrians driven beyond Gorizia are in more or less complete rout over an 18-kilometre front. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 12, 1891', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/blogs/12oldiht-1916-doberdo/12oldiht-1916-doberdo-articleLarge-v2.png', 'height': 680, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/12/blogs/12oldiht-1916-doberdo/12oldiht-1916-doberdo-articleLarge-v2.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 680}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/blogs/12oldiht-1916-doberdo/12oldiht-1916-doberdo-jumbo-v2.png', 'height': 727, 'width': 641, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/