8.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/us/politics/donald-trump-obama-isis.html', 'snippet': 'The Republican nominee said that he intended to stick with his unorthodox campaign style, even if it meant taking “a very, very nice long vacation” after Nov. 8.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Facing one of the toughest stretches of his presidential campaign, Donald J. Trump on Thursday acknowledged in unusually candid terms that he faced daunting hurdles in crucial states, as he swung wildly at Hillary Clinton to try to blunt her questions about his fitness to serve in the Oval Office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Laments Sliding Polls While Maintaining His Provocative Approach', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Laments Sliding Polls While Maintaining His Provocative Approach', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haberman, Maggie', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T15:57:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Haberman and Nick Corasaniti', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}