bject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dichter Pharmacy (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'BoConcept', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budgets and Budgeting', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T20:12:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Laura Collins-Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laura', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins-Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/747acb26-d2d3-52c0-a745-5bf14774d1f1', 'word_count': 619, 'uri': 'nyt://article/747acb26-d2d3-52c0-a745-5bf14774d1f1'}, {'abstract': 'The year-old brand Alumnae, from a Sigerson Morrison founder, offers a host of loafers and slippers in luxe materials.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/t-magazine/fashion/fall-shoes-boots-alumnae.html', 'snippet': 'The year-old brand Alumnae, from a Sigerson Morrison founder, offers a host of loafers and slippers in luxe materials.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The designer Kari Sigerson is more than just a flat enthusiast; rather, she calls herself a “student of the flat.” In 1991, she launched the brand Sigerson Morrison along with co-designer Miranda Morrison. Now she’s teamed up with Eliza Axelson-Chidsey, another colleague from the label, to found Alumnae, a shoe brand that launched last year. “It’s a celebration of both my and Kari’s wealth of experience designing shoes,” Axelson-Chidsey says of Alumnae. “It’s not an of-the-moment, disruptive type of start-up. Its emphasis is really crafting well-made, wearable footwear” — something not the norm in an industry that has for years been dominated by men fashioning high heels for what the designers call “fantasy women.” “The difference with Alumnae, and of course, Sigerson Morrison, is that we as women can come in and correct our own prototypes on our own feet. We know what we desire and can make it ourselves,” Sigerson says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/t-magazine/11tmag-Alumnae-02/11tmag-Alumnae-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Shoe Line That Finds Creativity in Flats', 'kicker': 'Feeling For', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'se