, '_id': 'nyt://article/c5c72295-59ef-5e12-95b1-2f5a445bb359', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5c72295-59ef-5e12-95b1-2f5a445bb359'}, {'abstract': 'John H. Lee’s drama concerns a squad of South Koreans who infiltrate North Korean forces and secure a lighthouse critical to the Battle of Inchon.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/movies/operation-chromite-review.html', 'snippet': 'John H. Lee’s drama concerns a squad of South Koreans who infiltrate North Korean forces and secure a lighthouse critical to the Battle of Inchon.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The last time there was a major movie about one of the turning points of the Korean War, it was 1982 and “Inchon” was making history, of a sort. Financed by the Rev. Sun Myung Moon to the tune of $45 million but bringing in $5 million, that spectacular flop was the first to sweep the big four categories at the Razzie Awards: worst picture, worst director, worst screenplay and worst actor — Laurence Olivier in a latex-enhanced chin, playing Gen. Douglas MacArthur.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12OPCHROMITE/12OPCHROMITE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1200, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Operation Chromite’ Revisits a Korean War Invasion', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Operation Chromite (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lee, John H', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Neeson, Liam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-11T22:28:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daniel M. Gold', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daniel', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/e18bb0d6-7dfd-55d1-9146-14e295870243', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e18bb0d6-7dfd-55d1-9146-14e295870243'}, {'abstract': 'Cillian Murphy and Jamie Dornan star as Resistance fighters in Czechoslovakia who set out to assassinate one of the chief architects of the Holocaust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/movies/anthropoid-review.html', 'snippet': 'Cillian Murphy and Jamie Dornan star as Resistance fighters in Czechoslovakia who set out to assassinate one of the chief architects of the Holocaust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It takes Sean Ellis’s World War II thriller “Anthropoid” a while to build steam, but once it does, hang on. An account of the true Czech-British mission to assassinate Reinhard Heydrich — the principal architect of the Final Solution, and often called the Butcher of Prague — the film follows Jozef Gabcik (Cillian Murphy) and Jan Kubis (Jamie Dornan), who parachute into Nazi-occupied territory near Prague in December 1941. They soon learn how untrustworthy certain locals can be. But a connection is made with an underground contact (Toby Jones) who aids their endeavor, as well as a Resistance leader (Marcin Dorocinski) who fears devastating reprisals if the goal is met.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANTHROPOID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANTHROPOID-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANTHROPOID-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANTHROPOID-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANTHROPOID-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/arts/12ANTHROPOID/12ANT