rative about the forces that unraveled the Arab world, and clocks in at 40,000 words.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/12/public-editor/why-d-you-do-that-jake-silverstein-fractured-lands-middle-east.html', 'snippet': 'This Sunday’s New York Times Magazine is dedicated to a single narrative about the forces that unraveled the Arab world, and clocks in at 40,000 words.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Sunday’s New York Times print magazine will be unlike any ever published. It has been completely turned over to a single narrative by Scott Anderson about the forces that unraveled the Arab world since the United States invaded Iraq 13 years ago. It is written by Scott Anderson with photography by Paolo Pellegrin, and clocking in at 40,000 words, it’s less like a magazine piece and more like a small book. (The crossword puzzle is the only survivor among the magazine’s normal features.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why’d You Do That? Magazine Editor Jake Silverstein on a History-Making Issue', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Virtual Reality (Computers)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silverstein, Jake (1975- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Falluja (Iraq)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-12T12:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c82f08ce-db7f-59ab-a9d6-73c158068fca', 'word_count': 596, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c82f08ce-db7f-59ab-a9d6-73c158068fca'}, {'abstract': 'The state updated a law in a bid to attract more women and girls to a sport dominated by men.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/13/nyregion/hunting-in-pink-new-york-adds-another-color-for-safety.html', 'snippet': 'The state updated a law in a bid to attract more women and girls to a sport dominated by men.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pink is the new orange for young hunters in New York, who can now wear the color for safety under an updated law that advocates said was meant to attract more women and girls to a sport dominated by men.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/nyregion/00xp-pink_web1/00xp-pink_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/11/nyregion/00xp-pink_web1/00xp-pink_web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/nyregion/00xp-pink_web1/00xp-pink_web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/nyregion/00xp-pink_web1/00xp-pink_web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 673, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/11/nyregion/00xp-pink_web1/00xp-pink_web1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', '