', 'lead_paragraph': 'Olivier Blanchard has a characteristically informed, lucid essay on the role of DSGE models in macroeconomics, in which he accurately describes the problems with these models but – again characteristically – tries to make peace with both sides, calling for reform of this dominant paradigm rather than tossing the whole thing. I understand his motivations. But what strikes me is just how sad a portrait he offers of the state of macroeconomic theory.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The State of Macro Is Sad (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-12T14:09:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/852aef8c-8e23-5b39-8aee-c40f176d9344', 'word_count': 581, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852aef8c-8e23-5b39-8aee-c40f176d9344'}, {'abstract': 'A lavish municipal property bearing a presidential candidate’s name yields little for the Bronx residents who live nearby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/nyregion/golf-course-deal-with-donald-trump-leaves-new-york-city-in-the-rough.html', 'snippet': 'A lavish municipal property bearing a presidential candidate’s name yields little for the Bronx residents who live nearby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last summer, when Donald J. Trump’s presidential bid still seemed like a protracted April Fool’s joke, a lavish municipal golf course bearing his name — Trump Golf Links at Ferry Point — had just opened in New York City. This was many unhinged remarks ago, back in the early-morning hours of all the rancor, when he was condemning Mexicans as rapists and drug dealers best kept out of the country he hoped to govern, or as others would come to view it, tyrannize. Do you remember when you thought it would all end there? Even then, before the Trump candidacy had attained the fervor it would eventually acquire, there was reason to speculate whether his political volatility would imperil his business interests, and what it would mean for the city’s partnership with him if it did.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/nyregion/14BIGCITY1/14BIGCITY1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1438, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'c