yt://article/d8c0f3af-5a74-56e2-be1c-9a32be6fe0c8', 'word_count': 1472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8c0f3af-5a74-56e2-be1c-9a32be6fe0c8'}, {'abstract': 'Water-quality issues; leaving a unit broom-clean; and possible tenant harassment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/14/realestate/brown-water-in-a-rental.html', 'snippet': 'Water-quality issues; leaving a unit broom-clean; and possible tenant harassment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I live in a rent-stabilized apartment in a building that opened in 2009. Since October, brown water has occasionally come out of the kitchen faucet. Since March, it has happened every other day. Initially, management ignored my requests to fix the problem, even questioning the validity of my concerns. I sent them date-stamped pictures of the brown water and saved a water sample. They finally agreed to buy a water-filtration system, but are charging me to install it. Can they legally charge me for installation? And am I entitled to a rent abatement?', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/realestate/14ask/14ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 458, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/14/realestate/14ask/14ask-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 458}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/realestate/14ask/14ask-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 782, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/realestate/14ask/14ask-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1964, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'imag