s critical as that of Germany and Austria-Hungary. According to information from various reliable sources bread is everywhere extremely scarce. In Sofia, white bread is unobtainable and black bread is given out sparingly. In some parts of the country only two pounds a week is allowed to each householder. Sugar, butter, eggs and salt are among the necessaries sold at exorbitant prices, and even then only in very small quantities.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 408, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 408}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 800, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/blogs/15oldiht-1916-bulgaria/