e and play.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/12/nyregion/12BARGES1/12BARGES1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Plan to Let Barges Park on the Hudson Meets Resistance in ‘River Towns’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plan to Let Barges Park on the Hudson Draws Ire From ‘River Towns’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Foderaro, Lisa W', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hudson River', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Maritime Assn of the Port of New York and New Jersey', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yonkers (NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dobbs Ferry (NY)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hastings-on-Hudson (NY)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United States Coast Guard', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:41:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa W. Foderaro', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Foderaro', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a3971935-6efb-5739-969d-e764fbbfdd6f', 'word_count': 1252, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a3971935-6efb-5739-969d-e764fbbfdd6f'}, {'abstract': 'Doughnuts are a hot commodity at Grindstone Coffee in Sag Harbor, N.Y.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/grindstone-coffee-donuts-sag-harbor.html', 'snippet': 'Doughnuts are a hot commodity at Grindstone Coffee in Sag Harbor, N.Y.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kyle Shanahan lives in Sag Harbor, N.Y., where he thought there was a shortage of coffee shops like the ones he recalled in his native Cleveland. “And nothing goes better with coffee than doughnuts,” he said. So he has opened his own coffee and doughnut shop, with help from his stepfather, the chef Michael Symon. Mr. Shanahan’s doughnuts are yeasted, but made from brioche dough, so they have a denser, more caky consistency than most. Each day he produces four classics and four special doughnuts, like one gleaming with chocolate glaze and a popcorn topping and another with lemon-poppy seed icing. The honey-glazed variety, one of his classics, is my favorite. He makes 1,300 on weekdays, 2,200 on weekends, and when they’re gone, they’re gone: Grindstone Coffee and Donuts, 7A Main Street (Bay Street), Sag Harbor, N.Y., 631-808-3370, grindstonecoffeeanddonuts.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB/17BURNER-DONUTS-WEB-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When They’re Gone, They’re Gone', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Indulge: Cleveland Doughnuts  Reach Long Island', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grindstone Coffee and Donuts (Sag Harbor, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coffeehouses', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doughnuts', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sag Harbor (NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:46:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7081d670-64da-54c3-80f3-78ff23f73f55', 'word_count': 139, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7081d670-64da-54c3-80f3-78ff23f73f55'}, {'abstract': 'Some 90 years after they were developed, Bronx seedless table grapes have arrived in New York.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/bronx-seedless-grapes.html', 'snippet': 'Some 90 years after they were developed, Bronx seedless table grapes have arrived in New York.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bronx grapes have arrived. Some 90 years after the Cornell Agricultural Experiment Station in Geneva, N.Y., and the New York Botanical Garden developed the Bronx Seedless table grape, Lagier Ranches in Escalon, Calif., has enough of a crop of these lovely translucent pale green-to-pink grapes (with thin skins and a lush, almost candied flavor) to ship them to New York. The organic grapes have been sold on a limited basis in Northern California, but the grape never grew well in the Northeast. They will be available for about three weeks: Bronx Seedless Table Grapes from Lagier Ranches, $6.99 for a one-pound box at Agata & Valentina and Eataly stores.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB3/17BURNER-GRAPES-WEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Give Them the Old Bronx Grape', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Nibble: Bronx Grapes Arrive  From California', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grapes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cornell University Agricultural Experiment Station', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bronx (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:47:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e4bee6bb-45dc-52e0-b0a9-b668b0af9627', 'word_count': 109, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e4bee6bb-45dc-52e0-b0a9-b668b0af9627'}, {'abstract': '“Preserving Italy” is a new cookbook that shows how to savor summer’s bounty the Italian way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/preserving-italy-book-domenica-marchetti.html', 'snippet': '“Preserving Italy” is a new cookbook that shows how to savor summer’s bounty the Italian way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In summer, books about canning and preserving are as common as apple cookbooks in the fall. But Domenica Marchetti’s book caught my eye for its uncommon point of view: preserving food the Italian way. Pack artichokes, peppers and mushrooms in oil. Make deliciously spicy pickles from melon. Even limoncello, mostarda and confections like torrone can come straight from your kitchen. There are simple cheeses and cured meats, along with a useful section covering tomatoes, but the option of freezing for preservation is not included. At the end of each chapter are some easy recipes for using your homemade creations. It’s a cautious book that stresses safety over shortcuts. The techniques may have been passed down by generations of nonnas, but they knew what they were doing: “Preserving Italy” by Domenica Marchetti (Houghton Mifflin Harcourt, $23).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 723, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 723}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 851, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 1095, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1/17BURNER-COOKBOOK-WEB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Canned Tomatoes and So Much More', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Consult: Making Preserves, Italian Style', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Italy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Preserving Italy (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marchetti, Domenica', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:48:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c843865-5123-5017-bdf7-9a03dd446e5c', 'word_count': 135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c843865-5123-5017-bdf7-9a03dd446e5c'}, {'abstract': 'Many jails in the South lack air-conditioning. To plenty of prisoners, and some federal judges, that effectively amounts to cruel and unusual punishment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/us/in-us-jails-a-constitutional-clash-over-air-conditioning.html', 'snippet': 'Many jails in the South lack air-conditioning. To plenty of prisoners, and some federal judges, that effectively amounts to cruel and unusual punishment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JENNINGS, La. — The air inside the Jefferson Davis Parish jail was hot and musty. Prisoners, often awakened by the morning heat, hoped for cooling rain after nightfall. And ice, one inmate recalled, brought fleeting relief in the cell she called a “sweatbox.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16