: 'Eighth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:55:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c844fed0-0955-5277-a5d8-f8bcef6de43d', 'word_count': 1294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c844fed0-0955-5277-a5d8-f8bcef6de43d'}, {'abstract': 'When you hear complaints about too much regulation, don’t forget to ask what harm that regulation may prevent.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/business/dealbook/the-risks-of-unfettered-capitalism.html', 'snippet': 'When you hear complaints about too much regulation, don’t forget to ask what harm that regulation may prevent.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Capitalism may be the best economic system ever devised, but one of its drawbacks is that it provides financial incentives to harm and even kill people. Just ask those people who say they have been victimized by cigarettes, predatory lenders, Volkswagen diesel emissions, Takata airbags, General Motors ignition switches, Trump University, Vioxx, asbestos or other products.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Risks of Unfettered Capitalism', 'kicker': 'Another View', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:58:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Sovern', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sovern', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eadaf04-233e-5dda-a15d-a3325ae9b779', 'word_count': 717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eadaf04-233e-5dda-a15d-a3325ae9b779'}, {'abstract': 'A new pink gin adds a blush to summer martinis.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/pink-gin-lane-1751.html', 'snippet': 'A new pink gin adds a blush to summer martinis.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This season of rosé now includes a gin. Pink gin, a Victorian-era throwback said to have been first concocted by the Royal Navy, achieves its pale salmon color from the botanicals and bitters used to mellow the spirit’s strong juniper profile. This English gin, made in pot stills in small batches, gets its name from the Gin Act of 1751, legislation designed to restrict the sale of “demon” gin to the poor. Consider it for a blushing martini or gimlet, or simply serve it on the rocks with a spritz of lime and just a splash of good tonic: Gin Lane 1751 “Victoria” Pink Gin, $27.99 from ginlane1751.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1170, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1170}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 526, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2/17BURNER-GIN-WEB2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1051, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rosé All Day, but at Night, Grab the Gin', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: Pink Gin Adds Blush to Martinis', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gin (Liquor)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gin Lane 1751', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T15:58:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ac7a135-e174-5ac5-b878-501b3ca0146f', 'word_count': 108, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ac7a135-e174-5ac5-b878-501b3ca0146f'}, {'abstract': 'Reflections on world-class performance by two Olympic gold medalists, along with a numeric challenge by the math educator Sunil Singh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/15/crosswords/olympic-strategies-part-2.html', 'snippet': 'Reflections on world-class performance by two Olympic gold medalists, along with a numeric challenge by the math educator Sunil Singh.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Great spirits have always encountered violent opposition from mediocre minds,” wrote Albert Einstein in 1940. The expression is a terrible cliché at this point, but it’s always intrigued me. What does “violent opposition” look like? Are only mediocre minds susceptible? And how do these great spirits respond?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/15/crosswords/wordplaybackstroke/wordplaybackstroke-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1349, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Numberplay: Olympic Strategies, Part 2', 'kicker': 'Numberplay', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (1988)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Council of Teachers of Mathematics', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Einstein, Albert', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sam Vandervelde', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sunil Singh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Puzzles', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mathematics', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T16:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Games', 'section_name': 'Crosswords & Games', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gary Antonick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gary', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Antonick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a413996-a7be-5e30-9a7b-07156b6b6daf', 'word_count': 1061, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a413996-a7be-5e30-9a7b-07156b6b6daf'}, {'abstract': 'Fresh chocolate mousse in white or dark chocolate now available in the dairy case.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/fresh-chocolate-mousse.html', 'snippet': 'Fresh chocolate mousse in white or dark chocolate now available in the dairy case.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There has to be a chocolate mousse that’s fresh, not frozen,” said Johan Halsberghe, who was the chef for the Belgian ambassador in New York. So he decided to do something about it. He uses organic Belgian chocolate for his white- and dark-chocolate mousses, made in Brooklyn and sold fresh in food shops. The dark variety is light-textured and creamy with an excellent balance of bitter and sweet. The white chocolate version, made with gelatin, is a trifle spongier in texture, but also not too sweet. Both are sold in small plastic containers. The mousses can be unmolded for more elegant service by running a knife around the inside of the cup and inverting it with a bit of force onto a plate: Johan Fresh Chocolate Mousse, dark, 2.47 ounces; white, 2.82 ounces, each $3.99 at Brooklyn Fare, 431 West 37th Street, 212-216-9700, brooklynfare.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 386, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 386}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 659, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1045, 'width': 1625, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/dining/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4/17BURNER-MOUSSE-WEB4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Belgian Chocolate in a Pudding Cup', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Spoon: Belgian Chocolate in a Pudding Cup', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Brooklyn Fare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T16:01:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d9d6763-bfb3-5a3c-af84-04ae0ebddfd1', 'word_count': 144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d9d6763-bfb3-5a3c-af84-04ae0ebddfd1'}, {'abstract': 'Airbnb has teamed up with corporate travel management companies and introduced new rules and services to appeal to business travelers and their bosses.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/business/airbnb-for-business-travelers-more-wi-fi-fewer-hosts-in-towels.html', 'snippet': 'Airbnb has teamed up with corporate travel management companies and introduced new rules and services to appeal to business travelers and their bosses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether traveling for business or pleasure, Tad Milbourn, chief executive of the San Francisco technology start-up Payable, stays at an Airbnb property whenever possible.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/business/16ITINERARIES-sub1/16ITINERARIES-sub1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airbnb for Business Travelers: More Wi-Fi, Fewer Hosts in Towels', 'kicker': 'Itineraries', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Traveling for Business, and Staying in an Airbnb', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Business Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Levere, Jane L', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'HomeAway Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T16:01:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jane L. Levere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jane', 'middlename': 'L.', 'lastname': 'Levere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4a3bf299-03eb-5c59-950e-b90cdf36c2cb', 'word_count': 1216, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4a3bf299-03eb-5c59-950e-b90cdf36c2cb'}, {'abstract': 'Eric Ripert recounts his early career at a talk at the Museum of Food and Drink.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/dining/eric-ripert-mofad-talk.html', 'snippet': 'Eric Ripert recounts his early career at a talk at the Museum of Food and Drink.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chef Eric Ripert will discuss his childhood in the south of France and his early years working in Paris as recounted in his new memoir, “32 Yolks: From My Mother’s Table to Working the Line,” at the Museum of Food and Drink. Signed copies of the book will be sold afterward: “32 Yolks, a Conversation With Eric Ripert,” Aug. 30, 6:30 to 8 p.m., $35, Museum of Food and Drink, 62 Bayard Street (Lorimer Street), Williamsburg, Brooklyn, mofad.org.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty