rs', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/88bb3b36-4ba2-5719-ac83-9857e0f720bb', 'word_count': 739, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88bb3b36-4ba2-5719-ac83-9857e0f720bb'}, {'abstract': 'Journalists have nothing to fear from my campaign against the website.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/opinion/peter-thiel-the-online-privacy-debate-wont-end-with-gawker.html', 'snippet': 'Journalists have nothing to fear from my campaign against the website.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, I spoke at the Republican National Convention in Cleveland because I believe our country is on the wrong track, and we need to solve real problems instead of fighting fake culture wars. I’m glad that an arena full of Republicans stood up to applaud when I said I was proud to be gay, because gay pride shouldn’t be a partisan issue. All people deserve respect, and nobody’s sexuality should be made a public fixation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16Thiel2-web/16Thiel2-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Thiel: The Online Privacy Debate Won’t End With Gawker', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Privacy Issues Won’t End With Gawker', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thiel, Peter A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gawker.com', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hogan, Hulk', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T19:53:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Thiel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Thiel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/94711c7f-2ebb-5ace-b4f1-0227b870fa28', 'word_count': 939, 'uri': 'nyt://article/94711c7f-2ebb-5ace-b4f1-0227b870fa28'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Shine, a loyal right-hand man to Roger Ailes, was little known outside the TV industry before Mr. Ailes’s abrupt departure and his promotion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/business/media/bill-shine-steps-out-from-behind-the-scenes-to-lead-fox-news.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Shine, a loyal right-hand man to Roger Ailes, was little known outside the TV industry before Mr. Ailes’s abrupt departure and his promotion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bill Shine, the newly appointed co-president of Fox News, commutes two hours every morning from Long Island to Midtown Manhattan, leaving his house so early that, as he tells colleagues, “the other guys on the train all have Sheetrock on their boots.”', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 778, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 778}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/business/16SHINE1/16SHINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 919, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16