paragraph': 'Lyft, the No. 2 American ride-hailing service, recently rebuffed takeover interest from General Motors, its 9 percent owner, according to the news service The Information. There are reasons for Lyft to steer clear of Detroit, despite a shared vision for autonomous cars. But cash-flush rivals could still force the Silicon Valley start-up into G.M.’s lane.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lyft Declined G.M. Takeover Effort, but Rivals Could Force Its Hand', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driverless and Semiautonomous Vehicles', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobiles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lyft Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'General Motors', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quattrone, Frank P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T20:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5a524c03-a550-5516-bacd-f796e9247dcf', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5a524c03-a550-5516-bacd-f796e9247dcf'}, {'abstract': 'The revelation that $12.7 million in cash payments from a pro-Russian political party were earmarked for Mr. Manafort provided yet another distraction to the campaign.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/us/politics/trump-campaign-paul-manafort-ukraine-cash-payments-russia.html', 'snippet': 'The revelation that $12.7 million in cash payments from a pro-Russian political party were earmarked for Mr. Manafort provided yet another distraction to the campaign.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Trump campaign was on the defensive on Monday after a New York Times report revealed that its chairman, Paul Manafort, was designated to receive $12.7 million in undisclosed and potentially illegal cash payments from a pro-Russian political party in Ukraine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1251, 'width': 1877, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/16fd-manafortreax/16fd-manafortreax-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Campaign and Its Chief, Paul Manafort, Try to Move Past Ukraine Report', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Campaign Tries to Steer Past Ukraine Link Report', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manafort, Paul J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ukraine', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Russia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lewandowski, Corey (1975- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T20:15:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Rappeport', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rappeport', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9cb0705a-8b7f-5d6a-8a5d-61844dd75cba', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9cb0705a-8b7f-5d6a-8a5d-61844dd75cba'}, {'abstract': 'Should we not call out lies, lest a bigger liar come along?', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/15/lies-lying-liars-and-donald-trump/', 'snippet': 'Should we not call out lies, lest a bigger liar come along?', 'lead_paragraph': 'So, there’s a new conservative take on who’s to blame for Donald Trump — and the answer, it turns out, is liberal commentators, and me in particular. Yep, by denouncing the dishonesty of people like Mitt Romney, I was crying wolf, so that voters paid no attention to warnings about Trump.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Lies, Lying Liars, and Donald Trump', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T20:26:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/372141bd-d280-52d1-96fb-6aa23437e951', 'word_count': 417, 'uri': 'nyt://article/372141bd-d280-52d1-96fb-6aa23437e951'}, {'abstract': 'Larry Tye’s biography goes beyond the “bad Bobby” and “good Bobby” approach in exploring how a hard-nosed politician came to tilt against social injustice.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/books/from-bare-knuckles-to-idealism-in-bobby-kennedy-the-making-of-a-liberal-icon.html', 'snippet': 'Larry Tye’s biography goes beyond the “bad Bobby” and “good Bobby” approach in exploring how a hard-nosed politician came to tilt against social injustice.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Reading about the life and death of Robert F. Kennedy, the reader can’t help but be reminded of the striking parallels between the late 1960s and today — polarized politics, racial tensions and growing social anxiety and tumult. It’s also impossible not to think about the vast gulf between the idealistic hopes Kennedy inspired among his young followers, and the fear and cynicism that have marked this year’s presidential campaign.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 788}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 781, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1268, 'width': 966, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/arts/16BOOKTYE/16BOOKTYE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'From Bare Knuckles to Idealism in ‘Bobby Kennedy: The Making of a Liberal Icon’', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Pragmatist Converting to Idealism', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bobby Kennedy: The Making of a Liberal Icon (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tye, Larry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Robert Francis', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-15T20:29:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/6eac87b5-b75b-5607-a817-9d22abfa7d07', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6eac87b5-b75b-5607-a817-9d22abfa7d07'}, {'abstract': 'Officials said there was no evidence that a report of gunfire at J.F.K. on Sunday night was a deliberate hoax. What followed, they said, was a sign of the times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/nyregion/from-false-alarm-to-panic-inside-kennedy-airports-chaotic-night.html', 'snippet': 'Officials said there was no evidence that a report of gunfire at J.F.K. on Sunday night was a deliberate hoax. What followed, they said, was a sign of the times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jennifer Rosen was scheduled to depart Kennedy International Airport on an 8:55 p.m. flight to San Francisco but instead found herself stuck at Gate C62 in Terminal 2. It was the typical misery of summer airline travel — or so it seemed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/nyregion/16JFK1/16JFK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/nyregion/16JFK1/16JFK1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/nyregion/16JFK1/16JFK1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/nyregion/16JFK1/16JFK1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'wid