 and using human odor as bait cut mosquito populations by 70 percent on a malaria-ridden island in Kenya.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A new type of mosquito trap running on solar electricity and using human odor as bait has cut mosquito populations by 70 percent in a test on a malaria-ridden island in Kenya, according to a new study.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1067, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1067}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 577, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1153, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/science/16GLOBAL/16GLOBAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Better (Smelly) Mosquito Trap, but With Caveats', 'kicker': 'Global Health', 'c