s with the promise that “all the things you love to do are more expressive, more dynamic and more fun than ever.” That especially includes emojis, those little icons that, according to one study, 92 percent of the online population now make part of their everyday communication.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 912, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 912}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 674, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/opinion/16zittrain/16zittrain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1510, 'width': 993, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Apple’s Emoji Gun Control', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Apple’s Emoji Gun Control', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zittrain, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emojis and Emoticons', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Apple Inc', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Speech and Expression', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-16T07:21:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Zittrain', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zittrain', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/189d949f-d080-5c55-9dcb-7106b635f72a', 'word_count': 900, 'uri': 'nyt://article/189d949f-d080-5c55-9dcb-7106b635f72a'}, {'abstract': 'Passage of state legislation would provide a national model for promoting retirement savings.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/opinion/from-california-a-better-way-to-retire.html', 'snippet': 'Passage of state legislation would provide a national model for promoting retirement savings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At any given moment, about half of the private-sector employees in the United States — some 60 million people — do not have any type of employer-sponsored retirement plan. The result is a growing American underclass, in which a third of current retirees live almost entirely on Social Security and fully half of future retirees will face reduced standards of living. Worse, the coverage gap has long proved intractable, with Congress and the financial industry unable or unwilling to design or support truly simple and low-cost retirement savings plans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'pr