riginal': 'By Donovan Hohn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Donovan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hohn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b4505de-0055-59c7-aa87-4cc1e9d779db', 'word_count': 6335, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b4505de-0055-59c7-aa87-4cc1e9d779db'}, {'abstract': 'Productions of “Jesus Christ Superstar,” “The Threepenny Opera,” “Show Boat” and “Guys and Dolls” are fun and fresh diversions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/theater/summertime-and-the-revivals-in-london-are-breezy.html', 'snippet': 'Productions of “Jesus Christ Superstar,” “The Threepenny Opera,” “Show Boat” and “Guys and Dolls” are fun and fresh diversions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — When you’re approaching a monumental landmark, it’s usually a good idea to leave the awe at home. That would seem to be the attitude of the creative teams behind four disarmingly relaxed and very enjoyable revivals of watershed musicals here this summer. They are shows that in their original incarnations caused such excitement that ever after they have inspired trepidation, agitation and extreme self-consciousness among those who revisit them.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21LONDONMUSICAL1/21LONDONMUSICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21LONDONMUSICAL1/21LONDONMUSICAL1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21LONDONMUSICAL1/21LONDONMUSICAL1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge',