dline': {'main': 'Summer Reading Contest Winner, Week 7 | On ‘In Hillary Clinton’s Nomination, Women See a Collective Step Up’', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-16T12:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Learning Network', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Learning Network'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/897d9cc3-0951-5170-a76d-78219f848dbd', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/897d9cc3-0951-5170-a76d-78219f848dbd'}, {'abstract': 'How did Hillary Clinton lose Americans’ trust? Stanley Greenberg, a top Democratic campaign strategist, describes how he addressed the trust issue for another Clinton: Bill. We also speak with Lissa CQ Muscatine, a longtime adviser for Hillary Clinton, and Mark Landler, a White House correspondent for The Times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/audio/2016/08/16/podcasts/16runup-trust.html', 'snippet': 'How did Hillary Clinton lose Americans’ trust? Stanley Greenberg, a top Democratic campaign strategist, describes how he addressed the trust issue for another Clinton: Bill. We also speak with Lissa CQ Muscatine, a longtime adviser for Hillary Cli...', 'lead_paragraph': 'How did Hillary Clinton lose Americans’ trust? Stanley Greenberg, a top Democratic campaign strategist, describes how he addressed the trust issue for another Clinton: Bill. We also speak with Lissa CQ Muscatine, a longtime adviser for Hillary Clinton, and Mark Landler, a White House correspondent for The Times.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why She’s Distrusted', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-16T12:04:25+0000', 'document_type': 'audio', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Podcasts', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/182fd7f0-eaa4-525e-88ea-eeed94b93a63', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/182fd7f0-eaa4-525e-88ea-eeed94b93a63'}, {'abstract': 'Has Hillary Clinton uttered untruths? Yes. But the perception that she is dishonest is about a confluence of mistakes, a marriage and partisanship.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/16/podcasts/hillary-clinton-trust.html', 'snippet': 'Has Hillary Clinton uttered untruths? Yes. But the perception that she is dishonest is about a confluence of mistakes, a marriage and partisanship.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A Clinton with a trust problem. We’ve seen that before. It was 1992, and doubts about Bill Clinton’s integrity, stoked by his marital infidelities and avoidance of the Vietnam War, were the biggest threat to his presidential campaign. Stanley Greenberg, a top Democratic campaign strategist, devised a secret plan to turn around the candidate’s reputation for dishonesty.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/17RUNUPweb1/17RUNUPweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/16/us/17RUNUPweb1/17RUNUPweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/17RUNUPweb1/17RUNUPweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/us/17RUNUPweb1/17RUNUPweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 354, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/us/17RUNUPweb1/17RUNUPweb1-a