ure in the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/world/asia/china-quantum-satellite-mozi.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers hope to beam transmissions from space to earth with quantum technology, a type of communication that could prove to be the most secure in the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BEIJING — China launched the world’s first quantum communications satellite from the Gobi Desert early Tuesday, a major step in the country’s bid to be at the forefront of quantum research, which could lead to new, completely secure methods of transmitting information.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'China Launches Quantum Satellite in Bid to Pioneer Secure Communications', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China Launches Satellite in Bid to Lead Quantum Research', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Satellites', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-16T16:10:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Edward Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Edward', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6f083580-d433-5f88-b4fb-41eab11d690b', 'word_count': 505, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6f083580-d433-5f88-b4fb-41eab11d690b'}, {'abstract': 'The bank is accelerating the sale of businesses it deems nonessential, hoping to return to growth — and higher dividends.', 