], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T04:01:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rachel Rabkin Peachman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rachel', 'middlename': 'Rabkin', 'lastname': 'Peachman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0fd28162-edcf-55ac-92c3-75ad292cd696', 'word_count': 559, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0fd28162-edcf-55ac-92c3-75ad292cd696'}, {'abstract': 'You know the actress from her films. The real Kristen Stewart — funny and fiercely open — is only just emerging. That took years of work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/t-magazine/entertainment/kristen-stewart-the-good-bad-girl.html', 'snippet': 'You know the actress from her films. The real Kristen Stewart — funny and fiercely open — is only just emerging. That took years of work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s hard to not be charmed by Kristen Stewart’s Los Feliz home, even harder to believe that it belongs to a movie star and not a college freshman. The basement den of her four-bedroom property, which hovers above Los Angeles — at once belonging to and separate from the hazy city below it — is a study in random: a stop sign on one wall, three metal letters — A, S and S — on another, a Batman action figure, a Winnie the Pooh-themed Pez dispenser, a Playboy pinball machine. The room’s centerpiece, an imposing bookcase, is packed with fashion tomes, a few to do with Chanel, for whom she models; monographs featuring the work of Basquiat, Eggleston and Mapplethorpe; books about food, travel and the Beatles; and novels by Dostoyevsky, Hesse and Kafka. A chunk of shelf is devoted to Jack Kerouac, whose character Marylou she played in a film version of “On the Road.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '237', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/t-magazine/17tmag-kstewpromo/17tmag-kstewpromo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Kristen Stewart, the Good Bad Girl', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Storm', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ACTORS AND ACTRESSES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stewart, Kristen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Cafe Society (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chanel SA', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Assayas, Olivier', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Personal Shopper (Movie)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T04:01:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Entertainment', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Haramis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haramis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f79e12c-d963-5aec-9628-f419f755d356', 'word_count': 1463, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f79e12c-d963-5aec-9628-f419f755d356'}, {'abstract': 'The Incroyables of 18th-century France used exquisitely malformed clothing to express outrage. So, too, are designers now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/t-magazine/fashion/fashion-as-protest-french-incroyables.html', 'snippet': 'The Incroyables of 18th-century France used exquisitely malformed clothing to express outrage. So, too, are designers now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the fall 2016 shows back in March, the fashion designer Rei Kawakubo presented a collection for her Comme des Garçons label that was an ode to the 18th century. Its shapes were grandly outsize: gargantuan balloons of brocade and jacquard malforming the body, hair \xadpiled high and frizzed. Anna Cleveland, daughter of Pat, strode with her unusual gait, toes pointed outward, nose pointed upward. “Eighteenth-\xadcentury punk” was Kawakubo’s stated inspiration. “The 18th century was a time of change and revolution,” she said. “This is how I imagine punks would look, if they had lived in this century.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '230', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna