0-5f4b-9d6c-60b0ba237481', 'word_count': 797, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66cbcfb7-2920-5f4b-9d6c-60b0ba237481'}, {'abstract': 'Extremists in Congress want to give away our federal lands.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/opinion/dont-give-away-our-wildlife-refuges.html', 'snippet': 'Extremists in Congress want to give away our federal lands.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tucked into the fiscal relief package for Puerto Rico this spring was a provision to give away a national treasure that belongs to all Americans — 3,100 acres of the Vieques National Wildlife Refuge. The proposal had nothing to do with the economic recovery of Puerto Rico. But it would have handed an important victory to extremists in Congress and state legislatures who want to grab national lands and turn them over to the states to be sold or leased.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 332, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 332}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 566, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17williams/17williams-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1132, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Don’t Give Away Our Wildlife Refuges', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Protect America’s Wildlife Refuges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildlife Sanctuaries and Nature Reserves', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Jamie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Puerto Rico', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wilderness Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Lands', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T07:21:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jamie Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jamie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c058b13b-a23b-5e30-a0a5-7a406585f989', 'word_count': 859, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c058b13b-a23b-5e30-a0a5-7a406585f989'}, {'abstract': 'Our cultural idealization of love could use a revision.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/opinion/love-labor-lost.html', 'snippet': 'Our cultural idealization of love could use a revision.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has not, by any measure, been a Summer of Love; more like a Summer of Anxiety, Fear and Hate. It would be facile to respond to recent events — political upheaval, mass murder, police violence and festering racism — with a call to “love.” But in extreme times, it’s worth considering: Can love (as we know it) act as a radical force rather than a distraction? Does our current idea of love need revision? Is there a new kind of love emerging in new social movements, one that works against the narrow kind of love fostered by capitalism? I discussed these and other matters with Moira Weigel, the author of “Labor of Love: The Invention of Dating.” — Natasha Lennard', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 533, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 533}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 909, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17stoneWEIGEL-web/17stoneWEIGEL-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1818, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Love. Labor. Lost.', 'kicker': 'The Stone', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reproduction (Biological)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T07:21:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natasha Lennard and Moira Weigel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natasha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lennard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Moira', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weigel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8052f6f1-29e4-5905-96e8-6fe50c7bbed3', 'word_count': 2329, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8052f6f1-29e4-5905-96e8-6fe50c7bbed3'}, {'abstract': 'Unions are strong, and they bring benefits that cocktail servers and hotel workers in other states can only dream of.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/opinion/how-unions-help-cocktail-servers.html', 'snippet': 'Unions are strong, and they bring benefits that cocktail servers and hotel workers in other states can only dream of.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Las Vegas — THIS summer I worked as a seasonal cocktail server, a job that came with a membership in the largest union local in Nevada, Culinary 226. In my first week on the job, I chatted with a co-worker in the elevator. I asked how long she had been working there. “Twenty-eight years,” she said. “And I just got my dream shift last week!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/opinion/17Bronson-web/17Bronson-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1291, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo