eling a devastating inland tropical deluge.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/17/how-an-inland-brown-ocean-and-climate-change-may-have-fueled-louisianas-deadly-flood/', 'snippet': 'Climate experts deconstruct the possible roles of global warming and Louisiana’s warm swampy landscapes in fueling a devastating inland tropical deluge.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As news media fixated on athletic achievements at the Rio Olympics, and of course remained fixated on Donald Trump, different corners of the United States were confronting weather-related hazards — including\xa0relentless steamy heat in the East\xa0and\xa0drought-fueled wildfires\xa0all around California, including the explosively spreading “Blue Cut” Fire east of Los Angeles. But nothing\xa0has come\xa0close to the deadly off-the-chart deluges and flooding in southern Louisiana, which the Red Cross\xa0says have produced the country’s\xa0worst\xa0natural disaster since Hurricane Sandy.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/blogs/dotlouisiananasa/dotlouisiananasa-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 442, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/16/blogs/dotlouisiananasa/dotlouisiananasa-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 442}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/blogs/dotlouisiananasa/dotlouisiananasa-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 755, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/16/blogs/dotlouisiananasa/dotlouisiananasa-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1099, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type':