2a8fc5f251f9'}, {'abstract': 'Thae Yong-ho is the most senior diplomat to flee the secretive nation since Jang Seung-gil, the envoy to Egypt, defected to the United States in 1997.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/world/asia/north-korea-defector-thae-yong-ho-britain.html', 'snippet': 'Thae Yong-ho is the most senior diplomat to flee the secretive nation since Jang Seung-gil, the envoy to Egypt, defected to the United States in 1997.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — He enjoyed a bit of tennis at the local club. He indulged in curry at an Indian restaurant in the west London neighborhood where he lived. As the No. 2 North Korean diplomat in Britain, he chaperoned a brother of his country’s reclusive leader to an Eric Clapton concert last year.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea’s No. 2 Diplomat in London Defects to the South', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'North Korean Diplomat, Who Embraced London, Defects', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Defectors (Political)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Korea', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thae Yong-ho', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diplomatic Service, Embassies and Consulates', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kim Jong-un', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T10:36:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Choe Sang-Hun and Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Choe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sang-Hun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e18fcb95-0297-5765-88c1-2f1cdc90a28d', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e18fcb95-0297-5765-88c1-2f1cdc90a28d'}, {'abstract': 'An exhibition in Monte Carlo includes 66 Bacon oil paintings and a dozen related works by Picasso, Soutine and others.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/arts/international/how-france-and-monaco-inspired-francis-bacon.html', 'snippet': 'An exhibition in Monte Carlo includes 66 Bacon oil paintings and a dozen related works by Picasso, Soutine and others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MONTE CARLO, Monaco — The glamorous Mediterranean principality of Monaco is not usually viewed as a cradle of pioneering modern art. Yet in the 1940s, the painter Francis Bacon spent three productive years here, developing his best-known pictorial theme: the screaming popes, inspired by a Velázquez portrait.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/18/arts/18iht-francisbacon18a/18iht-francisbacon18a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/18/arts/18iht-francisbacon18a/18iht-francisbacon18a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/18/arts/18iht-francisbacon18a/18iht-francisbacon18a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'c