405', 'word_count': 895, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d8291f6b-a612-5068-ba33-42fc5c050405'}, {'abstract': 'Why quibble when there’s clearly a dastardly villain in front of you? Just run.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-what-to-call-a-trench-coat.html', 'snippet': 'Why quibble when there’s clearly a dastardly villain in front of you? Just run.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Samantha writes: My boyfriend and I were on one of our evening walks, and we saw a man wearing a long black trench coat. I called it a “Matrix” coat, while my boyfriend insisted that it was a “vampire hunter” coat. Which is the correct cultural association to use upon seeing such a coat?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1023, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21hodgman/21mag-21hodgman-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1237, 'width': 1238, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge John Hodgman on What to Call a Trench Coat', 'kicker': 'Judge John Hodgman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bonus Advice From Judge John Hodgman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hodgman, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coats and Jackets', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Culture (Arts)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f64c65c-5fd1-5213-b5d4-6246ae5fa57e', 'word_count': 168, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f64c65c-5fd1-5213-b5d4-6246ae5fa57e'}, {'abstract': 'A heavily processed food that embodies our conquest of nature.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-cheddar-and-sour-cream-ruffles.html', 'snippet': 'A heavily processed food that embodies our conquest of nature.', 'lead_paragraph': 'About 12 years ago, my partner and I decided to wow our friends on Thanksgiving by ordering a heritage-breed turkey from a small farmer in Pennsylvania. For weeks we watched the turkey — our turkey — on the farmer’s webcam, a cluster of pixels frolicking inside a chicken-wire enclosure. It was butchered and shipped overnight (the FedEx shipping cost nearly as much as the bird) and when it emerged from the oven, mari\xadnated and basted decadently in butter, the turkey tasted so unspeakably bland that much of it was left on our friends’ plates, camouflaged awkwardly under brussels sprouts. The feel-good narrative of our lovingly raised, hormone-antibiotic-and-G.M.O.-free certified-organic turkey became supplanted with a more ambiguous one. We felt both duped and morally abject: Not only were we out nearly $200, but our ethical gambit put an end to the bird’s bucolic life.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21lor-copy/21mag-21lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Cheddar and Sour Cream Ruffles', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Cheddar and Sour Cream Ruffles', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Frito-Lay Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Potato Chips', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Snack Foods', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alex Halberstadt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alex', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Halberstadt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9b00a997-40ea-51b0-9dea-2532d24fe1c6', 'word_count': 850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9b00a997-40ea-51b0-9dea-2532d24fe1c6'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on telling a friend’s husband about her serial betrayals, sharing a dementia diagnosis with a sibling and whether it’s O.K. to ask a student to do free research.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/magazine/when-a-friend-cheats-often-on-her-husband-should-you-keep-quiet.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on telling a friend’s husband about her serial betrayals, sharing a dementia diagnosis with a sibling and whether it’s O.K. to ask a student to do free research.', 'lead_paragraph': 'More than two years ago, my best friend’s husband discovered that she was cheating on him with her business partner. They decided to work on their marriage and go to counseling, together and separately. I’ve had long conversations with my friend, and she confessed to me that she has slept with more than 10 other men while being married and even slept with an ex-\xadboyfriend while she was engaged. She has gone to addiction support groups; however, she’s still seeing and sleeping with the man she was caught cheating with, engaging in threesomes with him and sleeping with other men. She even brought him to my birthday party, where there were only a few friends celebrating (none of whom know her or her husband). ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21ethicist/21ethicist-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 520, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21ethicist/21ethicist-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 580, 'width': 520, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21ethicist/21ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21ethicist/21ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/magazine/21ethicist/21ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When a Friend Cheats Often on Her Husband, Should You Keep Quiet?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Friend Cheats on Her Husband — a Lot. Do I Keep Quiet?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Graduate Schools and Students', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lying', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Workplace Environment', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Internships', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c81468ab-1b34-57fe-9afa-eb5c8aa57084', 'word_count': 1365, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c81468ab-1b34-57fe-9afa-eb5c8aa57084'}, {'abstract': 'The social-bookmarking site enters the competition with Facebook, Twitter and others vying for a share of the increasing amounts marketers are spending on digital ads.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/business/media/pinterest-follows-rivals-into-selling-video-ads.html', 'snippet': 'The social-bookmarking site enters the competition with Facebook, Twitter and others vying for a share of the in