ls.html', 'snippet': 'Just as President Obama attacked Mitt Romney for paying a lower effective tax rate than most Americans, Mrs. Clinton said Mr. Trump’s plan would benefit people in his own bracket.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Clinton leaned into her plans to raise taxes on the wealthiest Americans on Wednesday, denouncing Donald J. Trump’s tax proposals as a boondoggle for billionaires.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Hillary Clinton Twists the Knife in Donald Trump’s Tax Proposals', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Getting Down to Details, Clinton Twists the Knife  in Trump’s Tax Proposals', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T22:56:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Chozick', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chozick', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1cb94be5-64f1-541f-9b3c-a7bb340536d2', 'word_count': 930, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1cb94be5-64f1-541f-9b3c-a7bb340536d2'}, {'abstract': 'The director of state-run Egyptian radio and television barred the women from appearing on the air for a month, and ordered them to go on a diet.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/world/middleeast/egypt-suspends-8-female-tv-anchors-saying-they-are-overweight.html', 'snippet': 'The director of state-run Egyptian radio and television barred the women from appearing on the air for a month, and ordered them to go on a diet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CAIRO — Most Egyptian journalists have had to watch their tongues and tone down their reporting over the past three years to keep their jobs under a military-dominated government. Now, the state is ordering some women working as television anchors to practice a similar restraint with their weight.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Egypt Suspends 8 Female TV Anchors, Saying They Are Overweight', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Egyptian TV Suspends Eight Women Over Weight', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Youssef, Nour', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weight', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hegazy, Safaa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Obesity', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-17T23:11:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nour Youssef', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nour', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Youssef', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/73b75425-28b5-5772-80c8-1572b4af672d', 'word_count': 430, 'uri': 'nyt://article/73b75425-28b5-5772-80c8-1572b4af672d'}, {'