News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2ce4491-ae05-56ea-bc23-d0153eead047', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2ce4491-ae05-56ea-bc23-d0153eead047'}, {'abstract': 'The government now seems to have Boko Haram on the run — but children must be rescued, and a host of other big problems remain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/opinion/nigerias-tragedy.html', 'snippet': 'The government now seems to have Boko Haram on the run — but children must be rescued, and a host of other big problems remain.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The release of a video on Sunday by Boko Haram, claiming to show as many as 50 of the 276 girls the terrorist group kidnapped in April 2014 from their school in Chibok, Nigeria, has given new hope that some of the missing girls can be rescued. The kidnapping sparked an international outcry, and a #BringBackOurGirls Twitter campaign.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nigeria’s Tragedy', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nigeria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boko Haram', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kidnapping and Hostages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-18T13:14:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c5537f6-a106-53a4-a59a-d60e5e4c21f1', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c5537f6-a106-53a4-a59a-d60e5e4c21f1'}, {'abstract': 'The rapper and godfather of the current boom in fashionable concert merch goes global with a constellation of temporary stores.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/fashion/before-the-tour-the-store-in-21-cities-around-the-world-kanye-west-sets-up-shop.html', 'snippet': 'The rapper and godfather of the current boom in fashionable concert merch goes global with a constellation of temporary stores.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kanye West’s “Saint Pablo” tour, for his platinum “Life of Pablo” album, begins its course through North America on Thursday. But even before it begins, his Pablo merchandise — tied to and inspired by the album — will have had its own worldwide debut.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Before the Tour, the Store: In 21 Cities Around the World, Kanye West Sets Up Shop', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kanye’s Merchandise Is on Tour Before He Is', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop-Up Stores and Restaurants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'West, Kanye', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Life of Pablo (Album)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-18T13:47:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a779723-94b9-54ba-86b8-eed0eca39807', 'word_count': 592, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a779723-94b9-54ba-86b8-eed0eca39807'}, {'abstract': 'The Smithsonian Channel’s day of nautical programming includes a look at the Queen Mary’s war years and the story of the U.S.S. Tang.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/arts/television/a-luxury-liner-at-war-a-submarine-in-peril.html', 'snippet': 'The Smithsonian Channel’s day of nautical programming includes a look at the Queen Mary’s war years and the story of the U.S.S. Tang.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Queen Mary, put into service 80 years ago, was built as a passenger liner, but World War II altered its mission, a transformation explored in “Mighty Ship at War: The Queen Mary,” which airs Sunday, Aug. 21, as part of a daylong nautical theme on the Smithsonian Channel. As the situation in Europe darkened, the ship was increasingly used to ferry emigrants out of troubled areas, and once Britain declared war, it was turned into a troop transport. The program recounts a catastrophic incident in 1942 when the liner collided with one of its own escort ships, the Curacao, splitting it in half and killing more than 300. Sunday’s lineup also includes the final installment of “Hell Below,” a six-part series on submarine warfare in World War II. Part 6, “Fatal Voyage,” is about the U.S.S. Tang, which compiled a formidable record against Japanese ships until a fateful engagement in October 1944, when it was sunk by one of its own malfunctioning torpedoes.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GUIDE7/21GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GUIDE7/21GUIDE7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GUIDE7/21GUIDE7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge'