1e0', 'word_count': 207, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5f04559-1faa-5aa3-a550-d93fa292a1e0'}, {'abstract': 'The newest wave of white rappers, acts like G-Eazy, Mike Stud and Lil Dicky, has avoided the established hip-hop industry.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/arts/music/white-rappers-geazy-mike-stud.html', 'snippet': 'The newest wave of white rappers, acts like G-Eazy, Mike Stud and Lil Dicky, has avoided the established hip-hop industry.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last month, the white rapper G-Eazy — a handsome ectomorph sporting a motorcycle jacket and 1950s-slick hair — headlined a show at the Barclays Center in Brooklyn, part of a weekslong tour. Over the last couple of years, this Oakland, Calif., musician has evolved from regional curio to legitimate pop contender: He appears on the lead single from the forthcoming Britney Spears album, and in March, his song “Me, Myself & I” with the guest singer Bebe Rexha — from his platinum album, “When It’s Dark Out” — went to No. 7 on the Billboard Hot 100.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GEAZY/21GEAZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GEAZY/21GEAZY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GEAZY/21GEAZY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21GEAZY/21GEAZY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'c