{}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Technology Can Help You Travel and Save', 'kicker': 'Frugal Traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Science and Technology', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-18T14:44:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Peterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a177d5f5-016c-515e-b1a7-56d12bd00f9a', 'word_count': 342, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a177d5f5-016c-515e-b1a7-56d12bd00f9a'}, {'abstract': 'In “Southside With You,” a 25-year-old Mrs. Obama, then Michelle Robinson, gets ice cream and a first kiss from the future president.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/movies/tika-sumpter-southside-with-you-michelle-obama.html', 'snippet': 'In “Southside With You,” a 25-year-old Mrs. Obama, then Michelle Robinson, gets ice cream and a first kiss from the future president.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEST HOLLYWOOD, Calif. — Tika Sumpter knew the screenplay was something special. It was, at its core, a romance, with two charming leads slowly falling for each other over the course of a single Chicago day. They speak passionately — at some points, angrily — about moral courage and racial politics and the struggles of staying true to oneself. They take sides on “Good Times” versus “The Brady Bunch,” ice cream versus pie. They quote the poet Gwendolyn Brooks (“We Real Cool”) from memory, while sizing up Ernie Barnes’s painting “Sugar Shack.” They watch “Do the Right Thing.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/arts/21TIKASUMPTER1/21TIKASUMPTER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tika Sumpter on Playing the Future First Lady, Michelle Obama', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On a First Date With a Guy Named Barack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sumpter, Tika (1980- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Michelle', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Southside With You (Movie)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-18T14:45:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Robert Ito', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Robert', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ito', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5d0414f5-ec53-5d63-a0d7-5c60cfa8c965', 'word_count': 1217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5d0414f5-ec53-5d63-a0d7-5c60cfa8c965'}, {'abstract': 'Adolph S. Ochs established the stand-alone Book Review 120 years ago. His great-grandson has no plans to stop it now.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/18/insider/1896-the-book-review-is-born.html', 'snippet': 'Adolph S. Ochs established the stand-alone Book Review 120 years ago. His great-grandson has no plans to stop it now.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider shares historical insights from The New York Times. In this piece, David W. Dunlap, a Metro reporter, looks back at The Times’s inaugural Book Review.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/18/insider/18Insider-Book/18Insider-Book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/18/insider/18Insider-Book/18Insider-Book-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/18/insider/18Insider-Book/18Insider-Book-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width'