19/business/dealbook/uber-speeds-toward-a-driverless-future-putting-jobs-in-danger.html', 'snippet': 'As Uber pushes ahead with autonomous taxis, and trucking considers going driverless, too, millions of Americans’ driving jobs are at risk.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Uber is steering its driverless vehicle technology toward a crash between robots and jobs. The private ride-hailing company, which was worth s $66 billion on Thursday, said that it had bought the autonomous big-rig start-up Otto and that it was unleashing driverless taxis in Pittsburgh. Putting computers instead of humans behind the wheel could save lives, but it would automate a task that employs millions of American workers. America’s safety net is ill-prepared for such a job-destroying juggernaut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber Speeds Toward a Driverless Future, Putting Jobs in Danger', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Uber Technologies Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Driverless and Semiautonomous Vehicles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Car Services and Livery Cabs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trucks and Trucking', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Automobile Safety Features and Defects', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kalanick, Travis', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pittsburgh (Pa)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-18T21:03:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8188566-5b58-5b54-be07-c8c5ffc67bb2', 'word_count': 374, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8188566-5b58-5b54-be07-c8c5ffc67bb2'}, {'abstract': 'A health official confirmed that the newly identified infections were contracted through suspected local transmission of the mosquito-borne virus.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/19/science/new-cluster-of-zika-cases-is-reported-in-miami-beach.html', 'snippet': 'A health official confirmed that the newly identified infections were contracted through suspected local transmission of the mosquito-borne virus.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MIAMI BEACH — A cluster of Zika cases most likely transmitted by local mosquitoes has been identified in Miami Beach, and federal and state officials are considering whether to advise pregnant women to avoid traveling to the city and possibly even all of Miami-Dade County, a health official said Thursday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/us/19zika-sub3/19zika-sub3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/19/us/19zika-sub3/19zika-sub3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/us/19zika-sub3/19zika-sub3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/us/19zika-sub3/19zika-sub3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna