hair arm.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 453, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 453}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 774, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1548, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/magazine/20mag-cheserek-1/20mag-cheserick-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Is the Country’s Most Dominant Distance Runner Not in Rio?', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cheserek, Edward', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2016)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Running', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Track and Field', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-19T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noah Gallagher Shannon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noah', 'middlename': 'Gallagher', 'lastname': 'Shannon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e6d2929-b424-525b-8d87-b437eff8ffc9', 'word_count': 2925, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e6d2929-b424-525b-8d87-b437eff8ffc9'}, {'abstract': 'How my daughter’s admiration of Olympic brawn made me finally embrace my own.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/19/magazine/seeing-what-my-muscles-can-do.html', 'snippet': 'How my daughter’s admiration of Olympic brawn made me finally embrace my own.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Day 3 of the 31st Olympiad, I sat on the couch with my 11-year-old daughter and watched the Hungarian swimmer Katinka Hosszu — a.k.a. the Iron Lady — roll out onto the pool deck like the assassin that she is. The woman is tough as nails, in her body and her mind. She knifed into the water; her back and shoulders exploded; she won gold in the 100-meter backstroke. Among her mottos is this: “The problem is not the problem. The problem is your attitude toward the problem.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/17/magazine/17mag-hosszu/17mag-hosszu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Seeing What My Muscles Can Do', 'kicker': 'Notebook', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Olympic Games (2012)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Swimming', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Muscles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hosszu, Katinka (1989- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-19T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Weil', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weil', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/144765eb-473a-58a0-b611-b19bbee9c101', 'word_count': 1096, 'uri': 'nyt://article/144765eb-473a-58a0-b611-b19bbee9c101'}, {'abstract': 'Market shifts and exits of large insurers are leaving Obamacare customers with no-frills plans that limit their choices of doctors and hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/20/upshot/think-your-obamacare-plan-will-be-like-employer-coverage-think-again.html', 'snippet': 'Market shifts and exits of large insurers are leaving Obamacare customers with no-frills plans that limit their choices of doctors and hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Obamacare was developed, one goal was to allow middle-class Americans to use the new marketplaces to buy the same kind of health insurance they had at their jobs. People could retire early, or quit a corporate job and become a freelancer, and still have the great care and financial protection that come with high-end plans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/upshot/18up-exchanges/18up-exchanges-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/19/upshot/18up-exchanges/18up-exchanges-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/upshot/18up-exchanges/18up-exchanges-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/19/upshot/18up-exchanges/18up-exchanges-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/19/upshot/18up-exchanges/18up-exchanges-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subty