ame': 'Tanis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f104bbb-0cd2-51ab-a597-73b81869c2aa', 'word_count': 519, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f104bbb-0cd2-51ab-a597-73b81869c2aa'}, {'abstract': 'With little more than two months until Election Day, three of the top five spots on the hardcover nonfiction list are occupied by anti-Clinton books.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/books/review/inside-the-list.html', 'snippet': 'With little more than two months until Election Day, three of the top five spots on the hardcover nonfiction list are occupied by anti-Clinton books.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Election Fever Dream: If Hillary Clinton did not exist, conservative writers would have to invent her — if, that is, they wanted to continue churning out best sellers. With little more than two months until Election Day, three of the top five spots on the hardcover nonfiction list are occupied by anti-Clinton books: Gary J. Byrne’s “Crisis of Character” (with Grant M. Schmidt) at No. 5; Dinesh D’Souza’s “Hillary’s America” at No.\u202f4; and “Armageddon,” by Dick Morris and Eileen McGann, at No. 3. Morris, of course, was Bill Clinton’s political adviser and chief campaign strategist during the 1990s, and he and McGann, his wife, have written other negative treatises about the Clintons with the zeal of converts. Morris resigned from Bill Clinton’s 1996 re-\xadelection campaign after a tabloid revealed Morris’s affair with a prostitute; he has since become the chief political commentator and correspondent for The National Enquirer.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 602, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 602}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/books/review/21inside-list-clinton/21inside-list-clinton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside the List', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-19T17:00:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Szalai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szalai', 'qualifier': None,