ported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/855667f2-32b6-55b0-bc26-37304af44742', 'word_count': 562, 'uri': 'nyt://article/855667f2-32b6-55b0-bc26-37304af44742'}, {'abstract': 'This win-win helps to raise earnings now and increase productivity over the long term while enriching the lives of children.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/20/opinion/affordable-child-care-the-secret-to-a-better-economy.html', 'snippet': 'This win-win helps to raise earnings now and increase productivity over the long term while enriching the lives of children.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Of the 24 million children under 6 in the United States today, some 12 million need day care, because both parents work or a single parent is the breadwinner. Yet most working families can’t afford good care — if they can even find it in the first place. In 2006, a federal study gave a “high quality” rating to only 10 percent of the nation’s child care programs, and the proportion today is almost certainly smaller, since government financing for child care has declined in the past decade.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/opinion/20sat1/20sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/20/opinion/20sat1/20sat1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/opinion/20sat1/20sat1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/20/opinion/20sat1/20sat1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1416, 'width': 1416, 