LINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Luggage and Packing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Air Transport Assn', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Southwest Airlines Company', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AIR FRANCE', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Qantas Airways', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Deutsche Lufthansa AG', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T01:58:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Christine Negroni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Negroni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffbfe9af-731f-539c-90ff-d0f4fd1ec03b', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffbfe9af-731f-539c-90ff-d0f4fd1ec03b'}, {'abstract': 'Chandra’s enduring faith in Naz’s innocence and Box’s doubts of his guilt are in contrast to the questions Naz’s mother now has of her son.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/arts/television/the-night-of-season-1-episode-7-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Chandra’s enduring faith in Naz’s innocence and Box’s doubts of his guilt are in contrast to the questions Naz’s mother now has of her son.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the classic 1955 Douglas Sirk melodrama “All That Heaven Allows,” the grown children of an affluent widow, along with her high-society friends, share the tacit expectation that she will remain a widow for the rest of her life. When she falls in love with a gardener many years her junior, these outside forces conspire to tear their relationship asunder. As a Christmas gift, the widow’s son gives her a television set, despite her earlier insistence that she had no interesting in owning one. Sirk frames her reflection in the TV like it’s a prison, confining her to a retirement of docile complacency while denying her the vibrant passion outside its borders.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21nightof-02/21nightof-02-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Night Of’ Season 1, Episode 7: A Test of Faith', 'kicker': 'The Night Of', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Night Of (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T02:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Scott Tobias', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Scott', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tobias', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/90d2d2da-f301-5165-ac46-27ac918c762d', 'word_count': 1110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90d2d2da-f301-5165-ac46-27ac918c762d'}, {'abstract': 'This series has bypassed a political sinkhole, reminding us that in a zombie apocalypse it doesn’t matter who you are or where you come from.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/21/arts/television/fear-the-walking-dead-season-2-episode-8-recap.html', 'snippet': 'This series has bypassed a political sinkhole, reminding us that in a zombie apocalypse it doesn’t matter who you are or where you come from.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When last we saw our group, their hard won respite at the Abigail compound had ended in literal flames, and families were split apart.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21fearthewalkingdead/21fearthewalkingdead-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/21/watching/21fearthewalkingdead/21fearthewalkingdead-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016