News', '_id': 'nyt://article/06494f0a-5bea-56d7-a0b5-956cec7b85d6', 'word_count': 460, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06494f0a-5bea-56d7-a0b5-956cec7b85d6'}, {'abstract': 'Syd Shelton’s photos capture the rise of the “Rock Against Racism” campaign — with glimpses of bands like the Clash, Matumbi and Sham 69 — that arose in Britain in the 1970s.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/22/the-radical-british-musicians-who-fought-racism-with-rock/', 'snippet': 'Syd Shelton’s photos capture the rise of the “Rock Against Racism” campaign — with glimpses of bands like the Clash, Matumbi and Sham 69 — that arose in Britain in the 1970s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mid-1970s, alarmed by the rapid rise of a neo-fascist political party that was embracing white supremacism, a radical coalition of socially engaged artists and leftist activists emerged in Britain. Infused by the international counterculture of the 1960s and with close ties\xa0to the Socialist Workers Party, this group sought to fight fascism through music.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Radical British Musicians Who Fought Racism With Rock', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clapton, Eric', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'England', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T08:00:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jean-Philippe deDieu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jean-philippe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'de Dieu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/45678f07-69bb-55c6-9a52-adc70ac69b80', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/45678f07-69bb-55c6-9a52-adc70ac69b80'}, {'abstract': 'How proud are you of the country you come from? Why?', 'web_url': 'https://learning.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/22/picture-prompt-national-pride/', 'snippet': 'How proud are you of the country you come from? Why?', 'lead_paragraph': 'These photos show fans at the Rio Olympics dressed up to represent the countries they come from. You can see them in a larger size here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Picture Prompt | National Pride', 'kicker': 'The Learning Network', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T08:07:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Education', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6c648470-448c-5db9-b62d-ea59221a7216', 'word_count': 53, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6c648470-448c-5db9-b62d-ea59221a7216'}, {'abstract': 'Ahmad al-Faqi al-Mahdi, a member of a Qaeda-linked group, was a defendant in the International Criminal Court’s first prosecution of destruction of cultural heritage as a war crime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/world/europe/ahmed-al-mahdi-hague-trial.html', 'snippet': 'Ahmad al-Faqi al-Mahdi, a member of a Qaeda-linked group, was a defendant in the International Criminal Court’s first prosecution of destruction of cultural heritage as a war crime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — An Islamic extremist pleaded guilty on Monday at the International Criminal Court to dest