 in Jamaica in August 1916.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/22/1916-hurricane-hits-jamaica/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Hurricane leaves trail of destruction in Jamaica in August 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — A despatch from Kingston, Jamaica, to the ‘‘Morning Post’’ states that the havoc wrought by the hurricane, which swept over the island on Tuesday, August 15, greatly exceeded the first estimates. General Sir W. H. Manning, Governor of Jamaica, in a telegram to Mr. Bonar Law, Secretary of State for the Colonies, says that the whole of the banana plants have been destroyed. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1916: Hurricane Hits Jamaica', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bananas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Caribbean Area', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T14:00:36+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04dc1ebf-24e1-5ed2-9a3d-154ab8536b4e', 'word_count': 101, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04dc1ebf-24e1-5ed2-9a3d-154ab8536b4e'}, {'abstract': 'Under President Rodrigo Duterte, 712 suspects have died in police operations and 1,067 have been killed by vigilantes, the nation’s police chief says.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/world/asia/philippines-rodrigo-duterte.html', 'snippet': 'Under President Rodrigo Duterte, 712 suspects have died in police operations and 1,067 have been killed by vigilantes, the nation’s police chief says.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANILA — Killings by the police and vigilantes in the Philippines’ war on drugs have soared to nearly 1,800 in the seven weeks since President Rodrigo Duterte was sworn into office, the nation’s top police official told a Senate hearing on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Nearly 1,800 Killed in Duterte’s Drug War, Philippine Police Official Tells Senators', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '1,800 Killed in 7 Weeks in Philippine Drug War', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Duterte, Rodrigo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Villamor, Felipe', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vigilantes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Murders, Attempted Murders and Homicides', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T14:19:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Felipe Villamor and Richard C. Paddock', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Felipe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Villamor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Paddock', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://artic