astname': 'Smale', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/23696e08-0196-5a7c-a4b6-9852215159d7', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/23696e08-0196-5a7c-a4b6-9852215159d7'}, {'abstract': 'The electro-pop musician Santigold’s collaboration with the artist and the director Ari Marcopoulos came after all three sat together at a Gucci show.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/22/t-magazine/entertainment/santigold-banshee-music-video-kara-walker-ari-marcopoulos.html', 'snippet': 'The electro-pop musician Santigold’s collaboration with the artist and the director Ari Marcopoulos came after all three sat together at a Gucci show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much can happen in the front row of a Gucci show. At the men’s show this past June, Jared Leto (sitting next to Olly Alexander of Years & Years) was clearly delighted by a green coat, a reaction made instantly meme-worthy by an Instagram by the artist and Gucci collaborator Trevor “Trouble” Andrew. And at the women’s fall/winter show in February, collaboration fomented: Andrew and his wife, the electro-pop musician Santigold, sat next to their old friend, the photographer Ari Marcopoulos, as well as the artist Kara Walker. “It was the perfect double date,” Santigold remembers. “We hung out all night, and at the end of the evening, they said, ‘Let’s do a video together! We have an idea!’ and Kara snapped a silhouette photo of me in the dark as I stepped into my cab.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/22/t-magazine/22tmag-santi01/22tmag-santi01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/22/t-magazine/22tmag-santi01/22tmag-santi01-thu