', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/656b9ae9-455b-544c-91f4-2f84e56a5896', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/656b9ae9-455b-544c-91f4-2f84e56a5896'}, {'abstract': 'Nikki Chasin embroiders, prints and hand-beads garments that appeal to a broad audience.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/22/t-magazine/fashion/nikki-chasin-womens-clothing-profile.html', 'snippet': 'Nikki Chasin embroiders, prints and hand-beads garments that appeal to a broad audience.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nikki Chasin can’t put her finger on the first time that she identified “fashion designer” as a profession, but she spent her girlhood in Coral Gables, Fla., practicing the basics. She remembers playing a Barbie computer game (“you could choose from her, Skipper or four other characters, pick their outfits and put them in a setting like the mall or at a sleepover — then I’d print them out and they were super-pixelated”). She and a friend started a “fashion company” called AKNC (the pair’s initials and also a nod to DKNY) that consisted of sketches of column dresses and feather boas. “We’d list the stores that sold AKNC and one day, my younger sister was drawing with us, and for one of the stores where you could buy her outfit, she put Dairy Queen,” Chasin says, laughing. She ultimately outlined her future career path in a book she made for school in fourth grade. “For the ‘about the author’ page, the last line read: ‘Nikki wants to go to FIT and then move to Los Angeles and become a fashion designer.’”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/08/t-magazine/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ/08tmag-chasin-slide-9LUZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brand to Know: A Line Worn by Grandmothers and Miley Cyrus Alike', 'kicker': 'On the Verge', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cyrus, Miley', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lower East Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-22T20:42:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_