', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Sporting-web/23Sporting-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Boxing Got Me to Face My Fears', 'kicker': 'Sporting', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boxing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fear (Emotion)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Deming', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deming', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8b0f9a9-de66-5ba7-82b6-6873ee0c7f53', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8b0f9a9-de66-5ba7-82b6-6873ee0c7f53'}, {'abstract': 'The money was a real debt and had to be paid at some point, but the United States exploited the timing so Iran didn’t delay freeing its hostages.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/opinion/the-fake-400-million-iran-ransom-story.html', 'snippet': 'The money was a real debt and had to be paid at some point, but the United States exploited the timing so Iran didn’t delay freeing its hostages.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first thing to know about the latest controversy over the Iran nuclear deal is that the Obama administration did not pay $400 million in “ransom” to secure the release of three American detainees. Yet that’s the story critics are peddling in another attempt to discredit an agreement that has done something remarkable — halted a program that had put Iran within striking distance of producing a nuclear weapon.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 594, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 594}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1014, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue1/23tue1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1914, 'width': 1932, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Fake $400 Million Iran ‘Ransom’ Story', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Fake $400 Million ‘Ransom’ Story', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nuclear Weapons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kirby, John F', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'State Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Political Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d2204b6-2bba-5f42-84e0-de81fd28abd8', 'word_count': 575, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d2204b6-2bba-5f42-84e0-de81fd28abd8'}, {'abstract': 'The call to service is drowned out by the system’s noise, and a vocation becomes a career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/opinion/why-americas-leadership-fails.html', 'snippet': 'The call to service is drowned out by the system’s noise, and a vocation becomes a career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'We’ve clearly had a failure of leadership in this country. The political system is not working as it should. Big problems are not being addressed.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 397, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 397}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 678, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1356, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Brooks-web/23Brooks-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why America’s Leadership Fails', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why  America’s Leaders Fail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2e776569-a741-57f6-b807-1772547b4b7b', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2e776569-a741-57f6-b807-1772547b4b7b'}, {'abstract': 'For one thing, it should stop using profile pictures before booking.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/opinion/how-airbnb-can-fight-racial-discrimination.html', 'snippet': 'For one thing, it should stop using profile pictures before booking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — While planning a trip to Buenos Aires two years ago, I decided to give Airbnb a try. The idea of renting a private apartment through the online service instead of paying for a generic hotel room was intriguing. Though August marks the off-season for tourism in Buenos Aires, I was rejected by the first three hosts I contacted. One host listed the days in question as available but nonetheless claimed my request overlapped with another reservation; another declined without explanation; and a third got back to me after a long delay, claiming to have missed my request.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 1020, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1020}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 603, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1966, 'width': 1156, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23clarke/23clarke-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Does Airbnb Enable Racism?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Airbnb Can Fight Racial Discrimination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clarke, Kristen', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Airbnb', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hotels and Travel Lodgings', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reservations (Airlines, Hotels, Etc.)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Holder, Eric H Jr', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristen Clarke', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clarke', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/44056bd3-674b-56de-8f7c-d3a18ecfd334', 'word_count': 809, 'uri': 'nyt://article/44056bd3-674b-56de-8f7c-d3a18ecfd334'}, {'abstract': 'America needs to improve its standing against China. But trade agreements won’t do the job.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/opinion/why-the-tpp-deal-wont-improve-our-security.html', 'snippet': 'America needs to improve its standing against China. But trade agreements won’t do the job.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Washington — With both presidential candidates running on their opposition to President Obama’s proposed Trans-Pacific Partnership free trade agreement, the White House is gearing up for one last, desperate push to get the deal through Congress. The pitch, which will begin in a few weeks, will rely on what President Obama thinks is his ace in the hole: the argument that, regardless of its economic merits, the deal, as a counter to China’s rising influence, is essential to America’s national security.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23Prestowitz-web/23Prestowitz-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why the TPP Deal Won’t Improve Our Security', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The TPP Deal Won’t Stop China', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prestowitz, Clyde', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Foreign Investments', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trans-Pacific Partnership', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T07:21:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clyde Prestowitz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clyde', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prestowitz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ba11fcab-ebdb-5607-ae22-69f550be02b2', 'word_count': 883, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ba11fcab-ebdb-5607-ae22-69f550be02b2'}, {'abstract': 'Building a new food hub in the Bronx would mean a lot more local produce for people with smaller budgets.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/opinion/a-more-egalitarian-approach-to-locavore-eating.html', 'snippet': 'Building a new food hub in the Bronx would mean a lot more local produce for people with smaller budgets.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Farmers’ markets across New York State are bulging with the season’s fleshiest tomatoes, stacks of yellow corn, and cauliflower from basic white to a startling shade of purple. Such a wealth of local produce has long been available to those with money ($6 for a dozen eggs, for example), especially at outdoor markets like the one at Union Square in New York City. Now, however, Gov. Andrew Cuomo, city officials and the nonprofit group GrowNYC have announced plans to bring a lot more local produce to people with smaller budgets.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 402, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 402}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 686, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/23/opinion/23tue3web/23tue3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1371, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'m