ter-today/', 'snippet': 'Scientists studying past and current climate conditions mull the challenges in making future warming matter today.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the past couple of months I’ve been part of a new podcast, Warm Regards, exploring climate science and its relevance to society. I’ve had a great time learning from, and sometimes debating with, two smart people with very different areas of expertise and vantage points: the\xa0blogging meteorologist Eric Holthaus\xa0and Jacquelyn Gill, who studies past climates in the context of ecological change.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 625, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 625}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 831, 'width': 798, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/07/15/blogs/dotwarmregards/dotwarmregards-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/20