raph': 'The use of unlawful detention and disappearance has become the tactic of choice in Bangladesh for dealing with anyone deemed a threat, including political enemies of the government of Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina. These practices are a violation of due process and are a mockery of Bangladesh’s laws.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Disappearances and Unlawful Detentions in Bangladesh', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Disappearances in Bangladesh', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T17:06:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/6db3e108-962c-5a99-b25f-655c1443bf00', 'word_count': 355, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6db3e108-962c-5a99-b25f-655c1443bf00'}, {'abstract': 'Julia Landauer, a Stanford graduate and former “Survivor” participant, is being promoted as an up-and-coming star in the Nascar racing system.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/sports/autoracing/julia-landauer-racecar-driver-zips-through-stereotypes.html', 'snippet': 'Julia Landauer, a Stanford graduate and former “Survivor” participant, is being promoted as an up-and-coming star in the Nascar racing system.', 'lead_paragraph': 'So much has changed in Julia Landauer’s life since she raced a five-horsepower go-kart up and down her driveway 16 years ago. She is now 24, with a bachelor’s degree from Stanford, a nascent public-speaking career and an appearance on a television reality show.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/14/sports/14DRIVER