e as many as 1.2 million displaced Iraqis when the battle begins to retake Mosul from Islamic State militants, who overran the northern city more than two years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1.2 Million Iraqis Could Be Uprooted in Mosul Battle, U.N. Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mosul (Iraq)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iraq', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T18:05:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Gladstone', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gladstone', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0065cf16-d961-507a-a906-20be879033f6', 'word_count': 503, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0065cf16-d961-507a-a906-20be879033f6'}, {'abstract': 'Keith Meister, a hedge fund investor who once sat on the company’s board, is nominating his own slate as placeholders for candidates to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/business/dealbook/investor-adds-a-new-twist-to-williamss-bizarre-tale.html', 'snippet': 'Keith Meister, a hedge fund investor who once sat on the company’s board, is nominating his own slate as placeholders for candidates to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Williams Companies, the American pipeline operator, is getting the proxy fight it deserves.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Investor Adds a New Twist to Williams’s Bizarre Tale', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Corvex Management LP', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meister, Keith A', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Williams Companies Inc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T18:16:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kevin Allison', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kevin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Allison', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6141ea6-aba5-5668-9187-d8407e122cd1', 'word_count': 375, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6141ea6-aba5-5668-9187-d8407e122cd1'}, {'abstract': 'A restaurant for Russian and Jewish specialties, a temple to Japanese udon noodles, and more food news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/dining/lox-restaurant-museum-of-jewish-heritage.html', 'snippet': 'A restaurant for Russian and Jewish specialties, a temple to Japanese udon noodles, and more food news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOX This spacious restaurant on the second floor of the Museum of Jewish Heritage takes its name seriously, offering five varieties of house-cured salmon, some smoked. Legendary Affairs, the company that has provided kosher food for catered events at the museum, was given the restaurant concession, and now David Teyf, the chef and owner, serves an array of Jewish and Russian dishes. Many, like the Russian coffee cake thickly barnacled with walnuts, and the salmon, are also sold to take away. Some other specialties are assorted herring dishes, smoked mackerel, cheese blintzes and mini black-and-white cookies. The restaurant serves dairy only. Some of the food, including a savory, buttery, garlic-laced matzoh babka from Minsk, which bears a slight resemblance to kugel, are recipes from Mr. Teyf’s grandfather. “My family is from Minsk, some of them are Holocaust survivors, and I am happy to honor them,” he said. The restaurant also has a lovely terrace:  36 Battery Place (First Place), 646-437-4231, loxnyc.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 405, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 405}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 691, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1382, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/24/dining/24OFF-WEB/24OFF-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag