8402cbdd-8079-5b31-b8fd-9eb9a3c0c179'}, {'abstract': 'The Dutch design collective We Make Carpets creates vibrant, intricately patterned installations out of everyday objects: deflated balloons, dry pasta and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/23/t-magazine/design/dream-out-loud-stedelijk-museum.html', 'snippet': 'The Dutch design collective We Make Carpets creates vibrant, intricately patterned installations out of everyday objects: deflated balloons, dry pasta and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At “Dream Out Loud,” a contemporary design exhibition opening Aug. 26 at the Stedelijk Museum Amsterdam, the Dutch collective We Make Carpets is bringing the party supplies. The trio, all in their early 30s, are known for installations of intricate patterns assembled from everyday objects, including colored sponges, dry pasta and deflated balloons. And in the Stedelijk show, three pulsating wall pieces, measuring about 6.5 by 9 feet, share a celebratory theme. “Stirrer Carpet” gets its glow from 8,000 neon-colored plastic cocktail stirrers; “Umbrella Carpet 2” employs 6,000 fancy-drink umbrellas; and “Cocktail Carpet 2” uses 16,000 shimmering cocktail sticks for its miniature fireworks. All of the pieces entice the viewer to zoom in and out to experience multiple perspectives on the work.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'When 6,000 Cocktail Umbrellas Become Art', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'On View; Dutch Fancies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Carpets and Rugs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Umbrellas', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Stedelijk Museum Amsterdam', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_d