re than a million people had filled out the surveys and described a high level of parent satisfaction with the public schools.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Good and Bad News in Survey of New York City Schools', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In City’s Survey of Schools, Good News and Some Bad', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Education Department (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T23:30:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth A. Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/810b06b0-cd2a-54a8-a506-2a45ef241cb7', 'word_count': 513, 'uri': 'nyt://article/810b06b0-cd2a-54a8-a506-2a45ef241cb7'}, {'abstract': 'State wildlife officials suspended recreation along almost 200 miles of the Yellowstone River last week to prevent a parasite from spreading.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/us/tiny-parasite-invader-deadly-to-fish-shuts-down-yellowstone-river-in-montana.html', 'snippet': 'State wildlife officials suspended recreation along almost 200 miles of the Yellowstone River last week to prevent a parasite from spreading.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LIVINGSTON, Mont. — The Yellowstone River, flowing in ribbons beneath the towering Absaroka mountains and through this small town, is usually flecked with drifting boats and rafts, sport fishermen and children jumping off bridges. But now the river, one of Montana’s premier fly-fishing destinations, is empty as wildlife officials and scientists race to contain the spread of a microscopic invader, a parasite that is deadly to fish.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/us/24montana-1/24montana-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tiny Invader, Deadly to Fish, Shuts Down a River in Montana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Parasite Deadly to Fish  Shuts a Montana River', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robbins, Jim', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parasites', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Invasive Species', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yellowstone River', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Montana', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fishing, Sport', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-23T23:36:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Robbins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robbins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/66fefaa2-2c79-5745-86c9-f014cca95279', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66fefaa2-2c79-5745-86c9-f014cca95279'}, {'abstract': 'Several clawback cases over buyouts that ended badly have resulted in thousands of shareholders fighting to keep the money that was paid to them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/business/dealbook/trying-to-turn-back-the-clock-on-deals-gone-sour.html', 'snippet': 'Several clawback cases over buyouts that ended badly have resulted in thousands of shareholders fighting to keep the money that was paid to them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Lyondell Chemical and Basell AF completed their merger nearly nine years ago. Yet today, former shareholders of Lyondell face the possibility that a new court ruling could force them to pay back money — all $12.5 billion of it.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/business/24DB-DEALPROF/24DB-DEALPROF