ation of the day for Wednesday, August 24, 2016.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/todayspaper/quotation-of-the-day.html', 'snippet': 'Quotation of the day for Wednesday, August 24, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The brain that should be there is not there.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Quotation of the Day', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Quotation of the Day', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-24T01:39:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Summary', 'section_name': 'Today’s Paper', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Quote', '_id': 'nyt://article/30041140-2dc1-5bc5-9f4a-d99fbf0270d3', 'word_count': 45, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30041140-2dc1-5bc5-9f4a-d99fbf0270d3'}, {'abstract': 'A playful debut by Matthew Sewell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/24/crosswords/field-of-draftkings-and-fanduel.html', 'snippet': 'A playful debut by Matthew Sewell.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WEDNESDAY PUZZLE — In 1979, Daniel Okrent, a former public editor for The New York Times and fellow crossword enthusiast, invented Rotisserie League Baseball, one of the best known of the fantasy sports leagues. He’s also been the managing editor of Life magazine and one of his books, “Great Fortune: The Epic of Rockefeller Center” was a finalist for a Pulitzer Prize. But what he is primarily known for is a game where baseball fans can draft the lineup of their fantasies and then play “baseball.” On paper.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/24/crosswords/24wordplay-baklava/24wordplay-baklava-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/24/crosswords/