one, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dc5b5a0-8e56-55b6-b7d0-5059d91a2a7d', 'word_count': 3203, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dc5b5a0-8e56-55b6-b7d0-5059d91a2a7d'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on when going along with your spouse is a gross deception, whether a child should know the real cause of his father’s death and when paying back a debt creates a greater burden than it lifts.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/magazine/my-wife-wants-to-adopt-when-do-i-tell-her-i-wont.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on when going along with your spouse is a gross deception, whether a child should know the real cause of his father’s death and when paying back a debt creates a greater burden than it lifts.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My wife and are I childless. We can’t have children of our own, and in any case, I have never wanted children. Now we are in our 40s, and my wife is starting the process of adoption. She is very well aware that I do not want to adopt a child, but to keep the peace in our relationship, I go along, under protest. I drag out every task required of me (writing application essays, for instance) for as long as I can, hoping either to change my mind (not happening yet) or to change hers (not happening either). This is putting a big strain on our friendship, as I feel she is pushing something on me that I don’t want. I also understand that I take away something from her that she really longs for — to be a mother.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 851, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 851}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 723, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1259, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28ethicist/28ethicist-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'My Wife Wants to Adopt. When Do I Tell Her I Won’t?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'My Wife Wants to Adopt. When Do I Tell Her I Won’t Go Through With It?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADOPTIONS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suicides and Suicide Attempts', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Alzheimer's Disease", 'rank': 7,