oomer-abortion-play-roe.html', 'snippet': 'Lisa Loomer tackles the politics of abortion in her new play, “Roe.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'ASHLAND, Ore. — Lisa Loomer has written plays about how women’s bodies are tortured in the name of beauty and about the relationship between white mothers and their Latina nannies in Los Angeles. Taking on the politics of abortion would seem right up her alley.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 830, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 830}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 740, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1480, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28LOOMER1/28LOOMER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Playwright Finds Drama, and Humor, in Roe v. Wade', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Finding Drama, and Humor, in Roe v. Wade', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Roe (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Loomer, Lisa', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauch, Bill', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oregon Shakespeare Festival', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-24T21:35:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Taylor', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Taylor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dc4451ed-e6d5-51cd-9966-4092f7dc3312', 'word_count': 1074, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dc4451ed-e6d5-51cd-9966-4092f7dc3312'}, {'abstract': 'Luke Dittrich’s book examines the case of Henry Molaison, who, after a brain operation, was almost unable to form memories. His surgeon was Mr. Dittrich’s grandfather.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/25/books/patient-hm-recalls-the-story-of-a-surgery-that-took-a-mans-memories.html', 'snippet': 'Luke Dittrich’s book examines the case of Henry Molaison, who, after a brain operation, was almost unable to form memories. His surgeon was Mr. Dittrich’s grandfather.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For nearly six decades, Henry Molaison was known only by his initials, H.M., a brutally fitting detail for a man whose identity had more or less been erased. On Aug. 25, 1953, a surgeon drilled two holes in his forehead, pried up his frontal lobes with a flat brain spatula and suctioned out several elegantly shaped structures — they looked like hooks, almonds, seahorses — in an effort to subdue an ungovernable case of epilepsy.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 857, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 857}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 983, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/arts/25BOOKDITTRICH/25BOOKDITTRICH-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Patient H.M.’ Recalls the Story of a Surgery That Took a Man’s Memories', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man Missing 25 Grams of Brain, and the Man Who Removed It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Patient H M: A Story of Me