ries as they happen; and Top Stories gives subscribers breaking news plus special reports, investigative stories or live events in sports or politics if The Times deems them important. Soon, subscribers to mobile push notifications will get the same choice.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Why’d You Do That? How The Times Decides to Send News Alerts', 'kicker': 'The Public Editor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T12:21:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Public Editor', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Spayd', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Spayd', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/bfd7feb9-bc53-5afa-9833-51400fe54acb', 'word_count': 1932, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bfd7feb9-bc53-5afa-9833-51400fe54acb'}, {'abstract': 'The company is not lowering the price it raised about 500 percent since 2007, but will offer help to needier cases.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/business/epipen-mylan-price.html', 'snippet': 'The company is not lowering the price it raised about 500 percent since 2007, but will offer help to needier cases.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Responding to a growing furor from consumers and politicians, the pharmaceutical company Mylan said on Thursday that it would lower the out-of-pocket costs to some patients who need EpiPens, which are used to treat life-threatening allergy attacks.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Mylan to Offer Some Patients Aid on Cost of EpiPens', 'kicker': None