ciation of Officials and Lawyers for Animal Rights', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utracan (Argentina)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T13:30:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Gilbert', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gilbert', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/755d7ef3-10ae-5fae-a2b5-4a32065adee0', 'word_count': 1320, 'uri': 'nyt://article/755d7ef3-10ae-5fae-a2b5-4a32065adee0'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. McCombs’s new album, “Mangy Love,” by turns lofty, cryptic and mystical, reaffirms him as one of the great songwriters of his time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/arts/music/cass-mccombs-mangy-love-interview.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. McCombs’s new album, “Mangy Love,” by turns lofty, cryptic and mystical, reaffirms him as one of the great songwriters of his time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cass McCombs’s words are a black hole. “It is not wealth to have more than others,” this 38-year-old singer-songwriter intones on “It,” a serene and unsettling ballad from his new album, “Mangy Love.” And then, a bit later: “It is not health to take vitamins and exercise.” His lyrics, whether lofty or cranky, often imply that very little is what it seems and that we are all probably doing wrong, or paying into a rotten system. A song is a gift, but what kind of gift is this? What kind of dude is this?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28MCCOMBS/28MCCOMBS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'im