ubject', 'value': 'Fires and Firefighters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'FRANCE', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War I (1914-18)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T14:29:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/13681f63-3a75-5cc6-b9ed-5f0a75f6ddf0', 'word_count': 100, 'uri': 'nyt://article/13681f63-3a75-5cc6-b9ed-5f0a75f6ddf0'}, {'abstract': 'The failed coup in Turkey and the purge that followed appear to have enhanced President Recep Tayyip Erdogan’s control of the military.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/world/europe/turkey-tanks-syria.html', 'snippet': 'The failed coup in Turkey and the purge that followed appear to have enhanced President Recep Tayyip Erdogan’s control of the military.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KARKAMIS, Turkey — In recent years, President Recep Tayyip Erdogan ordered plans drawn up for a Turkish military incursion into Syria. At every turn, though, military commanders, already fighting a war inside Turkey against Kurdish militants, pushed back.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/world/26Turkey-web/26Turkey-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/world/26Turkey-web/26Turkey-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/world/