ticle/f16f17aa-0a91-5fee-8b13-43b199c820c6', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f16f17aa-0a91-5fee-8b13-43b199c820c6'}, {'abstract': 'Dani Menkin’s film follows a 60-year-old Israeli to New York and Canada, where he searches for the long-ago love of his life.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/movies/is-that-you-review.html', 'snippet': 'Dani Menkin’s film follows a 60-year-old Israeli to New York and Canada, where he searches for the long-ago love of his life.', 'lead_paragraph': '“There is not one day in my life that I didn’t think, ‘What if?’” Ronnie (Alon Aboutboul) says in “Is That You?,” a bittersweet and lovely little movie. Most everyone else he meets has a story of regret, or a soft feeling of sorrow. Yet among this film’s surprises is that each scene still exudes affection.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 161, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 161}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 275, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 1907, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/isthatyou/isthatyou-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Pondering All of Life’s ‘What Ifs’ in ‘Is That You?’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Is That You? (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Menkin, Dani', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T20:24:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Jaworowski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Jaworowski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/453ac39e-359e-526c-a7e0-388b167499d7', 'word_count': 284, 'uri': 'nyt://article/453ac39e-359e-526c-a7e0-388b167499d7'}, {'abstract': 'As the U.S. Open begins, the tennis player, who last reached the finals in 2014, tries to balance rest and fun with preparing for her next match.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/nyregion/how-caroline-wozniacki-danish-tennis-player-spends-her-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'As the U.S. Open begins, the tennis player, who last reached the finals in 2014, tries to balance rest and fun with preparing for her next match.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Danish tennis player Caroline Wozniacki has a soft spot for the United States Open, which begins on Monday in Flushing Meadows, Queens. “The atmosphere is always spectacular,” said Ms.Wozniacki, 26, who last reached the women’s singles final in 2014 (she lost to her good friend Serena Williams). “The fact that it’s in New York makes it even more special.” Ms. Wozniacki travels frequently, but she considers herself a New Yorker. During the Open, she appreciates the nightly retreat to her apartment overlooking Union Square, which she shares with her Pomeranian, Bruno. The tournament is also nicely coordinated with another of Ms. Wozniacki’s favorite events: New York Fashion Week. Perhaps she’ll go with Ms. Williams, or someone else from her group of close-knit city friends.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 469, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 469}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 801, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1601, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/nyregion/28ROUTINE1/28ROUTINE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '