ph': 'The erstwhile journalist Cyrus Shahrad, who records under the name Hiatus, sees his electronic music career as having begun long before the drum-’n’-bass nights he D.J.-ed in his smoke-filled basement room as a student at Cambridge University. Rather, he says, it germinated in his early childhood, “sitting in the back of the car on pre-dawn drives to visit my English grandparents in Dorset, listening to the warped cassettes of mournful Iranian music my dad would play to keep himself awake.” At the time, Iran seemed to him “an idea as much as a place,” he says: Shahrad was born in the capital just before the 1979 revolution, and his family promptly fled to the U.K. But in 2005, he returned for a stint covering the presidential election for the Sunday Times, discovered his father’s old record collection and realized that he’d been missing “half of home.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/t-magazine/25tmag-hiatus01/25tmag-hiatus01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/25/t-magazine/25tmag-hiatus01/25tmag-hiatus01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/t-magazine/25tmag-hiatus01/25tmag-hiatus01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/t-magazine/25tmag-hiatus01/25tmag-hiatus01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/25/t-magazine/25tmag-hiatus01/25tmag-hiatus01-thumbStan