rty for Tom attended by, among others, their friends Clyde (Michael Chernus) and Sharon (Condola Rashad), he meets Alice (Rachel Weisz), who recently met Clyde at his office cafeteria.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26COMPLETEsub/26COMPLETEsub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: Rachel Weisz Toys With Identity in ‘Complete Unknown’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Complete Unknown (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marston, Joshua', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shannon, Michael', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Weisz, Rachel', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T22:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9f4ed8d-4f0f-5f11-be96-fe0e1b707e88', 'word_count': 273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9f4ed8d-4f0f-5f11-be96-fe0e1b707e88'}, {'abstract': 'With solid suspense, murky lighting and “gotcha!” scares, Fede Alvarez’s film will probably please fans intrigued by those elements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/movies/dont-breathe-review.html', 'snippet': 'With solid suspense, murky lighting and “gotcha!” scares, Fede Alvarez’s film will probably please fans intrigued by those elements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People who go to see movies like “Don’t Breathe” — some of them, anyway — tend to laugh when people are killed onscreen. And when people believed to be dead open their eyes. Even I laughed when the watchdog, which the three attractive young thieves had drugged into slumber, appeared in the hallway, growling. Ha! Guess he woke up, dudes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1125, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DONTBREATHE/26DONTBREATHE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Don’t Breathe’: Whose Bright Idea Was It to Rob a Blind Man?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Fede', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Don't Breathe (Movie)", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-25T22:26:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anita Gates', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anita', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gates', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5e43f190-367f-548b-af58-79bdce9f314a', 'word_count': 279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5e43f190-367f-548b-af58-79bdce9f314a'}, {'abstract': '“Remainders,” a body of work on display at Pioneer Works, is timeless, otherworldly and a little bit menacing. It has not been seen in public since 1995.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/arts/design/jimmy-desana-provocative-photographs-resurface-after-more-than-2-decades.html', 'snippet': '“Remainders,” a body of work on display at Pioneer Works, is timeless, otherworldly and a little bit menacing. It has not been seen in public since 1995.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Photography was the medium of choice for most art critics in the 1980s. Unlike painting, which thrived in a robust art market and came to symbolize the excesses of that era, photography could be used to critique mass media images, male-dominated art history — even photography itself. Despite the rise to prominence of so-called good postmodern artists like Nan Goldin and Cindy Sherman, however, there are still plenty of photographers being rediscovered today. One of them is Jimmy DeSana, who died in 1990 at the age of 40 from AIDS-related causes.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DESANA2/26DESANA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 698, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DESANA2/26DESANA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 698}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DESANA2/26DESANA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 881, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit':