rson': [{'firstname': 'Deb', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Amlen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b9a0d60a-1754-54ab-bc58-5bba84e40057', 'word_count': 729, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b9a0d60a-1754-54ab-bc58-5bba84e40057'}, {'abstract': 'The overall portrait in this 1953 play by N.C. Hunter is of an economically comfortable English family in coastal Dorset in the anxious postwar years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/theater/mint-theater-a-day-by-the-sea.html', 'snippet': 'The overall portrait in this 1953 play by N.C. Hunter is of an economically comfortable English family in coastal Dorset in the anxious postwar years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'There’s so much to like about the Mint Theater Company’s revisiting of “A Day by the Sea” that it’s hard to know what to single out for first-paragraph attention. Let’s go with this: Even secondary characters in this 1953 play by N. C. Hunter are given the chance to make an impression, and in this production they do.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DAYBYSEA1/26DAYBYSEA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 411, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DAYBYSEA1/26DAYBYSEA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 411}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DAYBYSEA1/26DAYBYSEA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 701, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/arts/26DAYBYSEA1/26DAYBYSEA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1403, 'width': 2048, 'subT