s draw, and Madison Keys, Karolina Pliskova and Mónica Puig stand out among the women.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Cilic, 27, won his first Masters 1000 tournament at Cincinnati on Aug. 21 and vaulted back into the top 10 with a straight-sets victory over Andy Murray, the reigning Wimbledon and Olympic champion. Cilic, who had three match points against Roger Federer in the Wimbledon quarterfinals, kept Murray off balance with a nearly unreturnable wide slice serve, followed by flat bombs up the middle. After parting ways with his longtime coach Goran Ivanisevic, Cilic hired Jonas Bjorkman to help strengthen his forehand and his return, both of which let him down in crucial moments against Federer at Wimbledon. Against Murray at Cincinnati, Cilic returned brilliantly. Cilic is seeded seventh at the United States Open, and his rising level of play suggests that he could be rounding into the kind of form that led him to the title in 2014.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/29/sports/29PLAYERS-web1/29PLAYERS-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dark Horses Abound at the United States Open', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Poised to Strike', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tennis', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Open (Tennis)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cilic, Marin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimitrov, Grigor', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Keys, Madison', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pliskova, Karolina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Puig, Monica', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'del Potro, Juan Martin', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-26T09:00:31+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Tennis', 'byline': {'original': 'By Geoff Macdonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Geoff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Macdonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ec134d1-c9c4-5eee-8d36-6a96bccdb37b', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ec134d1-c9c4-5eee-8d36-6a96bccdb37b'}, {'abstract': 'Jockeying for administration jobs usually occurs after Election Day, but both candidates’ transition teams are already working on filling potential posts, and speculation is rampant.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/27/us/politics/clinton-and-trump-campaigns-are-buzzing-about-the-race-for-the-cabinet.html', 'snippet': 'Jockeying for administration jobs usually occurs after Election Day, but both candidates’ transition teams are already working on filling potential posts, and speculation is rampant.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Hillary Clinton and Donald J. Trump have yet to face off in their first debate, but both candidates have already moved teams into a plush marble-and-glass office building a block from the White House, where they are vetting résumés, sketching out organizational charts and otherwise planning the transition to a Trump or Clinton administration.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/27/us/27transition/27transition-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/27/us/27transition/27transition-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/27/us/27transition/27transition-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/27/us/27transition/27transition-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/27/us/27transition/27transition-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, '