2016/08/28/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-safety-razors.html', 'snippet': 'How did marketers convince people that masculinity meant never being around sharp objects?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first razor I can remember owning is one I received as a present for my 18th birthday. It came in the mail from Gillette. I don’t know how the company knew, but I was happy to be in its database. The Fusion, with its novel five-blade design, had recently hit the market. I was thrilled, and I cycled back and forth through the cartridges until they were all hair-\xadclogged and uselessly dull. When I found out the price of a Fusion blade-\xadrefill box, I saw my whole life stretch in front of me.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 759, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1518, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28mag-28lor-t_CA0/28mag-28lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Safety Razors', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Safety Razors ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shaving and Shavers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Harris, Malcolm', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gillette Co', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-26T10:58:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malcolm Harris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malcolm', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Harris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ce55a013-8fce-5b81-8602-46e974c4a623', 'word_count': 882, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce55a013-8fce-5b81-8602-46e974c4a623'}, {'abstract': 'Learn to climb safely. Always remain harnessed.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/magazine/how-to-sleep-in-a-tree.html', 'snippet': 'Learn to climb safely. Always remain harnessed.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Start low to the ground,” says Andrew Joslin, who first slept in a tree 10 years ago, when he was a tech worker who regularly slept in a hammock in his Boston backyard. Now 60, Joslin lives in rural Massachusetts, where he works as an arborist. If you intend to sleep 15 feet off the ground or higher, first learn to climb safely. You’ll need 150 feet of arborist rope, a harness, a helmet, carabiners and a special tree-\xadsleeping hammock, or a lightweight platform called a portaledge. Before you ascend, check the weather. You don’t want to be dozens of feet off the ground in the dark during high winds or lightning.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 593, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 593}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1011, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/magazine/28tip/28tip-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1344, 'width': 1361, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Sleep in a Tree', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Sleep in a Tree', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wollan, Malia', 'rank': 1, 'majo