rted', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8cf5187f-6760-5bbd-94f8-32867388e57e', 'word_count': 501, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8cf5187f-6760-5bbd-94f8-32867388e57e'}, {'abstract': 'This recently reissued fixture, designed in 1972 by the Danish architect Louis Weisdorf, doesn’t merely illuminate a room.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/26/t-magazine/design/louis-weisdorf-pendant-lamp.html', 'snippet': 'This recently reissued fixture, designed in 1972 by the Danish architect Louis Weisdorf, doesn’t merely illuminate a room.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Designed in 1972 by the Danish architect Louis Weisdorf, this shape-shifting brass pendant lamp doesn’t merely illuminate a room; the light it throws can also mirror your mood. Futuristic, with a Fritz Langian appeal, it is made up of two center cylinders encompassed by quarter-spherical shells that can pivot to change the fixture’s shape. Recently reissued by the Danish manufacturer Gubi, it is available in brass, chrome, matte white, black or French blue, and can be configured in multiple ways, turning any room into a true reflection of the happily divided self.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '92', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/11/t-magazine/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0/11tmag-09qual_thing-t_CA0-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'cro