mes.com/2016/08/28/arts/music/julian-barnes-the-noise-of-time-shostakovich.html', 'snippet': 'Julian Barnes’s novel “The Noise of Time” enters the debate about whether the composer was a blameless martyr or a man who made pragmatic compromises.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Novelists have every right to use historical data to lend their works verisimilitude, and they are free to go beyond the facts, wherever their fancy leads them. Historians, though, are bound by circumstances, condemned to whatever partial, obstructed view their sources grant them. Their only recourse is to keep on looking and pray. Meanwhile, novelists can soar and gain an untrammeled vista.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/arts/28SHOSTAKOVICH1/28SHOSTAKOVICH1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo'