wers better.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BORROWERS wrestling with college debt often complain that it is frustrating to deal with the companies that manage their student loans. This summer, federal regulators have stepped up pressure on loan servicers to treat their borrowers better.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'U.S. Puts Private Student Loan Servicers on Notice: Play Nice', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'U.S. Puts Private Student Loan Servicers on Notice: Play Nice', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Carrns, Ann', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo Bank', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Consumer Financial Protection Bureau', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-26T15:43:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/e8a09094-4eb0-5b92-bc12-4108cf1f11d5', 'word_count': 750, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e8a09094-4eb0-5b92-bc12-4108cf1f11d5'}, {'abstract': 'A gifted young sprinter in a tough neighborhood unexpectedly finds the support he needs in Jason Reynolds’s “Ghost.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/books/review/jason-reynolds-ghost.html', 'snippet': 'A gifted young sprinter in a tough neighborhood unexpectedly finds the support he needs in Jason Reynolds’s “Ghost.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'GHOSTBy Jason Reynolds181 pp. Atheneum. $16.99. (Middle grade; ages 8 to 12)', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Young Sprinter Finds His Team in ‘Ghost’', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Running for His Life', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Ghost (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Jason (Author)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-26T15:44:32+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kate Messner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kate', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Messner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5f3fd3f3-1c4b-5a02-887a-a3da30d38931', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5f3fd3f3-1c4b-5a02-887a-a3da30d38931'}, {'abstract': 'A red door leads to adventure, a curious mouse sends himself to the moon, and a lonely man gets a mysterious invitation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/books/review/return-aaron-becker-uncorker-of-ocean-bottles-michelle-cuevas.html', 'snippet': 'A red door leads to adventure, a curious mouse sends himself to the moon, and a lonely man gets a mysterious invitation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For very young children, even a trip to a grocery store can be thrilling. Cheese samples, the fish department and the dewy surprise of automatic misting in the produce section: Lots of marvels are packed in those prosaic aisles. Some of the most enduring children’s books transform something ordinary — a purple crayon, a wardrobe, a red pebble — into vehicles for exhilarating journeys. Three new picture books follow the tradition. In space, at sea, in a twilight world — these books take readers on escapes so transporting it’s a pleasure to get lost.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 379, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 379}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 647, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 1591, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Lamy-02/0828-BKS-Lamy-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Three Stunning Picture Books Take Children on Unusual Journeys', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Great Escapades', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lamy, Nicole', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Return (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Becker, Aaron (1974- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Uncorker of Ocean Bottles (Book)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cuevas, Michelle (1982- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stead, Erin E', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Armstrong: The Adventurous Journey of a Mouse to the Moon (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kuhlmann, Torben', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-26T15:44:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicole Lamy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicole', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lamy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9618f0a-5e1e-57bf-9a48-8ac701ff13d7', 'word_count': 1031, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9618f0a-5e1e-57bf-9a48-8ac701ff13d7'}, {'abstract': 'Children climb typography mountains and craft their own adventures in four tributes to the power of storytelling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/books/review/child-of-books-oliver-jeffers-sam-winston-i-am-a-story-dan-yaccarino.html', 'snippet': 'Children climb typography mountains and craft their own adventures in four tributes to the power of storytelling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many creators of picture books become so immersed in the lengthy process of bringing a book into the world, they can’t help pitching the idea of making a book about books. I can relate. I have three or four such books in a shoe box under my bed. Looking back, I think I created them for the exclusive amusement of my bookish colleagues. Was I showing off? Maybe. The truth is, the very best picture books appeal to several audiences at the same time. These include parents, fellow bookmakers, librarians, award givers and, one hopes, even children. Four new books about books manage to thread that needle.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Viva-02/0828-BKS-Viva-02-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 345, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Viva-02/0828-BKS-Viva-02-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1275, 'width': 429, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Viva-02/0828-BKS-Viva-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Viva-02/0828-BKS-Viva-02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/books/review/0828-BKS-Viva-02/0828-BKS-Viva-02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Four New Picture Books Teach Children the Power of Stories', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'If These Books Could Talk', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books 