r day, speaking from an apartment building in TriBeCa where he is the superintendent, that with all the security cameras around the city these days, people might think twice about committing crimes in public. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Here’s Looking at You', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Benskin, Clay', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-27T09:00:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2970125d-97ce-5973-aa01-6c5ffa1f7678', 'word_count': 340, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2970125d-97ce-5973-aa01-6c5ffa1f7678'}, {'abstract': 'The industrial giant is investing big in an effort to adopt the nimble habits and digital wizardry of Silicon Valley. And, its C.E.O. says, there is no Plan B.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/technology/ge-the-124-year-old-software-start-up.html', 'snippet': 'The industrial giant is investing big in an effort to adopt the nimble habits and digital wizardry of Silicon Valley. And, its C.E.O. says, there is no Plan B.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It may not qualify as a lightning-bolt eureka moment, but Jeffrey R. Immelt, chief executive of General Electric, recalls the June day in 2009 that got him thinking. He was speaking with G.E. scientists about new jet engines they were building, laden with sensors to generate a trove of data from every flight — but to what end?', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype'