ers, near Block Island, R.I., was completed this month. With just five turbines, the farm won’t make much of a dent in the nation’s reliance on fossil fuels, but it shows the promise this renewable energy source could have. When the turbines start spinning in November, they will power the island, which currently relies on diesel generators, and will also send electricity to the rest of Rhode Island.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 590, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 590}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1007, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28sun2/28sun2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1200, 'width': 1220, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Unlimited Power of Ocean Winds', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Unlimited Power of Ocean Winds', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wind Power', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oceans and Seas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cape Wind Associates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Block Island (RI)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-27T18:30:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/0b0b7e93-d0e1-50f2-a10d-dbe754010b30', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0b0b7e93-d0e1-50f2-a10d-dbe754010b30'}, {'abstract': 'How do you square the image of the transcendent, unchanging champion with the fact of a player who is growing old?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/even-roger-federer-gets-old.html', 'snippet': 'How do you square the image of the transcendent, unchanging champion with the fact of a player who is growing old?', 'lead_paragraph': 'He heard a click. That was how Roger Federer discovered the knee injury that cost him most of his 2016 season. He was running a bath for his daughters — and since he is Roger Federer, we have to assume he was running a gorgeous bath, possibly the greatest bath of all time, perfect temperature, immaculate bubbles, faint scent of lavender, business as usual.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/opinion/sunday/28phillips/28phillips-thumb