esk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Perri Klass, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Perri', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klass', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26367996-465f-5cf1-911e-ec5b8856341b', 'word_count': 812, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26367996-465f-5cf1-911e-ec5b8856341b'}, {'abstract': 'The suspended president took the stand and fiercely argued that she was innocent of the charges of manipulating the federal budget.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/30/world/americas/brazil-dilma-rousseff-impeachment-trial.html', 'snippet': 'The suspended president took the stand and fiercely argued that she was innocent of the charges of manipulating the federal budget.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRASÍLIA — Brazil’s suspended president, Dilma Rousseff, took the stand on Monday at her impeachment trial in the Senate, delivering a last-ditch defense to prevent her final removal from office.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Dilma Rousseff of Brazil Says She Won’t Be Silenced in Impeachment Trial', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Her Impeachment Trial in Brazil, Rousseff Says She Won’t Be Silenced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romero, Simon', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rousseff, Dilma', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Temer, Michel (1940- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-29T14:23:43+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Simon Romero', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Simon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Romero', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/81139cf3-2979-58ac-a353-b923d24bf39b', 'word_count': 539, 'uri': 'nyt://article/81139cf3-2979-58ac-a353-b923d24bf39b'}, {'abstract': 'Testing with varnishtest made a huge impact when working with VCL. There is a bit of a learning curve to get started, so I wanted to share what I’ve learned in my work.', 'web_url': 'https://open.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/29/testing-varnish-using-varnishtest/', 'snippet': 'Testing with varnishtest made a huge impact when working with VCL. There is a bit of a learning curve to get started, so I wanted to share what I’ve learned in my work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I work on the Content API team at the New York Times and we have a lot of legacy code. Over the past year I spent months modernizing our platform for our continuous delivery initiative. If you have a lot of legacy code, and the people before you weren’t developing with continuous delivery practices, chances are you have your own fair share of challenges. One of the tougher challenges I faced was learning how to test the systems I inherited, and one of those platforms I inherited was our Varnish stack.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Testing Varnish Using Varnishtest', 'kicker': 'Open', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-08-29T14:28:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russell Simpkins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Simpkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/465b872c-60ff-581a-a446-f0c98c4bfe5e', 'word_count': 967, 'uri': 'nyt://article/465b872c-60ff-581a-a446-f0c98c4bfe5e'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: An American theater company arrives in Paris in August 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/29/1891-american-comedians-arrive/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: An American theater company arrives in Paris in August 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Daly Company open their Paris season tomorrow evening at the Vaudeville Theatre, with ‘‘As You Like It.’’ They will play for a week, varying the programme every night, and giving in succession ‘‘The Railroad of Love,’’ ‘‘The School for Scandal,’’ ‘‘A Night Off,’’ a piece written by Mr. Daly himself; ‘‘The Taming of the Shrew’’ and ‘‘The Lottery of Love.’’ This is the third time the Daly Company have visited Paris, but their last appearance was three years ago. It is owing to the fact that Mr. Daly’s theatre in New York is undergoing reconstruction, that he has found time to make a European trip. — The New York Herald, European Edition, August 30, 1891', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/blogs/30oldiht-1891-daly/30oldiht-1891-daly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/30/blogs/30oldiht-1891-daly/30oldiht-1891-daly-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/blogs/30oldiht-1891-daly/30oldiht-1891-daly-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/blogs/30oldiht-1891-daly/30