 'lead_paragraph': 'The Rio Olympics have come and gone, but tastes of Brazil linger. In NoLIta, a group of Brazilian entrepreneurs has opened a new spot that serves freshly made tapioca crepes. Lacy and crisp-edged, made from cassava flour and naturally gluten-free, they enclose combinations like scrambled eggs, tomatoes and mozzarella or bananas, feta and mint. There are tropical milkshakes alongside, all to devour at a few tables on the premises or to take away: Oca, 250 Mott Street (Prince Street), 212-966-0622, ocastore.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31burnerbrazil/31burnerbrazil-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 