rticle/ce456e5e-011d-52a0-8faf-3ae026dfdf9c', 'word_count': 1509, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ce456e5e-011d-52a0-8faf-3ae026dfdf9c'}, {'abstract': 'Students deserve support as they prepare to return to class after an attack on the American University of Afghanistan.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/30/opinion/a-barbarous-attack-on-afghan-students.html', 'snippet': 'Students deserve support as they prepare to return to class after an attack on the American University of Afghanistan.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It has always required a leap of faith to believe that the American University of Afghanistan, which opened its doors in 2006, would endure in the face of endless war and violence. The attack on the campus by militants last week, which killed at least 13 people, including seven students, three police officers and three security guards, demonstrates how perilous the conditions remain. But the resolve of students and faculty members, who vowed to carry on with their mission and education, offered hope.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/opinion/30tue3web/30tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/30/opinion/30tue3web/30tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/opinion/30tue3web/30tue3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/30/opinion/30tue3web/30tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 389, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge':