fsviertel, the city’s red light district, was the neighborhood that parents always warned their children about. “When I was a teenager my mother forbade me to ever come here,” said Marijana Condic, a Frankfurt-based fashion designer and one of two women behind the shoe label Lika Mimika, who until recently lived in the area. “At the time that small park over there,” she said, pointing to a rectangular lawn in Willy-Brandt-Platz, “was loaded with junkies.”', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 592}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1010, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/28/travel/28HEADSUP2/28HEADSUP2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1844, 'width': 1870, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Frankfurt’s Rough Red Light District Becomes Cool', 'kicker': 'Heads Up', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Respectability in the Red-Light District', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williams, Gisela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Frankfurt (Germany)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-30T13:45:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gisela Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gisela', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f7ee2dd2-d09c-5ed2-a357-5b0bc1c573d4', 'word_count': 749, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f7ee2dd2-d09c-5ed2-a357-5b0bc1c573d4'}, {'abstract': 'Tourism and global hipsterism have transformed the city where I once lived. But not entirely — the canals endure.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/travel/amsterdam-revisited.html', 'snippet': 'Tourism and global hipsterism have transformed the city where I once lived. But not entirely — the canals endure.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year we decided to take our summer vacation in Amsterdam. For my family, Amsterdam is not just any destination. I lived in the city for seven years and wrote a book about it. My partner, Pamela, lived there for 23 years. We met in Amsterdam. Our son was born in the city. We have friends, family, colleagues, memories and roots there. It is, logically and in our hearts, our second home. And yet, three years after returning to the United States, we realized that it had become shockingly remote in our lives. So while the trip would be a vacation, the real motive was to spend a couple of weeks reclaiming Amsterdam.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 666, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/travel/04COVER1/04COVER1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1332, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Amsterdam, Revisited', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Amsterdam, Revisited', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shorto, Russell', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'AMSTERDAM (NETHERLANDS)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-30T13:57:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Russell Shorto', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Russell', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shorto', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5768720a-fa23-584c-bf5f-b2aa16786fe9', 'word_count': 3125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5768720a-fa23-584c-bf5f-b2aa16786fe9'}, {'abstract': 'The comedian, actor, writer and director, whose movie “Don’t Think Twice” is in theaters, offers some unsolicited advice for people thinking about showbiz.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/movies/mike-birbiglias-6-tips-for-making-it-small-in-hollywood-or-anywhere.html', 'snippet': 'The comedian, actor, writer and director, whose movie “Don’t Think Twice” is in theaters, offers some unsolicited advice for people thinking about showbiz.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This summer, I went on a 30-city tour with my movie “Don’t Think Twice,” a comedy about an improv group that has to decide whether to stay in show business when one member is plucked for a “Saturday Night Live” type of show. At every Q. and A. session for the movie, people would ask the same question: “If I want to be a comedian [or actor or writer or improviser or film director], how do I get started?” The truth is they should probably pick someone more successful to ask — I make small films, small one-man shows Off Broadway and small comedy specials for Netflix — but I’m the person who showed up to talk to them. And now I’m the person offering you unsolicited advice — so if you don’t need it or want it, this is not for you. Anyway, I’ve boiled my answer down to six ideas.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/0