 '2016-08-30T14:00:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Birbiglia', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Birbiglia', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b54aedc2-3317-5213-af82-17159666ceb0', 'word_count': 1113, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b54aedc2-3317-5213-af82-17159666ceb0'}, {'abstract': 'A report by Amnesty International says that while just 8 percent of children in the state are indigenous, they make up 65 percent of those being held.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/31/world/australia/indigenous-children-detention.html', 'snippet': 'A report by Amnesty International says that while just 8 percent of children in the state are indigenous, they make up 65 percent of those being held.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SYDNEY, Australia — Indigenous children in the Australian state of Queensland are much likelier than others there to be held in juvenile detention, and Australia’s judicial system has held children as young as 10 criminally responsible for their actions, Amnesty International said in a report released on Wednesday.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/world/31australia-web3/31australia-web3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/31/world/31australia-web3/31australia-web3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/world/31australia-web3/31australia-web3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}},