how-restaurants.html', 'snippet': 'The most bulletproof of restaurants is the work of a man who sweats the details but not the criticism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Michael Chow looked at ease in his favorite banquette at the Carlyle hotel, beneath a portrait of Peter Fonda and Dennis Hopper in their “Easy Rider” prime, but something in his peripheral vision nagged at him.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/dining/31chow1/31chow1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1362, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sky-High Prices? Bad Reviews? No Matter: Mr. Chow Powers On', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mr. Chow, Powering On', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordinier, Jeff', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chow, Eva (1957- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chow, Michael', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Beverly Hills (Calif)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mr Chow Restaurants', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-30T15:35:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Gordinier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gordinier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b2f0f25b-0756-5900-afc1-7e821e16e3bd', 'word_count': 1649, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b2f0f25b-0756-5900-afc1-7e821e16e3bd'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: President Johnson says the U.S. could face a series of crises if the roots of the Vietnam war’s causes aren’t targeted.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/08/30/1966-johnson-targets-wars-causes/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: President Johnson says the U.S. could face a series of crises if the roots of the Vietnam war’s causes aren’t targeted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Johnson today said the United States and its allies could face a series of explosive crises — such as the Vietnam war — if they did not do more to ‘‘root out the very causes of war.’’ These, he said, are ‘‘the poverty of man’s body, the privation of his spirit, the imprisonment of his liberties.’’ Only when these have been done away with, he said, ‘‘will there be a final surrender of violence itself.’’ ‘‘That is our aim in Asia,’’ he added. He said cooperation among Asians ‘‘can become the means for liberating hundreds of millions of people — not the least the people of North and South Vietnam.’’ — New York Herald Tribune, European Edition, Aug. 31, 1966', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Johnson Targets War’s Causes', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'UNITED STATES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-30T15:38:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b24f19aa-d859-5dfe-ade0-4bfdf033f71d', 'word_count': 125, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b24f19aa-d859-5dfe-ade0-4bfdf033f71d'}, {'abstract': 'The State Court of Appeals ruled that a nonadoptive, nonbiological caretaker of a child could be allowed to ask for custody and visitation rights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/31/nyregion/new-york-court-parental-rights.html', 'snippet': 'The State Court of Appeals ruled that a nonadoptive, nonbiological caretaker of a child could be allowed to ask for custody and visitation rights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Expanding the definition of what it means to be a parent, especially for same-sex couples, the New York State Court of Appeals ruled on Tuesday that a caretaker who is not related to, or the adoptive guardian of, a child could still be permitted to ask for custody and visitation rights.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'New York’s Highest Court Expands Definition of Parenthood', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New York Court Expands  Definition of Parenthood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feuer, Alan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Child Custody and Support', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-30T15:39:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/034c7aa4-c730-5b77-8f35-a6d55bb718d0', 'word_count': 764, 'uri': 'nyt://article/034c7aa4-c730-5b77-8f35-a6d55bb718d0'}, {'abstract': 'Here, the beauty faves she has in her #nyfw makeup bag.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/fashion/model-lexi-boling-beauty-routine-new-york-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'Here, the beauty faves she has in her #nyfw makeup bag.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Forget your wholesome girl next door: Lexi Boling, 22, harks back to a different era when it was cool to be bad in the fashion industry. Just look at the raucous images on her Instagram account for evidence.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'm