to the Sound and the rail station, has the higher prices.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Riverside, Conn.: Coastal Beauty for a Price', 'kicker': 'Living In', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Coastal Beauty for a Price', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Prevost, Lisa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Riverside (Greenwich, Conn)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Greenwich (Conn)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-31T08:59:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Prevost', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Prevost', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/459e29e5-a140-5085-bc0e-c26d9ed08501', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/459e29e5-a140-5085-bc0e-c26d9ed08501'}, {'abstract': 'An executive toy that’s more like a battery-operated koan about humans and technology.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-the-useless-machine.html', 'snippet': 'An executive toy that’s more like a battery-operated koan about humans and technology.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the lower left-hand corner of my desk sits a wooden box, roughly the size and shape of a smallish jewelry case and featureless save for a small metal switch on its uppermost surface. From time to time over the course of my workday, I reach out to flick this switch, and a hatch opens at the top of the box, and a small fingerlike projection, driven by a whirring motor within, emerges and pushes the switch back into its original position. Having been switched on, this machine has now fulfilled its sole function of switching itself off again.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04lor/04mag-04lor-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: The Useless Machine', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Useless Machine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Robots and Robotics', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Shannon, Claude (1916-2001)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Minsky, Marvin', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Innovation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bell Laboratories', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-31T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': "By Mark O'Connell", 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': "O'Connell", 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0cdb898c-8ab7-5306-9910-4ca11498955d', 'word_count': 913, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0cdb898c-8ab7-5306-9910-4ca11498955d'}, {'abstract': 'The entertainer on menstrual-pain relief, staying single and the notion of “innocent until proven guilty.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/04/magazine/whoopi-goldberg-wants-to-make-you-feel-better.html', 'snippet': 'The entertainer on menstrual-pain relief, staying single and the notion of “innocent until proven guilty.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'You’ve been the moderator of “The View” since 2007, where you have been known to share the occasional provocative opinion, including that Bill Cosby should be considered innocent until proven guilty, which you later walked back. Do you consider the Roger Ailes case similarly? I used to think that “innocent until proven guilty” was the American way. But now social media makes that decision for you. People are at a disadvantage in a way that they weren’t before; you don’t really seem to be able to have your own opinion about something. I believe strongly that we should always encourage women to say something, so that if it’s true, you can prove it and get somebody off the street, and if it’s not, clear them and move on.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '50', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 944, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 944}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 651, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/04/magazine/04talk/04talk-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1302, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Whoopi Goldberg Wants to Make You Feel Better', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whoopi Goldberg Wants to Make You Feel Better', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Goldberg, Whoopi', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cox, Ana Marie', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The View (TV Program)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-31T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fdc756bf-bb3b-5b5c-8c00-e4209962b704', 'word_count': 681, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fdc756bf-bb3b-5b5c-8c00-e4209962b704'}, {'abstract': 'The last time that an airline in the United States had a regularly scheduled flight to the island, the passengers flew on a propeller plane.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/world/americas/cuba-us-first-flight-jetblue.html', 'snippet': 'The last time that an airline in the United States had a regularly scheduled flight to the island, the passengers flew on a propeller plane.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. — Amid live Cuban music, fresh guava pastries and a water cannon salute, the first scheduled passenger jet service in history between Cuba and the United States began on Wednesday with a 9:45 flight from here to Santa Clara, east of Havana.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Scheduled Flights to Cuba From U.S. Begin Again, Now With Jet Engines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Scheduled Flights to Cuba Resume, Now With Jets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Robles, Frances', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Cuba', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JetBlue Airways Corporation', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Embargoes and Sanctions', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-31T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frances Robles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frances', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8d880e0f-6574-50f5-8f4c-87c3ae2f0992', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8d880e0f-6574-50f5-8f4c-87c3ae2f0992'}, {'abstract': 'Halal food is big business in China. But to the Hui, a Muslim ethnic minority, a social pact may come before profit in the placement of halal noodle shops.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/world/what-in-the-world/china-halal-noodles.html', 'snippet': 'Halal food is big business in China. But to the Hui, a Muslim ethnic minority, a social pact may come before profit in the placement of halal noodle shops.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Amid the modern skyscrapers of Shanghai, the parties to a time-honored treaty are at war.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/26/world/what-in-the-world/00wit_china-noodle-treaty/00wit_china-noodle-treaty-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/26/world/