gé of Henri Cartier-Bresson, Mr. Riboud routinely traveled to restive places throughout Asia and Africa in the 1950s and ’60s as part of his decades-long career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marc Riboud, the celebrated French photojournalist who captured moments of grace even in the most fraught situations around the world, died in Paris on Tuesday. He was 93.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/01/obituaries/01riboud02/01riboud02-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Marc Riboud, Photojournalist Who Found Grace in the Turbulent, Dies at 93', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Marc Riboud, 93, Whose Photos Found Grace, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Woodward, Richard B', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Riboud, Marc', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-08-31T10:08:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard B. Woodward', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/1c3ed154-5da6-5053-b7e2-5489a870b25b', 'word_count': 1273, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1c3ed154-5da6-5053-b7e2-5489a870b25b'}, {'abstract': 'The countries are meeting in the opening match of the final round of Asian qualifications for the 2018 World Cup. They have met 30 times, and China has won only once.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/09/01/sports/soccer/political-tension-between-china-and-south-korea-intrudes-on-a-fierce-rivalry.html', 'snippet': 'The countries are meeting in the opening match of the final round of Asian qualifications for the 2018 World Cup. They have met 30 times, and China has won only once.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEOUL, South Korea — The term “Koreaphobia” was coined in China and is used with relish in Seoul. It does not refer to the recent political tension between the two neighbors but to the struggles that China’s soccer team has had when facing South Korea.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '17', 'source