lead_paragraph': 'In late 2006, Mary Boone phoned the artist Jacob Hashimoto several months ahead of his first show at her venerable gallery to ask about his progress. “She said, ‘I heard that you haven’t finished any of the work,’ and she explained that when she does a show of six or seven pieces, she hopes to choose from 15,” he remembers. “I told her that my studio is like a sourdough bread bakery — you have the mother, which is the dough that you’re growing, and you feed it flour and water, and the mother gets bigger and keeps leavening. And, eventually, you take off chunks and make your biscuits, but most of the time, you’re feeding the mother.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 650, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 650}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/08/31/t-magazine/31tmag-hashimoto1/31tmag-hashimoto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width'